 FR-30 | PASS | `getScheduleForDate`; integration \"FR-30/FR-31/FR-45\" (ordered entries for teacher and student; Saturday returns []) |\n| FR-31 | PASS | `getCurrentSlot`; same test (inside the period → slot; at the exclusive end → null) |\n| FR-32 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/config/navigation.ts has no Timetable, Timetable editor or Bell schedule entries |\n| FR-33 | PASS | src/app/api/periods/{route,[id]/route,reorder/route}.ts: GET uses `requireUser`, writes use `requireRole('ADMIN')`. Handler wiring was checked by reading the code; the service is tested in integration. |\n| FR-34 | PASS | src/app/api/school-days/route.ts (GET `requireUser`, PUT `requireRole('ADMIN')`); service tested in integration \"FR-7/FR-40\" |\n| FR-35 | PASS | `assertCanViewTimetable`; integration \"FR-35\" covers ADMIN any view, TEACHER own view and homeroom section, and 403 for another teacher, another section and a STUDENT. Note: TEACHER can also view sections they teach a course in (design decision D8), which is broader than \"homeroom only\". |\n| FR-36 | PASS | `getAvailability`; integration \"FR-36\" (key `4-<periodId>` holds the exact clash message; free cells are absent) |\n| FR-37 | PASS | slots routes are ADMIN-only; integration \"FR-37/FR-40\" (academicYearId comes from the course) and \"FR-9/FR-10\" (CONFLICT with `details.clashes[]` and 0 rows saved) |\n| FR-38 | PASS | `resolvePersonalTarget`; integration \"FR-38/FR-25\". Minor: a multi-child parent with no `studentId` gets 400 VALIDATION_ERROR rather than 403. That is reasonable, but it differs from the spec wording. |\n| FR-39 | PASS | src/lib/validators/timetable.ts holds every schema and is imported by all 10 handlers; unit \"periodSchema\" tests |\n| FR-40 | PASS | `audit()` calls in every write; integration checks the slot create, update and delete rows and `schoolDay.update` with `deletedSlotCount`. Period create, update, delete and reorder audits were checked by reading the code only. |\n| FR-41 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | pris