{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEwjAnrtTBjYDyJihiM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SH-6 fails UI verification: none of the timetable interface was built. All three timetable pages return a 404 \"page not found\" error, even when signed in as an admin.\n\nThe report has 20 screen-facing requirements: 0 pass, 19 fail and 1 is blocked. The JSON report was written first and checked as valid; the Markdown summary was written last.\n\n| Page | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `/timetable` | 404 |\n| `/admin/timetable` | 404 |\n| `/admin/timetable/periods` | 404 |\n| `/dashboard` | loads, but has no Timetable, Timetable editor or Bell schedule links |\n\n- **Pages I couldn't open:** the student \"Timetable\" tab and course \"Schedule\" tab need students or courses, and the dev database has none. I failed them from the code instead: neither the tab entries nor the route folders exist.\n- **Blocked:** browser and print checks (NFR-16). There is no interface to look at, and no browser was driven.\n- **What does work:** the data the interface would use. `GET /api/periods` returns an empty list because the seed data was never built, and `GET /api/school-days` returns Monday–Friday as teaching days.\n- **Cause:** this matches the QA report. Dev stopped after TASK-8 (the backend) and never built TASK-9 to TASK-16 (screens, navigation, seed data, end-to-end test).\n\nTo render the pages I created a temporary admin user (`uiv-sh6@test.local`) and ran a second dev server on port 3200. I then deleted the user and its audit-log entries, removed the helper script and stopped that server. Your own server on port 3000 was not touched.\n\nTwo problems from before this ticket showed up along the way. Both are noted in the report:\n- **Library version mismatch:** `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 is installed alongside `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0. Opening `/admin/sections` fails with a 500 error, and after that the dev server returns 500 for every request until it is restarted. That can make the timetable endpoints look broken when they aren't.\n- **No login page:** `/login` returns 404, so the only way to sign in is through the auth API.\n\n**Next step:** send SH-6 back to Dev to finish TASK-9 to TASK-16, then run this phase again with a real browser (`npx playwright install chromium`).\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/ui-verification/`:\n- `ui-verification-report.json`\n- `ui-verification-report.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2146,"cache_read_input_tokens":62476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2146},"output_tokens":718,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eef66e53-e26d-4204-b561-7eec81d716ed","uuid":"c2405066-ac38-4fa1-b25d-3dfa80367265","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:37:49.649Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEwiwtyw6QskQr7EVu7"}
