{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Nk878pMqRWfux3qmQ76cG","type":"tool_result","content":"total 32\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 ikramaansari  staff   128 Nov  5 10:37 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff   352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  6738 Nov  5 10:37 ui-verification-report.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  4649 Nov  5 10:37 ui-verification-report.md\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:36:59Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"surface\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Rendered as an authenticated ADMIN on `next dev` (:3200): the route returned HTTP 404 (Next not-found page). page.tsx and BellScheduleEditor.tsx are missing. Only GET /api/periods works; it returned 200 {data:[]}.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"surface\": \"Teaching days ToggleButtons + confirm dialog (on /admin/timetable/periods)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Rendered as an authenticated ADMIN on `next dev` (:3200): the route returned HTTP 404 (Next not-found page). Backend only: GET /api/school-days returned 200 with Mon\\u2013Fri teaching and slotCount per day. There is no ToggleButton UI and no confirmation dialog.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"surface\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable (view selector, entity picker, year selector)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Rendered as an authenticated ADMIN on `next dev` (:3200): the route returned HTTP 404 (Next not-found page). TimetableEditor.tsx is missing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"surface\": \"TimetableGrid (days \\u00d7 periods, greyed BREAK/LUNCH, filled-cell content)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"No source exists: no file under src\nFR-2 {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & Routes '/login'\"}\n\nFR-4 {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 2, 3\"}\n\nFR-7 {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n\nFR-11 {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"}\n\nFR-13 {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, FR-4.2; Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\"}\n\nFR-16 {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: the PasswordChecklist component exists. It must be wired into the invite, reset and security pages.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\"}\n\nFR-17 {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: the API exists; the /forgot-password UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"}\n\nFR-19 {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: the API exists; the /reset-password/[token] UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.3; Acceptance Criterion 7\"}\n\nFR-20 {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: the API exists; the /account/security UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1; Pages & Routes '/account/security'\"}\n\nFR-21 {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu. Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\"}\n\nFR-25 {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'. Status: MISSING (PLACEHOLDER_USER is still in shell.tsx).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\"}\n\nFR-26 {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login. Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n\nFR-27 {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role. Status: MISSING (navigationForRole(PLACEHOLDER_USER.role)).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\"}\n\nls: artifacts/intake/figma-readiness.json: No such file or directory\n- TASK-14: NotificationBell + shell wiring — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: /notifications page + NotificationsList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: /account/notifications page + PreferencesTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: /admin/email-log page + EmailLogTable — ✓ complete\n\nUI notes (NFR-10):\n- Before writing any UI, I called mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0), then `fetchDocs` for the v9 upgrade guide and the Badge, Popover, Tabs, Pagination, Switch and Chip APIs.\n- The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props (styles go in `sx`), and `slotProps.primary` for ListItemText, `slotProps.paper` for Popover and `slotProps.input` for Switch.\n- The admin email log reuses the shared DataTable as planned. DataTable's built-in search box writes `?q=`, which the email-log API ignores, so search has no effect there. Making it work would need a DataTable or API change outside this ticket's scope.\n- shell.tsx still has two lint errors (`Avatar` and `theme` unused). They were already there before this change and are not touched.\n- TASK-18: Seed demo notifications — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Unit tests (notifications) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Integration tests (dispatch) + vitest include — ✓ complete\n\nVerification for TASK-18 to TASK-20:\n- Seed:\n  - With the users missing, it logs a skip for each email.\n  - With temporary student@ and parent@ users, two seed runs leave exactly 3 rows each (1 read). The temporary users were removed afterwards.\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: 28 tests pass.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`:\n  - With `TEST_DATABASE_URL` pointing at the local DB, all 3 tests pass: concurrent dispatch sends each row once, a row stuck in SENDING for 11 minutes goes back to PENDING with attempts unchanged, and a freshly claimed SENDING row is left alone.\n  - Without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`, the tests are skipped.\n- Full `vitest run`: 112 tests pass. Three files fail, and none of them import code changed in this ticket:\n  - `lockout.test.ts`: next-auth cannot resolve `next/server` under vitest.\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx`: the `@mui/x-internals` exports map.\n  - `useToast.test.tsx`: the auto-hide timer test.\n- TASK-21: Playwright e2e (bell + preferences) — ✓ complete\n\n### HTTP verification (next dev on :3100, temporary admin, all data removed afterwards)\n- Without a session, `/api/notifications/unread-count` returns 401. Credentials sign-in works.\n- Notification flow:\n  - The admin test button returns `{ok:true}` and the unread count goes from 0 to 1.\n  - The list `category=SYSTEM` filter returns the row; ACADEMIC returns nothing; a bad category returns 400.\n  - read/unread toggles the count. Another user's id returns 404. read-all returns `{count:1}`, then the count is 0.\n- Preferences:\n  - GET returns only `system.test`; the emailOnly types are hidden.\n  - PUT persists the change.\n  - PUT returns VALIDATION_ERROR for `account.invite`, for `__proto__`, and for an extra key.\n- Email log:\n  - The `status` filter works and the response has no html or text.\n  - Retry on a non-FAILED row returns 404; retry on a FAILED row resets it to PENDING.\n- Dispatch:\n  - No token or a wrong token returns 401.\n  - The correct bearer token returns `{sent:1}`.\n- Pages:\n  - `/notifications` and `/account/notifications` render (200).\n  - The SSR markup has `role=\"switch\"` with the label \"Test notification email\" and the bell's \"Notifications\" label, matching the e2e selectors.\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA\n1. **Pre-existing dependency mismatch breaks every DataGrid page.**\n   - Cause: `package-lock.json` resolves `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0` against `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0`, so `./useFirstRender` is not exported.\n   - Effect: `/admin/email-log` (TASK-17) returns 500, and so does the existing `/admin/sections`. It is also why `DataTable.test.tsx` fails.\n   - Not fixed here, because the plan keeps `package.json` untouched.\n   - Fix: align the MUI X versions (for example, install `@mui/x-internals` at the version matching data-grid 9.5.0). After that, the first e2e test can pass, since it starts on `/admin/email-log`.\n2. **The e2e spec was not executed.**\n   - Cause: `@playwright/test@1.47.2` needs chromium revision 1248, but only 1200 is installed locally.\n   - It is listed by `playwright test --list` and its flow was exercised over HTTP as described above.\n   - To run it: `npx playwright install chromium`, then `npm run test:e2e`.\n3. The integration tests need `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. They pass against the local DB on :5433.\n4. The worker and cron route require env to be loaded. tsx does not read `.env` for `env.ts`. The worker happened to work locally because PrismaClient loads `.env` first. In production, set the variables in the process environment.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fec0918a-90f0-4d65-82e8-8c5873335661","uuid":"8c493a6e-204d-456b-bbdc-44a2a6710ef3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:15:30.638Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 32\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 ikramaansari  staff   128 Nov  5 10:37 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff   352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  6738 Nov  5 10:37 ui-verification-report.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  4649 Nov  5 10:37 ui-verification-report.md\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:36:59Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"surface\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Rendered as an authenticated ADMIN on `next dev` (:3200): the route returned HTTP 404 (Next not-found page). page.tsx and BellScheduleEditor.tsx are missing. Only GET /api/periods works; it returned 200 {data:[]}.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"surface\": \"Teaching days ToggleButtons + confirm dialog (on /admin/timetable/periods)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Rendered as an authenticated ADMIN on `next dev` (:3200): the route returned HTTP 404 (Next not-found page). Backend only: GET /api/school-days returned 200 with Mon\\u2013Fri teaching and slotCount per day. There is no ToggleButton UI and no confirmation dialog.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"surface\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable (view selector, entity picker, year selector)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Rendered as an authenticated ADMIN on `next dev` (:3200): the route returned HTTP 404 (Next not-found page). TimetableEditor.tsx is missing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"surface\": \"TimetableGrid (days \\u00d7 periods, greyed BREAK/LUNCH, filled-cell content)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"No source exists: no file under src\nFR-2 {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & Routes '/login'\"}\n\nFR-4 {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 2, 3\"}\n\nFR-7 {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n\nFR-11 {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"}\n\nFR-13 {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, FR-4.2; Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\"}\n\nFR-16 {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: the PasswordChecklist component exists. It must be wired into the invite, reset and security pages.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\"}\n\nFR-17 {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: the API exists; the /forgot-password UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"}\n\nFR-19 {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: the API exists; the /reset-password/[token] UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.3; Acceptance Criterion 7\"}\n\nFR-20 {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: the API exists; the /account/security UI page is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1; Pages & Routes '/account/security'\"}\n\nFR-21 {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu. Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\"}\n\nFR-25 {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'. Status: MISSING (PLACEHOLDER_USER is still in shell.tsx).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\"}\n\nFR-26 {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login. Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n\nFR-27 {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role. Status: MISSING (navigationForRole(PLACEHOLDER_USER.role)).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\"}\n\nls: artifacts/intake/figma-readiness.json: No such file or directory\n- TASK-14: NotificationBell + shell wiring — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: /notifications page + NotificationsList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: /account/notifications page + PreferencesTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: /admin/email-log page + EmailLogTable — ✓ complete\n\nUI notes (NFR-10):\n- Before writing any UI, I called mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0), then `fetchDocs` for the v9 upgrade guide and the Badge, Popover, Tabs, Pagination, Switch and Chip APIs.\n- The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props (styles go in `sx`), and `slotProps.primary` for ListItemText, `slotProps.paper` for Popover and `slotProps.input` for Switch.\n- The admin email log reuses the shared DataTable as planned. DataTable's built-in search box writes `?q=`, which the email-log API ignores, so search has no effect there. Making it work would need a DataTable or API change outside this ticket's scope.\n- shell.tsx still has two lint errors (`Avatar` and `theme` unused). They were already there before this change and are not touched.\n- TASK-18: Seed demo notifications — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Unit tests (notifications) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Integration tests (dispatch) + vitest include — ✓ complete\n\nVerification for TASK-18 to TASK-20:\n- Seed:\n  - With the users missing, it logs a skip for each email.\n  - With temporary student@ and parent@ users, two seed runs leave exactly 3 rows each (1 read). The temporary users were removed afterwards.\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: 28 tests pass.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`:\n  - With `TEST_DATABASE_URL` pointing at the local DB, all 3 tests pass: concurrent dispatch sends each row once, a row stuck in SENDING for 11 minutes goes back to PENDING with attempts unchanged, and a freshly claimed SENDING row is left alone.\n  - Without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`, the tests are skipped.\n- Full `vitest run`: 112 tests pass. Three files fail, and none of them import code changed in this ticket:\n  - `lockout.test.ts`: next-auth cannot resolve `next/server` under vitest.\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx`: the `@mui/x-internals` exports map.\n  - `useToast.test.tsx`: the auto-hide timer test.\n- TASK-21: Playwright e2e (bell + preferences) — ✓ complete\n\n### HTTP verification (next dev on :3100, temporary admin, all data removed afterwards)\n- Without a session, `/api/notifications/unread-count` returns 401. Credentials sign-in works.\n- Notification flow:\n  - The admin test button returns `{ok:true}` and the unread count goes from 0 to 1.\n  - The list `category=SYSTEM` filter returns the row; ACADEMIC returns nothing; a bad category returns 400.\n  - read/unread toggles the count. Another user's id returns 404. read-all returns `{count:1}`, then the count is 0.\n- Preferences:\n  - GET returns only `system.test`; the emailOnly types are hidden.\n  - PUT persists the change.\n  - PUT returns VALIDATION_ERROR for `account.invite`, for `__proto__`, and for an extra key.\n- Email log:\n  - The `status` filter works and the response has no html or text.\n  - Retry on a non-FAILED row returns 404; retry on a FAILED row resets it to PENDING.\n- Dispatch:\n  - No token or a wrong token returns 401.\n  - The correct bearer token returns `{sent:1}`.\n- Pages:\n  - `/notifications` and `/account/notifications` render (200).\n  - The SSR markup has `role=\"switch\"` with the label \"Test notification email\" and the bell's \"Notifications\" label, matching the e2e selectors.\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA\n1. **Pre-existing dependency mismatch breaks every DataGrid page.**\n   - Cause: `package-lock.json` resolves `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0` against `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0`, so `./useFirstRender` is not exported.\n   - Effect: `/admin/email-log` (TASK-17) returns 500, and so does the existing `/admin/sections`. It is also why `DataTable.test.tsx` fails.\n   - Not fixed here, because the plan keeps `package.json` untouched.\n   - Fix: align the MUI X versions (for example, install `@mui/x-internals` at the version matching data-grid 9.5.0). After that, the first e2e test can pass, since it starts on `/admin/email-log`.\n2. **The e2e spec was not executed.**\n   - Cause: `@playwright/test@1.47.2` needs chromium revision 1248, but only 1200 is installed locally.\n   - It is listed by `playwright test --list` and its flow was exercised over HTTP as described above.\n   - To run it: `npx playwright install chromium`, then `npm run test:e2e`.\n3. The integration tests need `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. They pass against the local DB on :5433.\n4. The worker and cron route require env to be loaded. tsx does not read `.env` for `env.ts`. The worker happened to work locally because PrismaClient loads `.env` first. In production, set the variables in the process environment.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014Nk878pMqRWfux3qmQ76cG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
