{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkAgijsDkrnKtNWX3Vfo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JhS3WMbccA1yoGKrApJS5u","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/ui-verification/ui-verification-report.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T17:22:19Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"method\": \"`next dev` on :3300 against the local Postgres (:5433, seeded users). Headless Chromium (Playwright chromium_headless_shell-1200) was run twice: Run A with the app's shipped Content-Security-Policy enforced, and Run B with `bypassCSP: true` to check the SH-1 code on its own. Test INVITE and PASSWORD_RESET tokens were created with createToken(). Afterwards teacher2's password hash and passwordChangedAt were restored, failedLoginCount was reset, and the test tokens were marked used. Screenshots are in artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/ (csp-* = Run A, bypass-* = Run B). There is no figma-readiness.json, so the checks are against the PRD text only.\",\n  \"blockingIssues\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\n      \"summary\": \"The shipped CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser. This was already present before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on client UI.\",\n      \"detail\": \"next.config.js sends `script-src 'self'`. Chromium blocks Next's inline RSC/bootstrap scripts (console: 'Executing inline script violates the following Content Security Policy directive'). The pages server-render correctly but never hydrate. Sign-in, forgot-password, invite accept, reset, password change, the password toggle, the live checklist and the user menu all do nothing. QA reported the same blocker; it is confirmed here independently.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Use a nonce-based CSP set in middleware, or allow 'unsafe-inline' for scripts (plus 'unsafe-eval' in dev only).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"summary\": \"Before hydration, the auth forms submit as native GET forms, which puts passwords in the URL and in the server log.\",\n      \"detail\": \"Run A: submitting /reset-password/[token] went to `/reset-password/<token>?password=LeakCheck2026z&confirm=LeakCheck2026z`. The next dev access log recorded the same query string. The forms have `name` attributes but no `method=\\\"post\\\"`. Under UIV-1 this happens on every submit. Even with a working CSP, it can still happen on slow networks before hydration.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Add method=\\\"post\\\" to the auth/password forms (TokenPasswordForm/SetPasswordForm, LoginForm, ForgotPasswordForm, ChangePasswordForm).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"surface\": \"/login page (Card, email/password TextFields, show-password toggle, Alert, Sign in button)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: the page renders correctly (MUI Card, SchoolHub logo, Email*/Password* fields, eye icon, SIGN IN button, 'Forgot your password?' link; see csp-login-error.png). It never hydrates, though (UIV-1), so the toggle and the signIn('credentials') submit do nothing. Run B: 1 Card, the toggle switches type password→text, and sign-in works.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"surface\": \"/login error Alert\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: no Alert ever appears because the form never hydrates. Run B: a wrong password for parent@ shows the Alert 'Email or password is incorrect.' (bypass-login-fail.png). The locked and disabled messages were not exercised in the browser.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"surface\": \"Post-sign-in redirect (callbackUrl)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: users can't sign in at all (UIV-1). Run B: callbackUrl=https://evil.example.com/x lands on /dashboard, and callbackUrl=/account/security lands on /account/security. Both are correct.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"surface\": \"middleware redirect for unauthenticated (app) pages\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A (shipped CSP): /dashboard → /login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard, and /account/security → /login?callbackUrl=%2Faccount%2Fsecurity. After sign-out, /account/security redirects to login again (Run B). This is server-side, so the CSP doesn't affect it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"surface\": \"/invite/[token] page (invalid and valid states)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Server-rendered states are correct in both runs. An invalid token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' with no sign-up link. A valid token shows 'Welcome to SchoolHub', read-only Name 'Ivy Invited' and Email 'invited@schoolhub.test', password and confirm fields, the checklist, and ACTIVATE ACCOUNT. FAIL because accepting is impossible in Run A (UIV-1), and a submit leaks the password into the URL (UIV-2). In Run B, submitting the invite was not exercised, to avoid activating the seed's INVITED user.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"surface\": \"PasswordChecklist on invite, reset and /account/security\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Present on all three pages with the 4 rules: 10–128 characters, a letter, a number, not the email. Run A: it stays static, because there is no hydration. Run B: it updates live. Typing 'abc1' marks letter, number and not-email as met (green check) and length as unmet (empty circle) (bypass-security-checklist.png).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"surface\": \"/forgot-password page\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Renders the email field, SEND RESET LINK and 'Back to sign in'. Run A: submit does nothing (UIV-1/UIV-2). Run B: an unknown email shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (bypass-forgot-done.png). The rate-limit message was not exercised.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"surface\": \"/reset-password/[token] page + /login success toast\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Invalid token: 'This link is invalid or has expired.' plus a 'Request a new reset link' link (both runs). Valid token: read-only Email, new and confirm fields, the checklist, and SET NEW PASSWORD. Run A: submitting does a native GET and the password lands in the URL and the server log (UIV-2). The reset does not happen. Run B: it redirects to /login?reset=1 and shows the toast 'Password updated. Sign in with your new password.' (bypass-reset-done-login.png). A minor dev-only hydration warning ('Extra attributes from the server: style' on an input) appears on this page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"surface\": \"/account/security page\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Can't be reached through the UI in Run A, because sign-in needs hydration. Run B: the shell layout shows the heading 'Account security', the helper text, Current/New/Confirm fields with visibility toggles, the checklist, and UPDATE PASSWORD. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' (bypass-security-wrong-current.png). The successful change and 'Password updated' toast were not exercised, to avoid changing seeded credentials.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"surface\": \"Top-bar user menu 'Account security' item\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: the menu can't open (no hydration). Run B: the menu shows 'Account security' with a lock icon, linking to /account/security (bypass-user-menu.png).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"surface\": \"App shell uses the session user (no PLACEHOLDER_USER)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run B: the server-rendered shell shows avatar initials 'AA' for admin@ (Alice Admin), and the student's dashboard shows the student's data. layout.tsx passes requirePageUser() into AppShell, and PLACEHOLDER_USER no longer exists in shell.tsx. This markup is server-rendered, so the CSP doesn't change it, but reaching it in a real browser still depends on UIV-1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"surface\": \"User menu: name, role badge, initials, Sign out\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Avatar 'AA' renders server-side. Run A: the menu can't open and Sign out can't be clicked. Run B: the menu shows 'Alice Admin', an 'ADMIN' Chip, Account security and Sign out. Sign out goes to /login, and the session is gone afterwards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"surface\": \"Sidebar navigation filtered by session role\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run B: ADMIN sees Dashboard, Notifications, Email log, then under Administration, Sections and Courses. STUDENT sees Dashboard, Notifications, My courses. The filtering is server-rendered; the same reachability caveat (UIV-1) applies.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blockedReason\": null\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":72931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fec0918a-90f0-4d65-82e8-8c5873335661","uuid":"8840e107-12d0-4016-9f48-27e1673a9716","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:22:54.541Z","request_id":"req_011CgkAgiWygn2K5YWvTiqD9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JhS3WMbccA1yoGKrApJS5u":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/ui-verification/ui-verification-report.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T17:22:19Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"method\": \"`next dev` on :3300 against the local Postgres (:5433, seeded users). Headless Chromium (Playwright chromium_headless_shell-1200) was run twice: Run A with the app's shipped Content-Security-Policy enforced, and Run B with `bypassCSP: true` to check the SH-1 code on its own. Test INVITE and PASSWORD_RESET tokens were created with createToken(). Afterwards teacher2's password hash and passwordChangedAt were restored, failedLoginCount was reset, and the test tokens were marked used. Screenshots are in artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/ (csp-* = Run A, bypass-* = Run B). There is no figma-readiness.json, so the checks are against the PRD text only.\",\n  \"blockingIssues\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\n      \"summary\": \"The shipped CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser. This was already present before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on client UI.\",\n      \"detail\": \"next.config.js sends `script-src 'self'`. Chromium blocks Next's inline RSC/bootstrap scripts (console: 'Executing inline script violates the following Content Security Policy directive'). The pages server-render correctly but never hydrate. Sign-in, forgot-password, invite accept, reset, password change, the password toggle, the live checklist and the user menu all do nothing. QA reported the same blocker; it is confirmed here independently.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Use a nonce-based CSP set in middleware, or allow 'unsafe-inline' for scripts (plus 'unsafe-eval' in dev only).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"summary\": \"Before hydration, the auth forms submit as native GET forms, which puts passwords in the URL and in the server log.\",\n      \"detail\": \"Run A: submitting /reset-password/[token] went to `/reset-password/<token>?password=LeakCheck2026z&confirm=LeakCheck2026z`. The next dev access log recorded the same query string. The forms have `name` attributes but no `method=\\\"post\\\"`. Under UIV-1 this happens on every submit. Even with a working CSP, it can still happen on slow networks before hydration.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Add method=\\\"post\\\" to the auth/password forms (TokenPasswordForm/SetPasswordForm, LoginForm, ForgotPasswordForm, ChangePasswordForm).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"surface\": \"/login page (Card, email/password TextFields, show-password toggle, Alert, Sign in button)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: the page renders correctly (MUI Card, SchoolHub logo, Email*/Password* fields, eye icon, SIGN IN button, 'Forgot your password?' link; see csp-login-error.png). It never hydrates, though (UIV-1), so the toggle and the signIn('credentials') submit do nothing. Run B: 1 Card, the toggle switches type password→text, and sign-in works.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"surface\": \"/login error Alert\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: no Alert ever appears because the form never hydrates. Run B: a wrong password for parent@ shows the Alert 'Email or password is incorrect.' (bypass-login-fail.png). The locked and disabled messages were not exercised in the browser.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"surface\": \"Post-sign-in redirect (callbackUrl)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: users can't sign in at all (UIV-1). Run B: callbackUrl=https://evil.example.com/x lands on /dashboard, and callbackUrl=/account/security lands on /account/security. Both are correct.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"surface\": \"middleware redirect for unauthenticated (app) pages\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A (shipped CSP): /dashboard → /login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard, and /account/security → /login?callbackUrl=%2Faccount%2Fsecurity. After sign-out, /account/security redirects to login again (Run B). This is server-side, so the CSP doesn't affect it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"surface\": \"/invite/[token] page (invalid and valid states)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Server-rendered states are correct in both runs. An invalid token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' with no sign-up link. A valid token shows 'Welcome to SchoolHub', read-only Name 'Ivy Invited' and Email 'invited@schoolhub.test', password and confirm fields, the checklist, and ACTIVATE ACCOUNT. FAIL because accepting is impossible in Run A (UIV-1), and a submit leaks the password into the URL (UIV-2). In Run B, submitting the invite was not exercised, to avoid activating the seed's INVITED user.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"surface\": \"PasswordChecklist on invite, reset and /account/security\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Present on all three pages with the 4 rules: 10–128 characters, a letter, a number, not the email. Run A: it stays static, because there is no hydration. Run B: it updates live. Typing 'abc1' marks letter, number and not-email as met (green check) and length as unmet (empty circle) (bypass-security-checklist.png).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"surface\": \"/forgot-password page\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Renders the email field, SEND RESET LINK and 'Back to sign in'. Run A: submit does nothing (UIV-1/UIV-2). Run B: an unknown email shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (bypass-forgot-done.png). The rate-limit message was not exercised.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"surface\": \"/reset-password/[token] page + /login success toast\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Invalid token: 'This link is invalid or has expired.' plus a 'Request a new reset link' link (both runs). Valid token: read-only Email, new and confirm fields, the checklist, and SET NEW PASSWORD. Run A: submitting does a native GET and the password lands in the URL and the server log (UIV-2). The reset does not happen. Run B: it redirects to /login?reset=1 and shows the toast 'Password updated. Sign in with your new password.' (bypass-reset-done-login.png). A minor dev-only hydration warning ('Extra attributes from the server: style' on an input) appears on this page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"surface\": \"/account/security page\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Can't be reached through the UI in Run A, because sign-in needs hydration. Run B: the shell layout shows the heading 'Account security', the helper text, Current/New/Confirm fields with visibility toggles, the checklist, and UPDATE PASSWORD. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' (bypass-security-wrong-current.png). The successful change and 'Password updated' toast were not exercised, to avoid changing seeded credentials.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"surface\": \"Top-bar user menu 'Account security' item\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: the menu can't open (no hydration). Run B: the menu shows 'Account security' with a lock icon, linking to /account/security (bypass-user-menu.png).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"surface\": \"App shell uses the session user (no PLACEHOLDER_USER)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run B: the server-rendered shell shows avatar initials 'AA' for admin@ (Alice Admin), and the student's dashboard shows the student's data. layout.tsx passes requirePageUser() into AppShell, and PLACEHOLDER_USER no longer exists in shell.tsx. This markup is server-rendered, so the CSP doesn't change it, but reaching it in a real browser still depends on UIV-1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"surface\": \"User menu: name, role badge, initials, Sign out\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Avatar 'AA' renders server-side. Run A: the menu can't open and Sign out can't be clicked. Run B: the menu shows 'Alice Admin', an 'ADMIN' Chip, Account security and Sign out. Sign out goes to /login, and the session is gone afterwards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"surface\": \"Sidebar navigation filtered by session role\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run B: ADMIN sees Dashboard, Notifications, Email log, then under Administration, Sections and Courses. STUDENT sees Dashboard, Notifications, My courses. The filtering is server-rendered; the same reachability caveat (UIV-1) applies.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blockedReason\": null\n}\n"}}}
