{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkAkNHB4yKiNfvMkRMLi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SH-1 fails UI verification: 3 of 13 user-facing requirements pass and 10 fail. The SH-1 pages themselves behave as the PRD describes, but in a real browser almost none of them work, because of two problems.\n\nI ran the dev server against the local database and drove the pages in headless Chromium twice: once with the app's real Content Security Policy (CSP, the security header) and once with it switched off.\n\n**1. Blocker: the CSP stops the pages from becoming interactive.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks the inline scripts Next.js needs to start React in the browser. Every page renders, but sign-in, all form submits, the show-password toggle, the live password checklist and the user menu do nothing. QA reported this too, and it was there before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on it. The fix is a nonce-based CSP set in middleware, or allowing `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts.\n\n**2. High: forms leak passwords into the URL.** When React hasn't started, submitting a form falls back to a plain browser GET. The reset form sent me to `/reset-password/<token>?password=LeakCheck2026z&confirm=...`, and the dev server log recorded the same URL. Adding `method=\"post\"` to the login, forgot-password, invite/reset and change-password forms fixes it. This can still happen on slow connections even after the CSP is fixed.\n\nWith the CSP switched off, everything I exercised worked:\n- **Login:** a wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\", and an external `callbackUrl` is ignored in favour of `/dashboard`.\n- **Forgot password:** shows the same message whether or not the email exists.\n- **Invite and reset pages:** the invalid-link and valid states render correctly. A completed reset redirects to `/login` with the success toast.\n- **Password checklist:** updates live as you type.\n- **`/account/security`:** a wrong current password shows \"Current password is incorrect.\"\n- **User menu:** shows the name, an ADMIN badge, \"Account security\" and a working Sign out.\n- **Sidebar:** filtered by role (admin and student see different items).\n\nThe three passes are the login redirect for signed-out users, the shell using the real signed-in user, and the role-filtered sidebar. These are server-rendered, so the CSP doesn't affect them.\n\nI didn't test the locked/disabled-account messages, accepting an invite, or a successful password change, so seeded accounts stay as they were.\n\nChanges to the local database:\n- teacher2's password was really reset during the test. I restored the original, and reset the failed-login counters.\n- Making a test invite token cancelled the invite link the seed printed earlier. Run `npm run db:seed` to get a new one.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/ui-verification/`:\n- `ui-verification-report.md`\n- `ui-verification-report.json`\n- `screenshots/`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":280,"cache_read_input_tokens":79335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":280},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fec0918a-90f0-4d65-82e8-8c5873335661","uuid":"1d8d9714-444b-48ea-bfd6-9c22be2453b3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:23:24.845Z","request_id":"req_011CgkAkMy5GPoQKZixjcVzi"}
