AIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"The content is correct: each meeting shows 'UIV Attendance – uiv-att · 00:00–23:59 · Now' with a 'Not taken' chip, and after the save it shows 'Taken 01:39 by Terry Teach' and a REVIEW button. Layout defect: at 360 px the page is 407 px wide. The 'Register date' DatePicker runs past the right edge, and the app bar stops at 360. Cause: PageHeader puts `actions` in a non-wrapping `Stack direction=\\\"row\\\"`, and DateNav's DatePicker keeps its full width beside the title. Screenshots: teacher-landing-360.png, teacher-landing-after-save-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take — 'Daily register – <section>' entry\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"With attendanceMode=BOTH, the homeroom teacher sees 'Daily register – uiv-att' with 'Not taken' and TAKE ATTENDANCE above the course meeting. Screenshot: teacher-landing-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register date picker and date limits\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The DatePicker renders (its 360 px overflow is reported under FR-6). A future date (2026-11-08) shows the alert 'Registers cannot be taken for future dates'. For the teacher, a 20-day-old date shows 'Teachers can edit registers up to 14 days after the register date'. An admin can open the same 20-day-old date. Screenshots: teacher-register-future-360.png, teacher-register-old-360.png, admin-register-1280.png. The calendar's own disabled-date UI was not clicked through.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take/[courseId] register list\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Students are sorted by last name (Absent, Late, Present). Each row has an initials avatar, the name and an exclusive P/A/L/E ToggleButtonGroup with aria-labels ('Mark Alex Absent absent'). Nothing is preselected (Unmarked 3). Selected buttons use theme colours: A error-red, L warning-orange, P success-green. Screenshots: teacher-register-empty-360.png, teacher-register-saved-1280.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"surface\": \"EXCUSED (E) toggle\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"E is disabled (greyed) for the teacher and enabled for the admin.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"surface\": \"'Mark all present' button\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Lee was marked Absent first. 'Mark all present' then gave Present 2 · Absent 1, so it does not overwrite existing selections. The button is disabled once nobody is unmarked.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"surface\": \"Minutes-late input and note field\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Selecting L reveals 'Minutes late' prefilled with 5. The note icon toggles a 'Note' text field; 'Called in sick' was entered and was still there after the save. The 1–240 range and the 500-character limit were not driven through the UI; the validators cover them and are unit-tested.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"surface\": \"Header counters and Save state\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The chips 'Present n · Absent n · Late n · Unmarked n' update live. Save is disabled while the bar reads '3 students not marked', and enabled once it reads 'Everyone is marked'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"surface\": \"Save and 'last changed' display\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The 'Attendance saved' toast appears, and 'Last changed by Terry Teach at 11/6/2026, 11:39:36 AM' shows on the saved register. Minor: this timestamp uses the browser's timezone (`toLocaleString`), while the landing page ('Taken 01:39') and the notification ('1:39 AM') use the school timezone (America/New_York). The same save therefore shows two different times. Screenshot: teacher-register-saved-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"surface\": \"Daily register roster\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"The homeroom teacher's daily register lists the 3 section members (Unmarked 3). Screenshot: teacher-daily-register-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"This route reuses the register component, with the breadcrumb 'Take attendance / Daily register' and the title 'Daily register – uiv-att · Friday 6 Nov 2026'. Saving a daily register was not exercised in the UI; the integration tests cover it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register at 360 px\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"No horizontal overflow on the register page. Row heights are 110–158 px (at least 48). All 12 P/A/L/E toggles measure at least 44×49 px. The save bar is a Paper with position: sticky and bottom: 0, and it stays on screen over the rows (teacher-register-filled-360.png). The 360 px overflow on the landing page is reported under FR-6.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"surface\": \"Register past the 14-day window (teacher)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"PRD FR-4.2 and AC-4 say: 'Given a register date 20 days ago, when Tom opens it, then it is read-only with the explanation'. What renders is only the heading 'Register' and a warning alert; no roster, statuses or counters are shown. Cause: `canOpen` (FR-8 window) refuses the page before `canEdit`'s readOnly path can run. RegisterForm's read-only branch exists but teachers can never reach it. The admin can still edit at 20 days. Screenshot: teacher-register-old-360.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"surface\": \"Parent /notifications (absence notification)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"After the teacher marked Alex absent, parent Paula at 375 px sees 'Alex Absent was marked absent — UIV Attendance – uiv-att, uiv-att, Friday 6 Nov 2026' with an unread badge of 1. Screenshot: parent-notifications-375.png. FR-22 ('attendance.corrected') has no separate UI surface and was not exercised; QA found a duplicate-notification defect in the service layer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student 'Attendance' tab\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"/students/[id]/attendance returns 500 with the compile overlay (UIV-1). Screenshot: parent-student-attendance-375.png.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: summary cards\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render because the page fails to compile (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: month calendar (coloured days and tooltip)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). So the parent red-day check (AC / FR-41) cannot be verified visually.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"surface\": \"Student tab: records table and note visibility\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). The DataTable itself is the failing import.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"surface\": \"/courses/[courseId]/attendance matrix\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run 1: GET returned 500 with 'Module not found: ./useFirstRender' and an import trace through CourseAttendanceMatrix.tsx. Not re-shot in run 2, because the dev server stays broken after the first DataGrid failure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"The whole page fails to compile (UIV-1); see the FR-5 screenshot.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Missing registers and 'Remind teacher'\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance report builder and CSV\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). ReportTab is the module that triggers the failure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Below threshold\",\n      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"surface\": \"Sidebar navigation\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Teacher sidebar: 'Attendance' links to /attendance/take. Admin sidebar: 'Attendance' links to /admin/attendance in the main group (above 'Administration'). Screenshots: teacher-register-saved-1280.png, admin-dashboard-1280.png.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": { \"PASS\": 14, \"FAIL\": 6, \"BLOCKED\": 7 },\n  \"blockedReason\": null\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":106,"newStart":1,"newLines":177,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T17:22:19Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:55:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\","," ","   \"status\": \"complete\",","-  \"method\": \"`next dev` on :3300 against the local Postgres (:5433, seeded users). Headless Chromium (Playwright chromium_headless_shell-1200) was run twice: Run A with the app's shipped Content-Security-Policy enforced, and Run B with `bypassCSP: true` to check the SH-1 code on its own. Test INVITE and PASSWORD_RESET tokens were created with createToken(). Afterwards teacher2's password hash and passwordChangedAt were restored, failedLoginCount was reset, and the test tokens were marked used. Screenshots are in artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/ (csp-* = Run A, bypass-* = Run B). There is no figma-readiness.json, so the checks are against the PRD text only.\",","+  \"method\": \"`next dev -p 3300` against the local Postgres (:5433). The existing :3000 server was stale, returned 500 for every route, and belongs to another checkout, so it was left alone. The dev DB has no courses, sections or periods, so a throwaway Playwright driver (outside the repo) created tagged fixtures: teacher Terry Teach as course teacher and homeroom teacher, 3 students (Alex Absent, Lee Late, Pat Present), parent Paula linked to Alex, a 00:00–23:59 period, section 'uiv-att' with members, course 'UIV Attendance' enrolled 30 days back, and timetable slots on every weekday. attendanceMode was set to BOTH for the run and restored to PER_PERIOD. All fixtures were deleted afterwards (verified 0 rows). Viewports: 360×740 (teacher), 375×667 (parent), 1280×800 (desktop and admin). One pass ran with the shipped CSP enforced; the rest used bypassCSP:true, the same as QA and the e2e spec. Screenshots are in artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/ and raw probe output is in artifacts/ui-verification/uiv-raw.json. There is no figma-readiness.json, so the checks are against the PRD and requirements.json text only. Note: the first DataGrid compile failure leaves `next dev` returning 500 for every later request, so DataGrid pages were visited last.\",","   \"blockingIssues\": [","     {","       \"id\": \"UIV-1\",","       \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",","-      \"summary\": \"The shipped CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser. This was already present before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on client UI.\",","-      \"detail\": \"next.config.js sends `script-src 'self'`. Chromium blocks Next's inline RSC/bootstrap scripts (console: 'Executing inline script violates the following Content Security Policy directive'). The pages server-render correctly but never hydrate. Sign-in, forgot-password, invite accept, reset, password change, the password toggle, the live checklist and the user menu all do nothing. QA reported the same blocker; it is confirmed here independently.\",","-      \"fix\": \"Use a nonce-based CSP set in middleware, or allow 'unsafe-inline' for scripts (plus 'unsafe-eval' in dev only).\"","+      \"summary\": \"MUI X version skew: @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0 imports @mui/x-internals/useFirstRender, but the installed x-internals 9.15.0 no longer exports it. Every SH-7 page with a DataGrid fails to compile.\",","+      \"detail\": \"Observed build-error overlays: /students/[id]/attendance (StudentAttendanceClient → DataTable), /admin/attendance (AdminAttendanceClient → ReportTab), and /courses/[courseId]/attendance (CourseAttendanceMatrix, seen in run 1 with a server-log import trace and a 500). The admin Settings, Today and Below-threshold tabs are lost as well, because ReportTab is a static import. This is the same root cause as QA finding 1, and it is outside SH-7 file ownership. Fix: pin @mui/x-internals to the 9.5 line or upgrade all @mui/x-* packages together.\"","     },","     {","       \"id\": \"UIV-2\",","-      \"severity\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"summary\": \"Before hydration, the auth forms submit as native GET forms, which puts passwords in the URL and in the server log.\",","-      \"detail\": \"Run A: submitting /reset-password/[token] went to `/reset-password/<token>?password=LeakCheck2026z&confirm=LeakCheck2026z`. The next dev access log recorded the same query string. The forms have `name` attributes but no `method=\\\"post\\\"`. Under UIV-1 this happens on every submit. Even with a working CSP, it can still happen on slow networks before hydration.\",","-      \"fix\": \"Add method=\\\"post\\\" to the auth/password forms (TokenPasswordForm/SetPasswordForm, LoginForm, ForgotPasswordForm, ChangePasswordForm).\"","+      \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",","+      \"summary\": \"The shipped CSP (`script-src 'self'`) blocks hydration. With CSP enforced, the register never hydrates: 'Mark all present' does nothing and there are 10 CSP console errors.\",","+      \"detail\": \"This was present before SH-7 (QA finding 5 / SH-1 UIV-1). Screenshot: csp-register-360.png. The server-rendered markup is correct, but no client interaction works in a real browser.\"","     }","   ],","   \"findings\": [","     {","-      \"requirementId\": \"FR-2\",","-      \"surface\": \"/login page (Card, email/password TextFields, show-password toggle, Alert, Sign in button)\",","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-5\",","+      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance → Settings tab (attendanceMode, alert threshold)\",","       \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Run A: the page renders correctly (MUI Card, SchoolHub logo, Email*/Password* fields, eye icon, SIGN IN button, 'Forgot your password?' link; see csp-login-error.png). It never hydrates, though (UIV-1), so the toggle and the signIn('credentials') submit do nothing. Run B: 1 Card, the toggle switches type password→text, and sign-in works.\"","+      \"notes\": \"The page renders a Next 'Failed to compile' overlay (UIV-1). The import trace runs through ReportTab.tsx, so the Settings tab cannot be reached. Screenshot: admin-attendance-1280.png.\"","     },","     {","-      \"requirementId\": \"FR-4\",","-      \"surface\": \"/login error Alert\",","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-6\",","+      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take landing (today's schedule)\",","       \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Run A: no Alert ever appears because the form never hydrates. Run B: a wrong password for parent@ shows the Alert 'Email or password is incorrect.' (bypass-login-fail.png). The locked and disabled messages were not exercised in the browser.\"","+      \"notes\": \"The content is correct: each meeting shows 'UIV Attendance – uiv-att · 00:00–23:59 · Now' with a 'Not taken' chip, and after the save it shows 'Taken 01:39 by Terry Teach' and a REVIEW button. Layout defect: at 360 px the page is 407 px wide. The 'Register date' DatePicker runs past the right edge, and the app bar stops at 360. Cause: PageHeader puts `actions` in a non-wrapping `Stack direction=\\\"row\\\"`, and DateNav's DatePicker keeps its full width beside the title. Screenshots: teacher-landing-360.png, teacher-landing-after-save-360.png.\"","     },","     {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",","-      \"surface\": \"Post-sign-in redirect (callbackUrl)\",","-      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Run A: users can't sign in at all (UIV-1). Run B: callbackUrl=https://evil.example.com/x lands on /dashboard, and callbackUrl=/account/security lands on /account/security. Both are correct.\"","+      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take — 'Daily register – <section>' entry\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"With attendanceMode=BOTH, the homeroom teacher sees 'Daily register – uiv-att' with 'Not taken' and TAKE ATTENDANCE above the course meeting. Screenshot: teacher-landing-360.png.\"","     },","     {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-8\",","+      \"surface\": \"Register date picker and date limits\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"The DatePicker renders (its 360 px overflow is reported under FR-6). A future date (2026-11-08) shows the alert 'Registers cannot be taken for future dates'. For the teacher, a 20-day-old date shows 'Teachers can edit registers up to 14 days after the register date'. An admin can open the same 20-day-old date. Screenshots: teacher-register-future-360.png, teacher-register-old-360.png, admin-register-1280.png. The calendar's own disabled-date UI was not clicked through.\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-9\",","+      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take/[courseId] register list\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"Students are sorted by last name (Absent, Late, Present). Each row has an initials avatar, the name and an exclusive P/A/L/E ToggleButtonGroup with aria-labels ('Mark Alex Absent absent'). Nothing is preselected (Unmarked 3). Selected buttons use theme colours: A error-red, L warning-orange, P success-green. Screenshots: teacher-register-empty-360.png, teacher-register-saved-1280.png.\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-10\",","+      \"surface\": \"EXCUSED (E) toggle\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"E is disabled (greyed) for the teacher and enabled for the admin.\"","+    },","+    {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-11\",","-      \"surface\": \"middleware redirect for unauthenticated (app) pages\",","+      \"surface\": \"'Mark all present' button\",","       \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","-      \"notes\": \"Run A (shipped CSP): /dashboard → /login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard, and /account/security → /login?callbackUrl=%2Faccount%2Fsecurity. After sign-out, /account/security redirects to login again (Run B). This is server-side, so the CSP doesn't affect it.\"","+      \"notes\": \"Lee was marked Absent first. 'Mark all present' then gave Present 2 · Absent 1, so it does not overwrite existing selections. The button is disabled once nobody is unmarked.\"","     },","     {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-12\",","+      \"surface\": \"Minutes-late input and note field\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"Selecting L reveals 'Minutes late' prefilled with 5. The note icon toggles a 'Note' text field; 'Called in sick' was entered and was still there after the save. The 1–240 range and the 500-character limit were not driven through the UI; the validators cover them and are unit-tested.\"","+    },","+    {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-13\",","-      \"surface\": \"/invite/[token] page (invalid and valid states)\",","-      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Server-rendered states are correct in both runs. An invalid token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' with no sign-up link. A valid token shows 'Welcome to SchoolHub', read-only Name 'Ivy Invited' and Email 'invited@schoolhub.test', password and confirm fields, the checklist, and ACTIVATE ACCOUNT. FAIL because accepting is impossible in Run A (UIV-1), and a submit leaks the password into the URL (UIV-2). In Run B, submitting the invite was not exercised, to avoid activating the seed's INVITED user.\"","+      \"surface\": \"Header counters and Save state\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"The chips 'Present n · Absent n · Late n · Unmarked n' update live. Save is disabled while the bar reads '3 students not marked', and enabled once it reads 'Everyone is marked'.\"","     },","     {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-14\",","+      \"surface\": \"Save and 'last changed' display\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"The 'Attendance saved' toast appears, and 'Last changed by Terry Teach at 11/6/2026, 11:39:36 AM' shows on the saved register. Minor: this timestamp uses the browser's timezone (`toLocaleString`), while the landing page ('Taken 01:39') and the notification ('1:39 AM') use the school timezone (America/New_York). The same save therefore shows two different times. Screenshot: teacher-register-saved-360.png.\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-15\",","+      \"surface\": \"Daily register roster\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"The homeroom teacher's daily register lists the 3 section members (Unmarked 3). Screenshot: teacher-daily-register-360.png.\"","+    },","+    {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",","-      \"surface\": \"PasswordChecklist on invite, reset and /account/security\",","-      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Present on all three pages with the 4 rules: 10–128 characters, a letter, a number, not the email. Run A: it stays static, because there is no hydration. Run B: it updates live. Typing 'abc1' marks letter, number and not-email as met (green check) and length as unmet (empty circle) (bypass-security-checklist.png).\"","+      \"surface\": \"/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"This route reuses the register component, with the breadcrumb 'Take attendance / Daily register' and the title 'Daily register – uiv-att · Friday 6 Nov 2026'. Saving a daily register was not exercised in the UI; the integration tests cover it.\"","     },","     {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-17\",","-      \"surface\": \"/forgot-password page\",","-      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Renders the email field, SEND RESET LINK and 'Back to sign in'. Run A: submit does nothing (UIV-1/UIV-2). Run B: an unknown email shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (bypass-forgot-done.png). The rate-limit message was not exercised.\"","+      \"surface\": \"Register at 360 px\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"No horizontal overflow on the register page. Row heights are 110–158 px (at least 48). All 12 P/A/L/E toggles measure at least 44×49 px. The save bar is a Paper with position: sticky and bottom: 0, and it stays on screen over the rows (teacher-register-filled-360.png). The 360 px overflow on the landing page is reported under FR-6.\"","     },","     {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-19\",","-      \"surface\": \"/reset-password/[token] page + /login success toast\",","+      \"surface\": \"Register past the 14-day window (teacher)\",","       \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Invalid token: 'This link is invalid or has expired.' plus a 'Request a new reset link' link (both runs). Valid token: read-only Email, new and confirm fields, the checklist, and SET NEW PASSWORD. Run A: submitting does a native GET and the password lands in the URL and the server log (UIV-2). The reset does not happen. Run B: it redirects to /login?reset=1 and shows the toast 'Password updated. Sign in with your new password.' (bypass-reset-done-login.png). A minor dev-only hydration warning ('Extra attributes from the server: style' on an input) appears on this page.\"","+      \"notes\": \"PRD FR-4.2 and AC-4 say: 'Given a register date 20 days ago, when Tom opens it, then it is read-only with the explanation'. What renders is only the heading 'Register' and a warning alert; no roster, statuses or counters are shown. Cause: `canOpen` (FR-8 window) refuses the page before `canEdit`'s readOnly path can run. RegisterForm's read-only branch exists but teachers can never reach it. The admin can still edit at 20 days. Screenshot: teacher-register-old-360.png.\"","     },","     {","-      \"requirementId\": \"FR-20\",","-      \"surface\": \"/account/security page\",","-      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Can't be reached through the UI in Run A, because sign-in needs hydration. Run B: the shell layout shows the heading 'Account security', the helper text, Current/New/Confirm fields with visibility toggles, the checklist, and UPDATE PASSWORD. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' (bypass-security-wrong-current.png). The successful change and 'Password updated' toast were not exercised, to avoid changing seeded credentials.\"","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-21\",","+      \"surface\": \"Parent /notifications (absence notification)\",","+      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","+      \"notes\": \"After the teacher marked Alex absent, parent Paula at 375 px sees 'Alex Absent was marked absent — UIV Attendance – uiv-att, uiv-att, Friday 6 Nov 2026' with an unread badge of 1. Screenshot: parent-notifications-375.png. FR-22 ('attendance.corrected') has no separate UI surface and was not exercised; QA found a duplicate-notification defect in the service layer.\"","     },","     {","-      \"requirementId\": \"FR-21\",","-      \"surface\": \"Top-bar user menu 'Account security' item\",","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-24\",","+      \"surface\": \"Student 'Attendance' tab\",","       \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Run A: the menu can't open (no hydration). Run B: the menu shows 'Account security' with a lock icon, linking to /account/security (bypass-user-menu.png).\"","+      \"notes\": \"/students/[id]/attendance returns 500 with the compile overlay (UIV-1). Screenshot: parent-student-attendance-375.png.\"","     },","     {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-25\",","-      \"surface\": \"App shell uses the session user (no PLACEHOLDER_USER)\",","-      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","-      \"notes\": \"Run B: the server-rendered shell shows avatar initials 'AA' for admin@ (Alice Admin), and the student's dashboard shows the student's data. layout.tsx passes requirePageUser() into AppShell, and PLACEHOLDER_USER no longer exists in shell.tsx. This markup is server-rendered, so the CSP doesn't change it, but reaching it in a real browser still depends on UIV-1.\"","+      \"surface\": \"Student tab: summary cards\",","+      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",","+      \"notes\": \"Cannot render because the page fails to compile (UIV-1).\"","     },","     {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-26\",","-      \"surface\": \"User menu: name, role badge, initials, Sign out\",","-      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","-      \"notes\": \"Avatar 'AA' renders server-side. Run A: the menu can't open and Sign out can't be clicked. Run B: the menu shows 'Alice Admin', an 'ADMIN' Chip, Account security and Sign out. Sign out goes to /login, and the session is gone afterwards.\"","+      \"surface\": \"Student tab: month calendar (coloured days and tooltip)\",","+      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",","+      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). So the parent red-day check (AC / FR-41) cannot be verified visually.\"","     },","     {","       \"requirementId\": \"FR-27\",","-      \"surface\": \"Sidebar navigation filtered by session role\",","+      \"surface\": \"Student tab: records table and note visibility\",","+      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",","+      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). The DataTable itself is the failing import.\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-29\",","+      \"surface\": \"/courses/[courseId]/attendance matrix\",","+      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",","+      \"notes\": \"Run 1: GET returned 500 with 'Module not found: ./useFirstRender' and an import trace through CourseAttendanceMatrix.tsx. Not re-shot in run 2, because the dev server stays broken after the first DataGrid failure.\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-30\",","+      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview\",","+      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",","+      \"notes\": \"The whole page fails to compile (UIV-1); see the FR-5 screenshot.\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-31\",","+      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Missing registers and 'Remind teacher'\",","+      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",","+      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1).\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-32\",","+      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance report builder and CSV\",","+      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",","+      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1). ReportTab is the module that triggers the failure.\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-33\",","+      \"surface\": \"/admin/attendance Below threshold\",","+      \"verdict\": \"BLOCKED\",","+      \"notes\": \"Cannot render (UIV-1).\"","+    },","+    {","+      \"requirementId\": \"FR-34\",","+      \"surface\": \"Sidebar navigation\",","       \"verdict\": \"PASS\",","-      \"notes\": \"Run B: ADMIN sees Dashboard, Notifications, Email log, then under Administration, Sections and Courses. STUDENT sees Dashboard, Notifications, My courses. The filtering is server-rendered; the same reachability caveat (UIV-1) applies.\"","+      \"notes\": \"Teacher sidebar: 'Attendance' links to /attendance/take. Admin sidebar: 'Attendance' links to /admin/attendance in the main group (above 'Administration'). Screenshots: teacher-register-saved-1280.png, admin-dashboard-1280.png.\"","     }","   ],","+  \"summary\": { \"PASS\": 14, \"FAIL\": 6, \"BLOCKED\": 7 },","   \"blockedReason\": null"," }"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T17:22:19Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"method\": \"`next dev` on :3300 against the local Postgres (:5433, seeded users). Headless Chromium (Playwright chromium_headless_shell-1200) was run twice: Run A with the app's shipped Content-Security-Policy enforced, and Run B with `bypassCSP: true` to check the SH-1 code on its own. Test INVITE and PASSWORD_RESET tokens were created with createToken(). Afterwards teacher2's password hash and passwordChangedAt were restored, failedLoginCount was reset, and the test tokens were marked used. Screenshots are in artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/ (csp-* = Run A, bypass-* = Run B). There is no figma-readiness.json, so the checks are against the PRD text only.\",\n  \"blockingIssues\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"BLOCKER\",\n      \"summary\": \"The shipped CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser. This was already present before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on client UI.\",\n      \"detail\": \"next.config.js sends `script-src 'self'`. Chromium blocks Next's inline RSC/bootstrap scripts (console: 'Executing inline script violates the following Content Security Policy directive'). The pages server-render correctly but never hydrate. Sign-in, forgot-password, invite accept, reset, password change, the password toggle, the live checklist and the user menu all do nothing. QA reported the same blocker; it is confirmed here independently.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Use a nonce-based CSP set in middleware, or allow 'unsafe-inline' for scripts (plus 'unsafe-eval' in dev only).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"UIV-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"summary\": \"Before hydration, the auth forms submit as native GET forms, which puts passwords in the URL and in the server log.\",\n      \"detail\": \"Run A: submitting /reset-password/[token] went to `/reset-password/<token>?password=LeakCheck2026z&confirm=LeakCheck2026z`. The next dev access log recorded the same query string. The forms have `name` attributes but no `method=\\\"post\\\"`. Under UIV-1 this happens on every submit. Even with a working CSP, it can still happen on slow networks before hydration.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Add method=\\\"post\\\" to the auth/password forms (TokenPasswordForm/SetPasswordForm, LoginForm, ForgotPasswordForm, ChangePasswordForm).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"surface\": \"/login page (Card, email/password TextFields, show-password toggle, Alert, Sign in button)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: the page renders correctly (MUI Card, SchoolHub logo, Email*/Password* fields, eye icon, SIGN IN button, 'Forgot your password?' link; see csp-login-error.png). It never hydrates, though (UIV-1), so the toggle and the signIn('credentials') submit do nothing. Run B: 1 Card, the toggle switches type password→text, and sign-in works.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"surface\": \"/login error Alert\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: no Alert ever appears because the form never hydrates. Run B: a wrong password for parent@ shows the Alert 'Email or password is incorrect.' (bypass-login-fail.png). The locked and disabled messages were not exercised in the browser.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"surface\": \"Post-sign-in redirect (callbackUrl)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: users can't sign in at all (UIV-1). Run B: callbackUrl=https://evil.example.com/x lands on /dashboard, and callbackUrl=/account/security lands on /account/security. Both are correct.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"surface\": \"middleware redirect for unauthenticated (app) pages\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A (shipped CSP): /dashboard → /login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard, and /account/security → /login?callbackUrl=%2Faccount%2Fsecurity. After sign-out, /account/security redirects to login again (Run B). This is server-side, so the CSP doesn't affect it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"surface\": \"/invite/[token] page (invalid and valid states)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Server-rendered states are correct in both runs. An invalid token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' with no sign-up link. A valid token shows 'Welcome to SchoolHub', read-only Name 'Ivy Invited' and Email 'invited@schoolhub.test', password and confirm fields, the checklist, and ACTIVATE ACCOUNT. FAIL because accepting is impossible in Run A (UIV-1), and a submit leaks the password into the URL (UIV-2). In Run B, submitting the invite was not exercised, to avoid activating the seed's INVITED user.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"surface\": \"PasswordChecklist on invite, reset and /account/security\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Present on all three pages with the 4 rules: 10–128 characters, a letter, a number, not the email. Run A: it stays static, because there is no hydration. Run B: it updates live. Typing 'abc1' marks letter, number and not-email as met (green check) and length as unmet (empty circle) (bypass-security-checklist.png).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"surface\": \"/forgot-password page\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Renders the email field, SEND RESET LINK and 'Back to sign in'. Run A: submit does nothing (UIV-1/UIV-2). Run B: an unknown email shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (bypass-forgot-done.png). The rate-limit message was not exercised.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"surface\": \"/reset-password/[token] page + /login success toast\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Invalid token: 'This link is invalid or has expired.' plus a 'Request a new reset link' link (both runs). Valid token: read-only Email, new and confirm fields, the checklist, and SET NEW PASSWORD. Run A: submitting does a native GET and the password lands in the URL and the server log (UIV-2). The reset does not happen. Run B: it redirects to /login?reset=1 and shows the toast 'Password updated. Sign in with your new password.' (bypass-reset-done-login.png). A minor dev-only hydration warning ('Extra attributes from the server: style' on an input) appears on this page.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"surface\": \"/account/security page\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Can't be reached through the UI in Run A, because sign-in needs hydration. Run B: the shell layout shows the heading 'Account security', the helper text, Current/New/Confirm fields with visibility toggles, the checklist, and UPDATE PASSWORD. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' (bypass-security-wrong-current.png). The successful change and 'Password updated' toast were not exercised, to avoid changing seeded credentials.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"surface\": \"Top-bar user menu 'Account security' item\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run A: the menu can't open (no hydration). Run B: the menu shows 'Account security' with a lock icon, linking to /account/security (bypass-user-menu.png).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"surface\": \"App shell uses the session user (no PLACEHOLDER_USER)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run B: the server-rendered shell shows avatar initials 'AA' for admin@ (Alice Admin), and the student's dashboard shows the student's data. layout.tsx passes requirePageUser() into AppShell, and PLACEHOLDER_USER no longer exists in shell.tsx. This markup is server-rendered, so the CSP doesn't change it, but reaching it in a real browser still depends on UIV-1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"surface\": \"User menu: name, role badge, initials, Sign out\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"Avatar 'AA' renders server-side. Run A: the menu can't open and Sign out can't be clicked. Run B: the menu shows 'Alice Admin', an 'ADMIN' Chip, Account security and Sign out. Sign out goes to /login, and the session is gone afterwards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"surface\": \"Sidebar navigation filtered by session role\",\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n      \"notes\": \"Run B: ADMIN sees Dashboard, Notifications, Email log, then under Administration, Sections and Courses. STUDENT sees Dashboard, Notifications, My courses. The filtering is server-rendered; the same reachability caveat (UIV-1) applies.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blockedReason\": null\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01N4XyafCqVURGygqgknhBP8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
