{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmDdpNDobLUvtXiTKU9P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MWnHJtgQQKt2g9uxMXCi1S","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/ui-verification/ui-verification-report.md","content":"# UI Verification — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)\n\n- **ticketId:** SH-7\n- **timestamp:** 2026-11-06T06:55:00Z\n- **status:** complete\n- **Result:** 13 PASS · 5 FAIL · 7 BLOCKED (25 UI-facing requirements)\n- **Design reference:** none. There is no `figma-readiness.json`, so every check is against the PRD and `requirements.json` text only.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 report. The old SH-1 screenshots were removed.\n\n## How it was checked\n\n1. **Server.** I ran `next dev -p 3300` against the local Postgres (:5433).\n   - The existing :3000 server was stale (500 on every route) and was started from another checkout, so I left it alone.\n2. **Test data.** The dev database has no courses, sections or periods, so a throwaway Playwright driver (kept outside the repo) created tagged fixtures:\n   - Teacher **Terry Teach**: course teacher and homeroom teacher.\n   - Students **Alex Absent**, **Lee Late** and **Pat Present**.\n   - Parent **Paula**, linked to Alex.\n   - A period running 00:00–23:59, section `uiv-att` with all three students as members, and course **UIV Attendance** with timetable slots every weekday.\n3. **Temporary settings change.** `attendanceMode` was set to `BOTH` for the run, then put back to `PER_PERIOD`.\n4. **Cleanup.** All fixtures were deleted afterwards; I checked that 0 rows remain.\n5. **Viewports:**\n   - 360×740 for the teacher.\n   - 375×667 for the parent.\n   - 1280×800 for the desktop and admin views.\n6. **CSP.** One pass ran with the shipped CSP enforced. All other passes used `bypassCSP: true`, the same as QA and the e2e spec.\n7. **Evidence.** Screenshots are in `screenshots/`. Raw probe output (counts, sizes, statuses) is in `uiv-raw.json`.\n\n## Blocking issues (both existed before SH-7)\n\n**UIV-1: MUI X version skew breaks every DataGrid page.**\n- What's wrong: `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0` imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, but the installed `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0` no longer exports it.\n- What I saw: a \"Failed to compile\" overlay on:\n  - `/students/[id]/attendance`\n  - `/admin/attendance`: all four tabs, because `ReportTab` is a static import.\n  - `/courses/[courseId]/attendance`\n- Side effect: after the first failure, `next dev` returns 500 for every request until it is restarted.\n- Fix: pin x-internals to the 9.5 line, or upgrade all `@mui/x-*` packages together.\n\n**UIV-2: the CSP blocks hydration.**\n- What's wrong: `script-src 'self'` blocks Next's inline scripts.\n- What I saw: with the CSP enforced, the register shows 10 CSP console errors and \"Mark all present\" does nothing (`csp-register-360.png`).\n\n## New defects found in this phase\n\n1. **FR-19 / AC-4: a teacher can't see an old register read-only.**\n   - Expected: AC-4 says a teacher opening a 20-day-old register sees it read-only with an explanation.\n   - Actual: the page shows only a heading and a warning alert. There is no roster and no statuses.\n   - Cause: `canOpen` (the FR-8 window check) refuses the page before `canEdit`'s `readOnly` path can run, so RegisterForm's read-only branch is unreachable for teachers.\n2. **FR-6: the landing page overflows at 360 px.**\n   - The page is 407 px wide, and the \"Register date\" DatePicker runs past the viewport.\n   - Cause: `PageHeader` puts `actions` in a non-wrapping row `Stack` beside the title.\n   - Fix: let the Stack wrap or stack below `sm`, or give the DatePicker a narrower width on mobile.\n3. **FR-14 (minor): one save shows two different times.**\n   - \"Last changed by … at 11:39:36 AM\" uses the browser's timezone (`toLocaleString`).\n   - The landing page (\"Taken 01:39\") and the notification (\"1:39 AM\") use the school timezone.\n\n## Findings\n\n| FR | Surface | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FR-5 | /admin/attendance Settings tab | **FAIL** | The page doesn't compile (UIV-1). `admin-attendance-1280.png` |\n| FR-6 | /attendance/take landing | **FAIL** | Content is correct (meeting, time, Now, Not taken, then \"Taken 01:39 by Terry Teach\" and REVIEW after the save). The page overflows to 407 px at 360 px. `teacher-landing-360.png` |\n| FR-7 | Daily register entry | PASS | \"Daily register – uiv-att · Not taken · TAKE ATTENDANCE\" shows with mode BOTH |\n| FR-8 | Date picker and limits | PASS | Future date is refused with an alert. Teacher at 20 days is refused. Admin opens a 20-day-old date. The picker's 360 px overflow is under FR-6 |\n| FR-9 | Register list | PASS | Sorted by last name. Avatars, P/A/L/E toggles with aria-labels, nothing preselected, theme colours when selected |\n| FR-10 | EXCUSED | PASS | E is disabled for the teacher and enabled for the admin |\n| FR-11 | Mark all present | PASS | It kept Lee's existing Absent, giving Present 2 · Absent 1 |\n| FR-12 | Minutes late and note | PASS | L reveals \"Minutes late\" prefilled with 5. The note icon opens a note field, and the note is still there after saving. The range and length limits were not tested in the UI |\n| FR-13 | Counters and Save state | PASS | Counters update live. Save is disabled at \"3 students not marked\" and enabled at \"Everyone is marked\" |\n| FR-14 | Save and last changed | PASS | \"Attendance saved\" toast and \"Last changed by Terry Teach…\" both show. Minor timezone mismatch (defect 3) |\n| FR-15 | Daily register roster | PASS | All 3 section members are listed |\n| FR-16 | Section register route | PASS | Same component, with the \"Daily register\" breadcrumb and title. Saving was not tested in the UI |\n| FR-17 | Register at 360 px | PASS | No overflow. Rows are 110–158 px tall, toggles are at least 44×49 px, and the save bar is sticky at the bottom |\n| FR-19 | Register past 14 days (teacher) | **FAIL** | An alert only, no read-only register (defect 1). `teacher-register-old-360.png` |\n| FR-21 | Parent absence notification | PASS | \"Alex Absent was marked absent\" shows with an unread badge of 1, at 375 px |\n| FR-24 | Student Attendance tab | **FAIL** | 500 with the compile overlay (UIV-1). `parent-student-attendance-375.png` |\n| FR-25 | Summary cards | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-26 | Month calendar (red day and tooltip) | BLOCKED | UIV-1, so the parent red-day check can't be confirmed |\n| FR-27 | Records table and note visibility | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-29 | Course matrix | **FAIL** | 500 with an import trace through CourseAttendanceMatrix.tsx (run 1, server log) |\n| FR-30 | Admin Today overview | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-31 | Missing registers and Remind | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-32 | Report builder and CSV | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-33 | Below threshold | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-34 | Navigation | PASS | Teacher: Attendance links to /attendance/take. Admin: Attendance links to /admin/attendance in the main group |\n\n## Not covered\n\n- **FR-22** (the corrected notification) has no separate UI surface and was not driven. QA already reported a service-level defect for it.\n- **FR-20 and FR-23** are type registrations with no UI of their own.\n\n## Recommended next steps\n\n1. **Fix UIV-1** (a dependency pin), then re-run this phase so the student tab, course matrix and admin page can be checked visually.\n2. **Fix FR-19:** let teachers *open* out-of-window registers in read-only mode. That means relaxing `canOpen` for reads and keeping `canEdit` for writes.\n3. **Fix the 360 px overflow** on the landing page's PageHeader and DatePicker.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":709,"cache_read_input_tokens":98119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tok