n members are listed |\n| FR-16 | Section register route | PASS | Same component, with the \"Daily register\" breadcrumb and title. Saving was not tested in the UI |\n| FR-17 | Register at 360 px | PASS | No overflow. Rows are 110–158 px tall, toggles are at least 44×49 px, and the save bar is sticky at the bottom |\n| FR-19 | Register past 14 days (teacher) | **FAIL** | An alert only, no read-only register (defect 1). `teacher-register-old-360.png` |\n| FR-21 | Parent absence notification | PASS | \"Alex Absent was marked absent\" shows with an unread badge of 1, at 375 px |\n| FR-24 | Student Attendance tab | **FAIL** | 500 with the compile overlay (UIV-1). `parent-student-attendance-375.png` |\n| FR-25 | Summary cards | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-26 | Month calendar (red day and tooltip) | BLOCKED | UIV-1, so the parent red-day check can't be confirmed |\n| FR-27 | Records table and note visibility | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-29 | Course matrix | **FAIL** | 500 with an import trace through CourseAttendanceMatrix.tsx (run 1, server log) |\n| FR-30 | Admin Today overview | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-31 | Missing registers and Remind | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-32 | Report builder and CSV | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-33 | Below threshold | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |\n| FR-34 | Navigation | PASS | Teacher: Attendance links to /attendance/take. Admin: Attendance links to /admin/attendance in the main group |\n\n## Not covered\n\n- **FR-22** (the corrected notification) has no separate UI surface and was not driven. QA already reported a service-level defect for it.\n- **FR-20 and FR-23** are type registrations with no UI of their own.\n\n## Recommended next steps\n\n1. **Fix UIV-1** (a dependency pin), then re-run this phase so the student tab, course matrix and admin page can be checked visually.\n2. **Fix FR-19:** let teachers *open* out-of-window registers in read-only mode. That means relaxing `canOpen` for reads and keeping `canEdit` for writes.\n3. **Fix the 360 px overflow** on the landing page's PageHeader and DatePicker.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":51,"newStart":1,"newLines":97,"lines":["-# UI Verification — SH-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)","+# UI Verification — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)"," ","-**Status:** complete · **Result:** 3 PASS / 10 FAIL / 0 BLOCKED","+- **ticketId:** SH-7","+- **timestamp:** 2026-11-06T06:55:00Z","+- **status:** complete","+- **Result:** 13 PASS · 5 FAIL · 7 BLOCKED (25 UI-facing requirements)","+- **Design reference:** none. There is no `figma-readiness.json`, so every check is against the PRD and `requirements.json` text only."," ","-## How it was verified","+> This file replaces the stale SH-1 report. The old SH-1 screenshots were removed."," ","-- **App:** `next dev` on :3300 against the local Postgres (:5433, seeded users). Headless Chromium was run twice:","-  - **Run A:** with the app's shipped Content-Security-Policy enforced (the real user experience).","-  - **Run B:** with `bypassCSP: true`, to check the SH-1 code on its own.","-- **Test data:** INVITE and PASSWORD_RESET tokens were created with `createToken()`. Afterwards:","-  - teacher2's password hash and `passwordChangedAt` were restored;","-  - failed-login counters were reset;","-  - the test tokens were marked used.","-- **Design reference:** there is no `figma-readiness.json`, so the checks are against the PRD text only.","-- **Screenshots:** `artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/`. `csp-*` files are from Run A and `bypass-*` files are from Run B.","+## How it was checked"," ","-## Blocking issues","+1. **Server.** I ran `next dev -p 3300` against the local Postgres (:5433).","+   - The existing :3000 server was stale (500 on every route) and was started from another checkout, so I left it alone.","+2. **Test data.** The dev database has no courses, sections or periods, so a throwaway Playwright driver (kept outside the repo) created tagged fixtures:","+   - Teacher **Terry Teach**: course teacher and homeroom teacher.","+   - Students **Alex Absent**, **Lee Late** and **Pat Present**.","+   - Parent **Paula**, linked to Alex.","+   - A period running 00:00–23:59, section `uiv-att` with all three students as members, and course **UIV Attendance** with timetable slots every weekday.","+3. **Temporary settings change.** `attendanceMode` was set to `BOTH` for the run, then put back to `PER_PERIOD`.","+4. **Cleanup.** All fixtures were deleted afterwards; I checked that 0 rows remain.","+5. **Viewports:**","+   - 360×740 for the teacher.","+   - 375×667 for the parent.","+   - 1280×800 for the desktop and admin views.","+6. **CSP.** One pass ran with the shipped CSP enforced. All other passes used `bypassCSP: true`, the same as QA and the e2e spec.","+7. **Evidence.** Screenshots are in `screenshots/`. Raw probe output (counts, sizes, statuses) is in `uiv-raw.json`."," ","-1. **UIV-1 · BLOCKER: the shipped CSP stops hydration.**","-   - `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, and Chromium blocks Next's inline scripts.","-   - Every page server-renders correctly but stays non-interactive. Sign-in, the password toggle, the checklist, the user menu and every form submit do nothing.","-   - This was already present before SH-1, and QA reported it too; it is confirmed here independently.","-   - **Fix:** a nonce-based CSP set in middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts (plus `'unsafe-eval'` in dev only).","-2. **UIV-2 · HIGH: passwords leak into the URL before hydration.**","-   - The forms have no `method=\"post\"`, so an unhydrated submit becomes a native GET.","-   - Run A produced `/reset-password/<token>?password=LeakCheck2026z&confirm=LeakCheck2026z`, and the dev server's access log recorded the same query string.","-   - **Fix:** add `method=\"post\"` to LoginForm, ForgotPasswordForm, SetPasswordForm/TokenPasswordForm and ChangePasswordForm.","+## Blocking issues (both existed before SH-7)"," ","-With CSP bypassed (Run B), every SH-1 surface behaves as the PRD describes. Fixing UIV-1 and UIV-2 should turn most FAILs below into PASS.","+**UIV-1: MUI X version skew breaks every DataGrid page.**","+- What's wrong: `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0` imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, but the installed `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0` no longer exports it.","+- What I saw: a \"Failed to compile\" overlay on:","+  - `/students/[id]/attendance`","+  - `/admin/attendance`: all four tabs, because `ReportTab` is a static import.","+  - `/courses/[courseId]/attendance`","+- Side effect: after the first failure, `next dev` returns 500 for every request until it is restarted.","+- Fix: pin x-internals to the 9.5 line, or upgrade all `@mui/x-*` packages together."," ","+**UIV-2: the CSP blocks hydration.**","+- What's wrong: `script-src 'self'` blocks Next's inline scripts.","+- What I saw: with the CSP enforced, the register shows 10 CSP console errors and \"Mark all present\" does nothing (`csp-register-360.png`).","+","+## New defects found in this phase","+","+1. **FR-19 / AC-4: a teacher can't see an old register read-only.**","+   - Expected: AC-4 says a teacher opening a 20-day-old register sees it read-only with an explanation.","+   - Actual: the page shows only a heading and a warning alert. There is no roster and no statuses.","+   - Cause: `canOpen` (the FR-8 window check) refuses the page before `canEdit`'s `readOnly` path can run, so RegisterForm's read-only branch is unreachable for teachers.","+2. **FR-6: the landing page overflows at 360 px.**","+   - The page is 407 px wide, and the \"Register date\" DatePicker runs past the viewport.","+   - Cause: `PageHeader` puts `actions` in a non-wrapping row `Stack` beside the title.","+   - Fix: let the Stack wrap or stack below `sm`, or give the DatePicker a narrower width on mobile.","+3. **FR-14 (minor): one save shows two different times.**","+   - \"Last changed by … at 11:39:36 AM\" uses the browser's timezone (`toLocaleString`).","+   - The landing page (\"Taken 01:39\") and the notification (\"1:39 AM\") use the school timezone.","+"," ## Findings"," ","-| Req | Surface | Verdict | Notes |","+| FR | Surface | Verdict | Notes |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| FR-2 | `/login` | FAIL | Renders correctly: Card, fields, eye toggle, Sign in button, \"Forgot your password?\" link. It does not hydrate in Run A. In Run B the toggle and sign-in work. |","-| FR-4 | `/login` error Alert | FAIL | Run A shows no Alert. Run B shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" Locked and disabled messages were not exercised. |","-| FR-7 | callbackUrl redirect | FAIL | Users can't sign in in Run A. In Run B, an external callbackUrl goes to `/dashboard` and `/account/security` is honoured. |","-| FR-11 | middleware redirect | **PASS** | `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard` with CSP enforced. This is server-side. |","-| FR-13 | `/invite/[token]` | FAIL | The invalid and valid states render correctly: exact invalid-link copy, read-only name and email, checklist, Activate account. Accepting is impossible in Run A, and a submit would leak the password (UIV-2). Accepting was not exercised in Run B, to avoid activating the seeded invite user. |","-| FR-16 | PasswordChecklist | FAIL | Present on the invite, reset and security pages with all 4 rules. It is static in Run A. In Run B it updates live: for \"abc1\", letter, number and not-email are met and length is unmet. |","-| FR-17 | `/forgot-password` | FAIL | Renders correctly. In Run B, an unknown email shows the message that doesn't reveal whether the account exists. In Run A, submit does nothing. |","-| FR-19 | `/reset-password/[token]` | FAIL | The invalid state shows the copy plus a \"Request a new reset link\" link. Run A: the password leaked into the URL and the log, and no reset happened. Run B: redirect to `/login?reset=1` and the toast \"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\" Minor: a dev-only hydration warning appears on this page. |","-| FR-20 | `/account/security` | FAIL | Not reachable through the UI in Run A. In Run B the fields, toggles and checklist render, and a wrong current password shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" The successful change was not exercised. |","-| FR-21 | Menu \"Account security\" | FAIL | The menu can't open in Run A. In Run B the item is present with a lock icon and links correctly. |","-| FR-25 | Shell uses the session user | **PASS** | Server-rendered initials \"AA\" for Alice Admin. PLACEHOLDER_USER is gone. |","-| FR-26 | User menu name/badge/sign out | FAIL | The avatar renders, but the menu can't open in Run A. In Run B it shows \"Alice Admin\", an ADMIN chip and Sign out, and Sign out goes to `/login` with the session cleared. |","-| FR-27 | Role-filtered sidebar | **PASS** | ADMIN sees Dashboard, Notifications, Email log, Sections, Courses. STUDENT sees Dashboard, Notifications, My courses. |","+| FR-5 | /admin/attendance Settings tab | **FAIL** | The page doesn't compile (UIV-1). `admin-attendance-1280.png` |","+| FR-6 | /attendance/take landing | **FAIL** | Content is correct (meeting, time, Now, Not taken, then \"Taken 01:39 by Terry Teach\" and REVIEW after the save). The page overflows to 407 px at 360 px. `teacher-landing-360.png` |","+| FR-7 | Daily register entry | PASS | \"Daily register – uiv-att · Not taken · TAKE ATTENDANCE\" shows with mode BOTH |","+| FR-8 | Date picker and limits | PASS | Future date is refused with an alert. Teacher at 20 days is refused. Admin opens a 20-day-old date. The picker's 360 px overflow is under FR-6 |","+| FR-9 | Register list | PASS | Sorted by last name. Avatars, P/A/L/E toggles with aria-labels, nothing preselected, theme colours when selected |","+| FR-10 | EXCUSED | PASS | E is disabled for the teacher and enabled for the admin |","+| FR-11 | Mark all present | PASS | It kept Lee's existing Absent, giving Present 2 · Absent 1 |","+| FR-12 | Minutes late and note | PASS | L reveals \"Minutes late\" prefilled with 5. The note icon opens a note field, and the note is still there after saving. The range and length limits were not tested in the UI |","+| FR-13 | Counters and Save state | PASS | Counters update live. Save is disabled at \"3 students not marked\" and enabled at \"Everyone is marked\" |","+| FR-14 | Save and last changed | PASS | \"Attendance saved\" toast and \"Last changed by Terry Teach…\" both show. Minor timezone mismatch (defect 3) |","+| FR-15 | Daily register roster | PASS | All 3 section members are listed |","+| FR-16 | Section register route | PASS | Same component, with the \"Daily register\" breadcrumb and title. Saving was not tested in the UI |","+| FR-17 | Register at 360 px | PASS | No overflow. Rows are 110–158 px tall, toggles are at least 44×49 px, and the save bar is sticky at the bottom |","+| FR-19 | Register past 14 days (teacher) | **FAIL** | An alert only, no read-only register (defect 1). `teacher-register-old-360.png` |","+| FR-21 | Parent absence notification | PASS | \"Alex Absent was marked absent\" shows with an unread badge of 1, at 375 px |","+| FR-24 | Student Attendance tab | **FAIL** | 500 with the compile overlay (UIV-1). `parent-student-attendance-375.png` |","+| FR-25 | Summary cards | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |","+| FR-26 | Month calendar (red day and tooltip) | BLOCKED | UIV-1, so the parent red-day check can't be confirmed |","+| FR-27 | Records table and note visibility | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |","+| FR-29 | Course matrix | **FAIL** | 500 with an import trace through CourseAttendanceMatrix.tsx (run 1, server log) |","+| FR-30 | Admin Today overview | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |","+| FR-31 | Missing registers and Remind | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |","+| FR-32 | Report builder and CSV | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |","+| FR-33 | Below threshold | BLOCKED | UIV-1 |","+| FR-34 | Navigation | PASS | Teacher: Attendance links to /attendance/take. Admin: Attendance links to /admin/attendance in the main group |"," ","-## Side effects to know about","+## Not covered"," ","-- Creating a test INVITE token for `invited@schoolhub.test` invalidated the invite link the seed logged earlier. Re-run `npm run db:seed` to get a fresh link.","+- **FR-22** (the corrected notification) has no separate UI surface and was not driven. QA already reported a service-level defect for it.","+- **FR-20 and FR-23** are type registrations with no UI of their own.","+","+## Recommended next steps","+","+1. **Fix UIV-1** (a dependency pin), then re-run this phase so the student tab, course matrix and admin page can be checked visually.","+2. **Fix FR-19:** let teachers *open* out-of-window registers in read-only mode. That means relaxing `canOpen` for reads and keeping `canEdit` for writes.","+3. **Fix the 360 px overflow** on the landing page's PageHeader and DatePicker."]}],"originalFile":"# UI Verification — SH-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n**Status:** complete · **Result:** 3 PASS / 10 FAIL / 0 BLOCKED\n\n## How it was verified\n\n- **App:** `next dev` on :3300 against the local Postgres (:5433, seeded users). Headless Chromium was run twice:\n  - **Run A:** with the app's shipped Content-Security-Policy enforced (the real user experience).\n  - **Run B:** with `bypassCSP: true`, to check the SH-1 code on its own.\n- **Test data:** INVITE and PASSWORD_RESET tokens were created with `createToken()`. Afterwards:\n  - teacher2's password hash and `passwordChangedAt` were restored;\n  - failed-login counters were reset;\n  - the test tokens were marked used.\n- **Design reference:** there is no `figma-readiness.json`, so the checks are against the PRD text only.\n- **Screenshots:** `artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots/`. `csp-*` files are from Run A and `bypass-*` files are from Run B.\n\n## Blocking issues\n\n1. **UIV-1 · BLOCKER: the shipped CSP stops hydration.**\n   - `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, and Chromium blocks Next's inline scripts.\n   - Every page server-renders correctly but stays non-interactive. Sign-in, the password toggle, the checklist, the user menu and every form submit do nothing.\n   - This was already present before SH-1, and QA reported it too; it is confirmed here independently.\n   - **Fix:** a nonce-based CSP set in middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts (plus `'unsafe-eval'` in dev only).\n2. **UIV-2 · HIGH: passwords leak into the URL before hydration.**\n   - The forms have no `method=\"post\"`, so an unhydrated submit becomes a native GET.\n   - Run A produced `/reset-password/<token>?password=LeakCheck2026z&confirm=LeakCheck2026z`, and the dev server's access log recorded the same query string.\n   - **Fix:** add `method=\"post\"` to LoginForm, ForgotPasswordForm, SetPasswordForm/TokenPasswordForm and ChangePasswordForm.\n\nWith CSP bypassed (Run B), every SH-1 surface behaves as the PRD describes. Fixing UIV-1 and UIV-2 should turn most FAILs below into PASS.\n\n## Findings\n\n| Req | Surface | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FR-2 | `/login` | FAIL | Renders correctly: Card, fields, eye toggle, Sign in button, \"Forgot your password?\" link. It does not hydrate in Run A. In Run B the toggle and sign-in work. |\n| FR-4 | `/login` error Alert | FAIL | Run A shows no Alert. Run B shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" Locked and disabled messages were not exercised. |\n| FR-7 | callbackUrl redirect | FAIL | Users can't sign in in Run A. In Run B, an external callbackUrl goes to `/dashboard` and `/account/security` is honoured. |\n| FR-11 | middleware redirect | **PASS** | `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard` with CSP enforced. This is server-side. |\n| FR-13 | `/invite/[token]` | FAIL | The invalid and valid states render correctly: exact invalid-link copy, read-only name and email, checklist, Activate account. Accepting is impossible in Run A, and a submit would leak the password (UIV-2). Accepting was not exercised in Run B, to avoid activating the seeded invite user. |\n| FR-16 | PasswordChecklist | FAIL | Present on the invite, reset and security pages with all 4 rules. It is static in Run A. In Run B it updates live: for \"abc1\", letter, number and not-email are met and length is unmet. |\n| FR-17 | `/forgot-password` | FAIL | Renders correctly. In Run B, an unknown email shows the message that doesn't reveal whether the account exists. In Run A, submit does nothing. |\n| FR-19 | `/reset-password/[token]` | FAIL | The invalid state shows the copy plus a \"Request a new reset link\" link. Run A: the password leaked into the URL and the log, and no reset happened. Run B: redirect to `/login?reset=1` and the toast \"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\" Minor: a dev-only hydration warning appears on this page. |\n| FR-20 | `/account/security` | FAIL | Not reachable through the UI in Run A. In Run B the fields, toggles and checklist render, and a wrong current password shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" The successful change was not exercised. |\n| FR-21 | Menu \"Account security\" | FAIL | The menu can't open in Run A. In Run B the item is present with a lock icon and links correctly. |\n| FR-25 | Shell uses the session user | **PASS** | Server-rendered initials \"AA\" for Alice Admin. PLACEHOLDER_USER is gone. |\n| FR-26 | User menu name/badge/sign out | FAIL | The avatar renders, but the menu can't open in Run A. In Run B it shows \"Alice Admin\", an ADMIN chip and Sign out, and Sign out goes to `/login` with the session cleared. |\n| FR-27 | Role-filtered sidebar | **PASS** | ADMIN sees Dashboard, Notifications, Email log, Sections, Courses. STUDENT sees Dashboard, Notifications, My courses. |\n\n## Side effects to know about\n\n- Creating a test INVITE token for `invited@schoolhub.test` invalidated the invite link the seed logged earlier. Re-run `npm run db:seed` to get a fresh link.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MWnHJtgQQKt2g9uxMXCi1S","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
