{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmDfifEdSHbi2LktogBE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran the SH-7 UI verification. **Result: 13 PASS, 5 FAIL, 7 BLOCKED** across 25 UI-facing requirements. Every page that uses a data table (DataGrid) fails to build, so about a third of the feature couldn't be checked at all.\n\nThe teacher register itself works, tested at phone (360 px) and desktop width: marking, the \"Mark all present\" button, the live counters, saving, and the 48 px rows and 44 px buttons the PRD asks for. The parent saw the absence notification.\n\n**Blocking issues (both existed before SH-7):**\n- **Data-table pages don't build.** A version mismatch between two MUI X packages breaks every page that contains a data table, including the student Attendance tab, the course attendance matrix, and the whole `/admin/attendance` page. All four admin tabs go with it, including Settings. Pinning the MUI X packages to matching versions should fix it.\n- **Security headers stop the app working in a real browser.** With the shipped Content-Security-Policy enforced, no button does anything. All my other checks bypassed it, the same way QA and the e2e tests do.\n\n**New defects from this phase:**\n1. **FR-19 (FAIL):** a teacher opening a 20-day-old register sees only a warning message, not the register in read-only form. The PRD's acceptance criterion AC-4 requires the read-only register. The 14-day date check rejects the page before the read-only view can load, so teachers never reach it.\n2. **FR-6 (FAIL):** at 360 px the \"Take attendance\" landing page is 407 px wide because the date picker runs off the right edge. The shared page header puts its controls in a row that never wraps.\n3. **FR-14 (minor):** a single save shows two different times. \"Last changed by\" uses the browser's timezone; the landing page and the notification use the school's (New York).\n\n**How I ran it:**\n- The existing server on port 3000 belongs to another checkout and returns errors on every page, so I left it alone and started my own on port 3300. I stopped mine afterwards.\n- The dev database has no courses, sections or periods, so a throwaway script outside the repo created tagged test users and classes.\n- I temporarily switched the attendance mode setting to cover both modes, then restored it. All test data was deleted afterwards and I confirmed none remains.\n- I deleted the old screenshots from the earlier SH-1 run and replaced both report files.\n\nFixing the package mismatch and re-running this phase is what will unblock the 7 BLOCKED items and the remaining data-table failures (FR-5, FR-24, FR-29).\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/ui-verification/`:\n- ui-verification-report.json\n- ui-verification-report.md\n- uiv-raw.json\n- screenshots/"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3257,"cache_read_input_tokens":98828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3257},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0d33c40-44ea-44a6-8793-0fcbf67c071f","uuid":"d6643f81-8790-48b4-92e0-11bd4f08c134","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:42:18.899Z","request_id":"req_011CgmDfiR6yk6gwU1t2sxmQ"}
