{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fqq1KGFrffaiNpvRSENxFs","type":"tool_result","content":"handoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\ndict_keys(['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prd', 'runMode', 'brownfieldFindings', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'status'])\n{\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId\\u2192User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 File storage (Prisma block)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.1\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; Acceptance Criterion 4\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2 (inferred: file-type cannot detect txt/csv; OOXML sniffs as zip container)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.3\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; Acceptance Criterion 3\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.5\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Content data model\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title \\u2264120, lesson title \\u2264150, contentMarkdown \\u2264100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1\\u2013600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 field comments; Code layout (validators)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1 (contextId 'id of the owning record once attached'); FR-5.2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table; Acceptance Criterion 7\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; NFR Accessibility\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; Acceptance Criterion 1\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4; API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Parents can view a course's Content tab only when a linked student is ACTIVE-enrolled. The existing assertCanViewCourse already enforces this (verified in src/server/auth/course-access.ts PARENT branch), so reuse it as is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Roles (parents see data for linked students)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (storage of the URL in logoUrl inferred; existing column reused, no rename)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"/admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (references a page from PRD-02 not found in src/app/(app)/admin/)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Code layout (response shape)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"API table ('view (visibility rules)'); FR-3.1\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod \\u2192 service \\u2192 JSON).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (feature-named subdirectory precedent)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-46\", \"description\": \"Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (AuditLog rule)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-47\", \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules \\u00d7 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-48\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload \\u2192 attach \\u2192 download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4236bb9b-3e91-459f-a600-1de35f9962e2","uuid":"3ede6256-1bde-48cd-a215-b1e8423d3494","timestamp":"2026-11-07T04:07:44.603Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"handoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\ndict_keys(['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prd', 'runMode', 'brownfieldFindings', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'status'])\n{\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId\\u2192User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 File storage (Prisma block)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.1\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; Acceptance Criterion 4\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2 (inferred: file-type cannot detect txt/csv; OOXML sniffs as zip container)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.3\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; Acceptance Criterion 3\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.5\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Content data model\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title \\u2264120, lesson title \\u2264150, contentMarkdown \\u2264100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1\\u2013600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 field comments; Code layout (validators)\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1 (contextId 'id of the owning record once attached'); FR-5.2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for