missing in a production install. ADR-1 (no new dependencies) holds. Values go to Prisma as 2 dp strings, so the two Decimal classes never mix.\n3. **Decimal serialization:** done in explicit typed mappers (`serializeDecimal` helper → `\"14.40\"`), not a generic walker. Same output as D5.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"completed\": [\n    \"TASK-1\",\n    \"TASK-2\",\n    \"TASK-3\",\n    \"TASK-4\",\n    \"TASK-5\",\n    \"TASK-6\",\n    \"TASK-7\",\n    \"TASK-8\",\n    \"TASK-9\",\n    \"TASK-10\",\n    \"TASK-11\",\n    \"TASK-12\",\n    \"TASK-13\",\n    \"TASK-14\",\n    \"TASK-15\",\n    \"TASK-16\",\n    \"TASK-17\",\n    \"TASK-18\",\n    \"TASK-19\",\n    \"TASK-20\",\n    \"TASK-21\",\n    \"TASK-22\",\n    \"TASK-23\",\n    \"TASK-24\",\n    \"TASK-25\",\n    \"TASK-26\"\n  ]\n}\n# QA Report — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-9\n- timestamp: 2026-11-09T06:10:50Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 78\n- requirementsPassed: 76\n- requirementsFailed: 2\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-8 QA report. All 61 functional requirements PASS. The 2 failures are non-functional:\n> **NFR-12** is a small fix (3 `console.log` lines in the seed). **NFR-13** fails because `npm run test` is not fully green. All 6 failing tests are outside SH-9 and existed before it.\n> The feature is complete and works end to end. It is ready for review once NFR-12 is fixed and the NFR-13 failures are accepted as known or fixed separately.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n### 1. The build and test suite run, and the feature works end to end\n- `tsc --noEmit` is clean and `npm run lint` is clean.\n- All 57 SH-9 tests are green (29 unit, 23 integration against a real Postgres on :5433, 5 Playwright e2e against `next start -p 3100`).\n- QA added `tests/integration/assignments/qa-sh9.test.ts` (9 tests). It covers what Dev's tests did not: scheduling and visibility, publish-once, delete vs archive, duplicate, privacy and access control, the roster, \"To grade\", and editing max points.\n- All 9 pass. QA found no functional defects.\n- Dev's self-report checked out. All 55 `file-ownership-matrix.json` paths are present (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` was deleted as planned). A grep found no TODO, FIXME or stub implementations in the SH-9 files.\n\n### 2. NFR-13: `npm run test` is not fully green, and the cause is outside SH-9\nThe full suite passed 306 of 312 tests on the first run. The 6 failures:\n\n| Test | Failure | Why it is not SH-9 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `attendance-qa.test.ts` FR-22 | expected 2 absence notifications to be 1 | `attendance-service.ts` was last changed Nov 6, before SH-9. SH-9 only added entries to `notifications/types.ts`. |\n| `attendance-qa.test.ts` FR-10/FR-19 | `FORBIDDEN` vs `OK` | Depends on the time of day (the attendance edit window). Not SH-9 code. |\n| `attendance-qa.test.ts` NFR-1 perf | timing | Flaky: it passed on the rerun. |\n| `auth.test.ts` rate limit | — | Flaky: it passed on the rerun. |\n| `auth-forms.test.tsx`, `useToast.test.tsx` | focus and timer assertions | Do not import SH-9 code. |\n| `lockout.test.ts` | next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM | Environment problem. Not SH-9 code. |\n\n- The repo has no git baseline: the git root is `$HOME` and the whole project is untracked. Before SH-9, `vitest.config.ts` could not load at all.\n- So QA cannot prove these failures existed before SH-9. The evidence above (file dates, imports, flakiness) points that way.\n- Strictly, NFR-13 (\"npm run test keeps passing\") is **not met**. It needs a separate fix outside this ticket.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TczMwtajxuD5rN5cmg7a1a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
