.get('files') or t.get('filePaths'), t.get('requirementIds') or t.get('requirements'))\n\"","description":"Summarize requirements and plan tasks"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01P5hBVrarqKAJmXm9wcxghM":{"cwd":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P5hBVrarqKAJmXm9wcxghM","type":"tool_result","content":"dict_keys(['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prdTitle', 'prdTicketRef', 'runMode', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'brownfieldFindings', 'status', 'confidenceMethod'])\nfunctionalRequirements FR-1 | Add the Prisma enums SubmissionType (ONLINE_TEXT, FILE_UPLOAD, TEXT_AND_FILE, NO_SUBMISSION), AssignmentStatus (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and SubmissionStatus (SUBMITTED, RETURNED) in a new prisma migrate migration.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-2 | Add an Assignment model with the fields listed in FR-1. Also add allowExtraCredit Boolean @default(false) (from FR-5.6), notifiedAt DateTime? (from FR-7.1) and archivedAt DateTime? (from the API table). Add a Course→Assignment rel\nfunctionalRequirements FR-3 | Add the models AssignmentAttachment (assignment↔FileObject), Rubric and RubricCriterion. RubricCriterion has title, description?, maxPoints Decimal(6,2), order, and levels Json [{label, points, description}].\nfunctionalRequirements FR-4 | Add the models Submission (@@unique([assignmentId, studentId]), with Decimal rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore and Json rubricScores [{criterionId, points, comment}]), SubmissionFile (submission↔FileObject) and SubmissionHistory \nfunctionalRequirements FR-5 | Add a GradeExemption model with a composite id (assignmentId, studentId), an optional reason and createdAt.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-6 | Add an AssignmentReminder table {assignmentId, studentId, kind} with a unique key on all three columns. It makes the due_soon and missing reminders idempotent.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-7 | Enforce the field limits in Zod schemas in src/lib/validators/assignments.ts, shared by forms and handlers: title ≤150; instructions ≤50,000; maxPoints 0–1000; lateCutoffAt > dueAt; latePenaltyPercentPerDay and maxLatePenaltyPerce\nfunctionalRequirements FR-8 | A teacher can record a grade for a student who did not submit. The service creates a Submission with text = null, no files, submittedAt = gradedAt and attemptNumber = 0 (the offline/no-submission marker).\nfunctionalRequirements FR-9 | Build the create/edit page at /courses/[courseId]/assignments/new. Fields: title, Markdown instructions (the PRD-08 editor), attachments (FileUpload, context 'assignment'), submission type, max points, due date-time (school timezo\nfunctionalRequirements FR-10 | Default the due date-time to the next teaching day at 23:59 in the school timezone. 'Teaching day' is taken from the existing SchoolDay.isTeaching weekday table, because holidays are not modelled before PRD-14.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-11 | Rubric builder: add, reorder and remove criteria (title, description, levels with label + points + description). The sum of the criterion maximums must equal max points. Otherwise show the inline error 'Rubric totals {sum} points \nfunctionalRequirements FR-12 | Offer 'Save draft' (DRAFT), 'Publish' (PUBLISHED) and 'Schedule' (SCHEDULED). Schedule requires an available-from in the future, and the assignment stays hidden from students and parents until then.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-13 | A SCHEDULED assignment counts as visible once availableFrom ≤ server now. Visibility is computed at read time. No background job rewrites the status to PUBLISHED.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-14 | Editing the due date or max points of a published assignment that has submissions shows a warning. Changing max points recalculates nothing: existing scores are kept, and a banner prompts the teacher to review grades.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-15 | A 'Duplicate to other courses' action copies the assignment as DRAFT to selected courses the teacher manages (POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}). The copy keeps the instructions, attachments, settings and rubric. The\nfunctionalRequirements FR-16 | Register an 'Assignments' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts for all roles that can view the course.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-17 | Teacher/admin view of the course Assignments tab: a table with title, due date, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted and a 'Grade' button.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-18 | Student view of the course Assignments tab: a list grouped as Upcoming, Past due (missing), Submitted and Returned. Parents see the same view, read-only, for their linked child.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-19 | The assignment page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId] shows the instructions (sanitised Markdown), attachments, due date, late policy summary, rubric (if any) and the submission panel. When under 48 hours remain, it a\nfunctionalRequirements FR-20 | The submission panel shows a Markdown text editor and/or file upload, depending on submissionType (NO_SUBMISSION shows neither). File upload respects maxFileCount. Draft text autosaves to localStorage only, never to the server.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-21 | Clicking Submit opens a confirmation Dialog before the POST.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-22 | Server submission rules: the assignment is visible; the student is ACTIVE-enrolled in the course; the student is not exempt. If now > dueAt, allowLate must be true and now ≤ lateCutoffAt (when set). Otherwise return VALIDATION_ERR\nfunctionalRequirements FR-23 | On submit, compute isLate = submittedAt > dueAt and lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h), using server time. For example, due Mon 23:59 and submitted Wed 10:00 gives lateDays = 2.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-24 | Resubmission is allowed until dueAt (or lateCutoffAt / indefinitely when late is allowed) and only while status = SUBMITTED. It copies the previous attempt into SubmissionHistory, increments attemptNumber, and clears rawScore, pen\nfunctionalRequirements FR-25 | After submitting, the student sees a receipt such as 'Submitted Mon 14 Sep 2026, 21:04 (attempt 2)', in the school timezone, plus the files and text submitted.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-26 | After return, the student sees the final score, rubric breakdown, feedback and the late penalty applied.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-27 | Until the work is returned, the student and parent see 'Submitted — awaiting grading'. No score, rubric scores or feedback are sent in the API response.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-28 | Grading page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade, left panel: an MUI List of all enrolled students with status Chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter, and sorting by name\nfunctionalRequirements FR-29 | Grading main panel: the selected submission's text as sanitised Markdown, and its files listed with inline preview for images and PDFs (<img>/<iframe> to /api/files/:id?inline=1, which already exists). Previous attempts (Submissio\nfunctionalRequirements FR-30 | Grading form. With a rubric, each criterion is an exclusive ToggleButtonGroup of levels, and the selected points auto-sum into the raw score (for example 8 + 9 → 17). Without a rubric, the raw score is entered directly. The late p\nfunctionalRequirements FR-31 | finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100), rounded half-up to 2 dp. For example, raw 18 with 20 % → 14.40. It is computed server-side at grading time.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-32 | Grading buttons: 'Save' (graded, not visible to the student), 'Save & return' (returns this submission and sets returnedAt) and the bulk 'Return all graded' (POST /api/assignments/:id/return; submissionIds optional, defaults to al\nfunctionalRequirements FR-33 | Keyboard shortcuts on the grading screen: J = next student, K = previous student, Ctrl+Enter = save and go to the next student. The shortcuts are not captured while typing in text fields, except Ctrl+Enter.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-34 | 'Grade without submission' for students who did not submit (POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}). It creates the attemptNumber = 0 Submission described in FR-8.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-35 | An 'Exempt' toggle (PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId) writes or deletes a GradeExemption. Exempt students are removed from missing counts and lists, get no due_soon or missing reminders, cannot submit, and are\nfunctionalRequirements FR-36 | Validate scores server-side: rawScore and the rubric points must be within 0..maxPoints. When allowExtraCredit is true, rawScore may go up to 120 % of maxPoints. penaltyPercent must be 0–100.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-37 | Build the /assignments page for STUDENT. It lists every assignment across the student's ACTIVE enrollments in four tabs: Upcoming (sorted by due date), Missing (past due, not submitted, not exempt), Submitted and Returned. There i\nfunctionalRequirements FR-38 | The /assignments page for PARENT has a child selector (linked students only) and shows the same content as the student view, read-only.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-39 | The /assignments page for TEACHER is a 'To grade' list of submitted, ungraded submissions across the courses they teach (teacherId or coTeacherIds), oldest first.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-40 | Add an 'Assignments' nav entry for /assignments to src/config/navigation.ts for STUDENT, PARENT and TEACHER.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-41 | Register an 'Assignments' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts. It shows the same per-student data to teachers and admins who view the student (GET /api/students/:id/assignments).\nfunctionalRequirements FR-42 | Register and send assignment.published to ACTIVE-enrolled students (in-app; email default false). It is sent on publish, or for SCHEDULED assignments on the first student list load after availableFrom. It is sent exactly once, usi\nfunctionalRequirements FR-43 | Register and send assignment.due_soon to students with no submission (and not exempt) once dueAt − 24 h has passed and before dueAt. sendDueReminders() runs on every PRD-04 maintenance dispatcher call (src/app/api/internal/email/d\nfunctionalRequirements FR-44 | Register and send assignment.returned to the student and their parents through the existing notifyStudentAndParents(). The body includes course, title and score, for example 'Mathematics: Fractions worksheet — 18/20'.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-45 | Register and send assignment.missing to parents only (email default true), once per student, 24 hours after dueAt if the student has still not submitted and is not exempt. It is idempotent via AssignmentReminder (kind 'missing') a\nfunctionalRequirements FR-46 | Add the four notification types to NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts with the category ACADEMIC and the role lists that match their recipients.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-47 | Register two file access contexts in src/server/files/contexts.ts: 'assignment' (anyone who can view the assignment, with visibility rules applied) and 'submission' (the submitting student, their linked parents, course managers an\nfunctionalRequirements FR-48 | GET /api/courses/:id/assignments (view course) returns a role-shaped list. Managers get every status with counts. Students and parents get only visible, non-archived assignments, with their own submission state.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-49 | POST /api/courses/:id/assignments (manage course) creates an assignment with its rubric and attachments.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-50 | GET /api/assignments/:id (view). For students and parents the response includes their own submission, with grading fields only once returned.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-51 | PATCH /api/assignments/:id (manage). DELETE /api/assignments/:id (manage) hard-deletes only when there are no submissions. Otherwise it sets archivedAt.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-52 | Archived assignments are hidden from student and parent lists, /assignments, reminders and new submissions. Managers can still see them.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-53 | POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions (STUDENT) {text?, fileIds[]} applies the FR-22 to FR-24 rules. The fileIds must be the student's own uploads with context 'submission', and their number must be ≤ maxFileCount.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-54 | GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions (manage) lists every enrolled student, including those who have not submitted, with their status, exemption and submission summary.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-55 | GET /api/submissions/:id is open to the submitting student, their parents and course managers. SubmissionHistory is included only for managers.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-56 | PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade (manage) {rawScore, penaltyPercent, feedback, rubricScores} sets gradedById/gradedAt and the computed finalScore.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-57 | GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab= (any role) returns the role-shaped data for /assignments. studentId is accepted for parents (it must be a linked child).\nfunctionalRequirements FR-58 | GET /api/students/:id/assignments (view student; uses the existing assertCanViewStudent) returns the per-student assignment list.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-59 | Grading, returning, exempting and offline grading change records owned by a student, so each writes an AuditLog row through the existing audit().\nfunctionalRequirements FR-60 | Assignments with submissionType NO_SUBMISSION are not counted as Missing and trigger no due_soon or missing reminders. They are graded offline only.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-61 | Seed data: MATH-7A gets 4 assignments (one returned with all students graded at 55–100 %; one submitted and awaiting grading with 60 % submitted and 2 late; one due in 2 days; one draft). ENG-7A gets 2 (one with a 3-criterion rubr\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-1 | Correctness: all score arithmetic uses Decimal end to end (Prisma.Decimal / decimal.js, which ships with Prisma), never JS floating point. Final scores round half-up to 2 dp.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-2 | Integrity: submission, deadline, late-day, visibility and reminder checks use server time only. Client timestamps are never trusted.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-3 | Performance: the grading screen switches between students in under 300 ms by prefetching the next and previous submissions.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-4 | Privacy: students never see other students' submissions, scores or files, in the API or through the file URLs.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-5 | Access control is enforced server-side on every handler and server page through requireUser/requireRole and the existing assertCanViewCourse, assertCanManageCourse and assertCanViewStudent. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-6 | UI component rule: Material UI v9.5.0 and MUI X only, styled through the theme, sx and styled(). No banned libraries, enforced by the ESLint no-restricted-imports rule. Every component (List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs,\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-7 | API conventions: route handlers are thin (Zod → service → JSON). They use the {data} / list {data,page,pageSize,total} / {error:{code,message,details}} envelopes and the standard error codes. Pagination defaults to 20 (max 100), w\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-8 | Code layout: business logic goes in src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts (the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent). Zod schemas go in src/lib/validators/assignments.ts. Routes go under src/app/api/{courses,assignments,s\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-9 | Time handling: timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The late-day calculation is correct across a DST change in the school timezone and on the exact 24 h boundary (exactly 24 h late = 1 day).\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-10 | Markdown (instructions, submission text, feedback) is rendered with react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with every element mapped to an MUI component.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-11 | Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold, rename existing routes or models, or duplicate existing helpers. Reuse notify(), notifyStudentAndParents(), audit(), registerFileAccess/contexts, the files service and /api/files, the DataTable\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-12 | Committed code has no console.log. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-13 | Quality gate: npm run lint, npm run typecheck and npm run test keep passing.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-14 | Unit tests cover: the late-days calculation (exact 24 h boundary, DST change), the penalty cap, final-score rounding and rubric-sum validation. Integration tests cover: resubmission history, the return flow, reminder idempotency a\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-15 | Scope guard: no plagiarism detection, peer review, group assignments, inline document annotation, or gradebook weighting / term grades (PRD-11 consumes these scores). Do not change behaviour owned by later PRDs.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-16 | Usability goals: a teacher can create and publish an assignment in under 2 minutes, and can grade 30 submissions with the keyboard without leaving the grading screen.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-17 | English-only UI, single school, support for evergreen browsers (last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari), and basic accessibility (labelled inputs, keyboard-operable controls).\nclarificationLog None | \nclarificationLog None | \nTASK-1 None ['package.json', 'package-lock.json', 'vitest.config.ts', 'vitest.tmp.config.ts'] ['NFR-13', 'FR-17', 'FR-9']\nTASK-2 None ['prisma/schema.prisma', 'prisma/migrations/20261109000000_add_assignments/migration.sql'] ['FR-1', 'FR-2', 'FR-3', 'FR-4', 'FR-5', 'FR-6', 'NFR-11']\nTASK-3 None ['src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts', 'tests/unit/assignments/grading-math.test.ts'] ['FR-23', 'FR-28', 'FR-30', 'FR-31', 'FR-36', 'NFR-1', 'NFR-9', 'NFR-14']\nTASK-4 None ['src/lib/dates.ts', 'tests/unit/dates.test.ts'] ['FR-10', 'NFR-9', 'NFR-14']\nTASK-5 None ['src/lib/validators/assignments.ts', 'tests/unit/assign