r a student who did not submit. The service creates a Submission with text = null, no files, submittedAt = gradedAt and attemptNumber = 0 (the offline/no-submission marker).\nfunctionalRequirements FR-9 | Build the create/edit page at /courses/[courseId]/assignments/new. Fields: title, Markdown instructions (the PRD-08 editor), attachments (FileUpload, context 'assignment'), submission type, max points, due date-time (school timezo\nfunctionalRequirements FR-10 | Default the due date-time to the next teaching day at 23:59 in the school timezone. 'Teaching day' is taken from the existing SchoolDay.isTeaching weekday table, because holidays are not modelled before PRD-14.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-11 | Rubric builder: add, reorder and remove criteria (title, description, levels with label + points + description). The sum of the criterion maximums must equal max points. Otherwise show the inline error 'Rubric totals {sum} points \nfunctionalRequirements FR-12 | Offer 'Save draft' (DRAFT), 'Publish' (PUBLISHED) and 'Schedule' (SCHEDULED). Schedule requires an available-from in the future, and the assignment stays hidden from students and parents until then.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-13 | A SCHEDULED assignment counts as visible once availableFrom ≤ server now. Visibility is computed at read time. No background job rewrites the status to PUBLISHED.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-14 | Editing the due date or max points of a published assignment that has submissions shows a warning. Changing max points recalculates nothing: existing scores are kept, and a banner prompts the teacher to review grades.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-15 | A 'Duplicate to other courses' action copies the assignment as DRAFT to selected courses the teacher manages (POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}). The copy keeps the instructions, attachments, settings and rubric. The\nfunctionalRequirements FR-16 | Register an 'Assignments' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts for all roles that can view the course.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-17 | Teacher/admin view of the course Assignments tab: a table with title, due date, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted and a 'Grade' button.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-18 | Student view of the course Assignments tab: a list grouped as Upcoming, Past due (missing), Submitted and Returned. Parents see the same view, read-only, for their linked child.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-19 | The assignment page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId] shows the instructions (sanitised Markdown), attachments, due date, late policy summary, rubric (if any) and the submission panel. When under 48 hours remain, it a\nfunctionalRequirements FR-20 | The submission panel shows a Markdown text editor and/or file upload, depending on submissionType (NO_SUBMISSION shows neither). File upload respects maxFileCount. Draft text autosaves to localStorage only, never to the server.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-21 | Clicking Submit opens a confirmation Dialog before the POST.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-22 | Server submission rules: the assignment is visible; the student is ACTIVE-enrolled in the course; the student is not exempt. If now > dueAt, allowLate must be true and now ≤ lateCutoffAt (when set). Otherwise return VALIDATION_ERR\nfunctionalRequirements FR-23 | On submit, compute isLate = submittedAt > dueAt and lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h), using server time. For example, due Mon 23:59 and submitted Wed 10:00 gives lateDays = 2.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-24 | Resubmission is allowed until dueAt (or lateCutoffAt / indefinitely when late is allowed) and only while status = SUBMITTED. It copies the previous attempt into SubmissionHistory, increments attemptNumber, and clears rawScore, pen\nfunctionalRequirements FR-25 | After submitting, the student sees a receipt such as 'Submitted Mon 14 Sep 2026, 21:04 (attempt 2)', in the school timezone, plus the files and text submitted.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-26 | After return, the student sees the final score, rubric breakdown, feedback and the late penalty applied.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-27 | Until the work is returned, the student and parent see 'Submitted — awaiting grading'. No score, rubric scores or feedback are sent in the API response.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-28 | Grading page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade, left panel: an MUI List of all enrolled students with status Chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter, and sorting by name\nfunctionalRequirements FR-29 | Grading main panel: the selected submission's text as sanitised Markdown, and its files listed with inline preview for images and PDFs (<img>/<iframe> to /api/files/:id?inline=1, which already exists). Previous attempts (Submissio\nfunctionalRequirements FR-30 | Grading form. With a rubric, each criterion is an exclusive ToggleButtonGroup of levels, and the selected points auto-sum into the raw score (for example 8 + 9 → 17). Without a rubric, the raw score is entered directly. The late p\nfunctionalRequirements FR-31 | finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100), rounded half-up to 2 dp. For example, raw 18 with 20 % → 14.40. It is computed server-side at grading time.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-32 | Grading buttons: 'Save' (graded, not visible to the student), 'Save & return' (returns this submission and sets returnedAt) and the bulk 'Return all graded' (POST /api/assignments/:id/return; submissionIds optional, defaults to al\nfunctionalRequirements FR-33 | Keyboard shortcuts on the grading screen: J = next student, K = previous student, Ctrl+Enter = save and go to the next student. The shortcuts are not captured while typing in text fields, except Ctrl+Enter.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-34 | 'Grade without submission' for students who did not submit (POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}). It creates the attemptNumber = 0 Submission described in FR-8.\nfunctionalRequi