ents FR-44 | Register and send assignment.returned to the student and their parents through the existing notifyStudentAndParents(). The body includes course, title and score, for example 'Mathematics: Fractions worksheet — 18/20'.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-45 | Register and send assignment.missing to parents only (email default true), once per student, 24 hours after dueAt if the student has still not submitted and is not exempt. It is idempotent via AssignmentReminder (kind 'missing') a\nfunctionalRequirements FR-46 | Add the four notification types to NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts with the category ACADEMIC and the role lists that match their recipients.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-47 | Register two file access contexts in src/server/files/contexts.ts: 'assignment' (anyone who can view the assignment, with visibility rules applied) and 'submission' (the submitting student, their linked parents, course managers an\nfunctionalRequirements FR-48 | GET /api/courses/:id/assignments (view course) returns a role-shaped list. Managers get every status with counts. Students and parents get only visible, non-archived assignments, with their own submission state.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-49 | POST /api/courses/:id/assignments (manage course) creates an assignment with its rubric and attachments.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-50 | GET /api/assignments/:id (view). For students and parents the response includes their own submission, with grading fields only once returned.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-51 | PATCH /api/assignments/:id (manage). DELETE /api/assignments/:id (manage) hard-deletes only when there are no submissions. Otherwise it sets archivedAt.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-52 | Archived assignments are hidden from student and parent lists, /assignments, reminders and new submissions. Managers can still see them.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-53 | POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions (STUDENT) {text?, fileIds[]} applies the FR-22 to FR-24 rules. The fileIds must be the student's own uploads with context 'submission', and their number must be ≤ maxFileCount.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-54 | GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions (manage) lists every enrolled student, including those who have not submitted, with their status, exemption and submission summary.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-55 | GET /api/submissions/:id is open to the submitting student, their parents and course managers. SubmissionHistory is included only for managers.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-56 | PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade (manage) {rawScore, penaltyPercent, feedback, rubricScores} sets gradedById/gradedAt and the computed finalScore.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-57 | GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab= (any role) returns the role-shaped data for /assignments. studentId is accepted for parents (it must be a linked child).\nfunctionalRequirements FR-58 | GET /api/students/:id/assignments (view student; uses the existing assertCanViewStudent) returns the per-student assignment list.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-59 | Grading, returning, exempting and offline grading change records owned by a student, so each writes an AuditLog row through the existing audit().\nfunctionalRequirements FR-60 | Assignments with submissionType NO_SUBMISSION are not counted as Missing and trigger no due_soon or missing reminders. They are graded offline only.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-61 | Seed data: MATH-7A gets 4 assignments (one returned with all students graded at 55–100 %; one submitted and awaiting grading with 60 % submitted and 2 late; one due in 2 days; one draft). ENG-7A gets 2 (one with a 3-criterion rubr\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-1 | Correctness: all score arithmetic uses Decimal end to end (Prisma.Decimal / decimal.js, which ships with Prisma), never JS floating point. Final scores round half-up to 2 dp.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-2 | Integrity: submission, deadline, late-day, visibility and reminder checks use server time only. Client timestamps