ents/[assignmentId] shows the instructions (sanitised Markdown), attachments, due date, late policy summary, rubric (if any) and the submission panel. When under 48 hours remain, it adds a live countdown such as 'Due in 5 h 12 min'.\n\nFR-20 The submission panel shows a Markdown text editor and/or file upload, depending on submissionType (NO_SUBMISSION shows neither). File upload respects maxFileCount. Draft text autosaves to localStorage only, never to the server.\n\nFR-21 Clicking Submit opens a confirmation Dialog before the POST.\n\nFR-25 After submitting, the student sees a receipt such as 'Submitted Mon 14 Sep 2026, 21:04 (attempt 2)', in the school timezone, plus the files and text submitted.\n\nFR-26 After return, the student sees the final score, rubric breakdown, feedback and the late penalty applied.\n\nFR-27 Until the work is returned, the student and parent see 'Submitted — awaiting grading'. No score, rubric scores or feedback are sent in the API response.\n\nFR-28 Grading page /courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade, left panel: an MUI List of all enrolled students with status Chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter, and sorting by name or submission time.\n\nFR-29 Grading main panel: the selected submission's text as sanitised Markdown, and its files listed with inline preview for images and PDFs (<img>/<iframe> to /api/files/:id?inline=1, which already exists). Previous attempts (SubmissionHistory) are available in a dropdown.\n\nFR-30 Grading form. With a rubric, each criterion is an exclusive ToggleButtonGroup of levels, and the selected points auto-sum into the raw score (for example 8 + 9 → 17). Without a rubric, the raw score is entered directly. The late penalty is pre-filled as min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty) and can be overridden. The final score is computed live. There is a Markdown feedback editor.\n\nFR-32 Grading buttons: 'Save' (graded, not visible to the student), 'Save & return' (returns this submission and sets returnedAt) and the bulk 'Return all graded' (POST /api/assignments/:id/return; submissionIds optional, defaults to all graded and unreturned).\n\nFR-33 Keyboard shortcuts on the grading screen: J = next student, K = previous student, Ctrl+Enter = save and go to the next student. The shortcuts are not captured while typing in text fields, except Ctrl+Enter.\n\nFR-34 'Grade without submission' for students who did not submit (POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}). It creates the attemptNumber = 0 Submission described in FR-8.\n\nFR-35 An 'Exempt' toggle (PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId) writes or deletes a GradeExemption. Exempt students are removed from missing counts and lists, get no due_soon or missing reminders, cannot submit, and are flagged for exclusion from future gradebook calculation (PRD-11).\n\nFR-37 Build the /assignments page for STUDENT. It lists every assignment across the student's ACTIVE enrollments in four tabs: Upcoming (sorted by due date), Missing (past due, not submitted, not exempt), Submitted and Returned. There is a course filter.\n\nFR-38 The /assignments page for PARENT has a child selector (linked students only) and shows the same content as the student view, read-only.\n\nFR-39 The /assignments page for TEACHER is a 'To grade' list of submitted, ungraded submissions across the courses they teach (teacherId or coTeacherIds), oldest first.\n\nFR-40 Add an 'Assignments' nav entry for /assignments to src/config/navigation.ts for STUDENT, PARENT and TEACHER.\n\nFR-41 Register an 'Assignments' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts. It shows the same per-student data to teachers and admins who view the student (GET /api/students/:id/assignments).\n\nFR-61 Seed data: MATH-7A gets 4 assignments (one returned with all students graded at 55–100 %; one submitted and awaiting grading with 60 % submitted and 2 late; one due in 2 days; one draft). ENG-7A gets 2 (one with a 3-criterion rubric, returned). SCI-7A gets 1 NO_SUBMISSION assignment graded offline. The seed is idempotent and skips when those courses do not exist.\n\nls: artifacts/intake/figma-readiness.json: No such file or directory\nnode      18582 ikramaansari   17u  IPv6 0x529afee513169827      0t0  TCP *:3001 (LISTEN)\nnode      54428 ikramaansari   29u  IPv6 0xbfa51c58facdac7e      0t0  TCP [::1]:5173 (LISTEN)\npostgres  62627 ikramaansari    7u  IPv6  0xab2ac6a7b2555d8      0t0  TCP [::1]:5433 (LISTEN)\npostgres  62627 ikramaansari    8u  IPv4 0x17681b6fd0b66908      0t0  TCP 127.0.0.1:5433 (LISTEN)\nnode      63666 ikramaansari   13u  IPv6 0xbe5893508a3669c1      0t0  TCP *:3000 (LISTEN)\n# Postgres connection string used by Prisma. Points at a local Homebrew\n# postgresql@14 instance on port 5433 (5432 was already taken by another\n# Postgres server on this machine). schoolhub/schoolhub db/user/password.\nDATABASE_URL=***@localhost:5433/schoolhub?schema=public\"\n\n# Public base URL of the app (used for absolute links, e.g. in emails later).\nAPP_URL=\"http://localhost:3000\"\n\n# `openssl rand -base64 32` for real environments.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DRJJmLPHwAMEruPzzoVoor","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
