{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RCzJfLFsnM1fSwGffkbp1E","type":"tool_result","content":"src/app/(app)/assignments/AssignmentList.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/assignments/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/edit/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade/GradingWorkspace.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/SubmissionPanel.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/AssignmentForm.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/CourseAssignmentsTable.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/RubricBuilder.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx\nFileList\nFileUpload\n15:const SEED_PASSWORD = 'SchoolHub123!';\n16:const SEED_USERS: { email: string; firstName: string; lastName: string; role: Role }[] = [\n17:  { email: 'admin@schoolhub.test', firstName: 'Alice', lastName: 'Admin', role: 'ADMIN' },\n18:  { email: 'teacher@schoolhub.test', firstName: 'Tom', lastName: 'Teacher', role: 'TEACHER' },\n19:  { email: 'teacher2@schoolhub.test', firstName: 'Tina', lastName: 'Tutor', role: 'TEACHER' },\n20:  { email: 'student@schoolhub.test', firstName: 'Sam', lastName: 'Student', role: 'STUDENT' },\n21:  { email: 'student2@schoolhub.test', firstName: 'Sara', lastName: 'Scholar', role: 'STUDENT' },\n22:  { email: 'parent@schoolhub.test', firstName: 'Pat', lastName: 'Parent', role: 'PARENT' },\n25:/** PRD-01 FR-28–FR-31: demo accounts. update:{} so a re-run never resets a changed password. */\n30:  const passwordHash = await bcrypt.hash(SEED_PASSWORD, 12);\n34:      where: { email: user.email },\n36:      create: { ...user, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash, passwordChangedAt: now },\n42:    where: { email: 'invited@schoolhub.test' },\n45:      email: 'invited@schoolhub.test',\n50:      passwordHash: null,\n76:      email: 'office@schoolhub.test',\n200:          enrollments: { where: { status: 'ACTIVE' }, select: { student: { select: { id: true, email: true, lastName: true } } } },\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | No ESLint warnings or errors |\n| Unit: `tests/unit/assignments/*`, `tests/unit/dates.test.ts` | 29 / 29 pass |\n| Integration: `tests/integration/assignments/*` (`TEST_DATABASE_URL` = local Postgres :5433, tagged fixtures, cleaned up) | 14 / 14 pass; 3 consecutive full-folder runs green |\n| `npm run build` | **passes** (needs network access for `next/font` Google Fonts) |\n| e2e `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` against a fresh `next start -p 3100` | 5 / 5 pass |\n| Seed: run twice against temporary MATH-7A/ELA-7A/SCI-7A courses | 7 created, then 0 (idempotent); missing courses skip with a log line. Temp data removed. |\n| Migration `20261109000000_add_assignments` | applied with `prisma migrate deploy`; additive only (no DROP/ALTER of existing tables) |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp gate | reachable. `useMuiDocs` (material-ui 9.5.0 llms.txt) + `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup and LinearProgress. Other components follow existing in-repo v9 usage. |\n\n### Decisions and deviations (for QA / reviewer)\n1. **ADR-2 is not enough on its own — follow-up fix in `next.config.js`.** With `@mui/x-internals` pinned to 9.1.0 (`npm ls` shows 9.1.0 everywhere), `next build` still failed with\n   `'useFirstRender' is not exported`. Root cause: webpack resolves `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender` to its **CJS** build. That build re-exports through `Object.keys`, which webpack can't analyse statically,\n   so x-data-grid's `export *` of it breaks. Fix: one `webpack()` alias that points that specifier at the ESM file (commented, removable on a MUI X upgrade). With the alias,\n   DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9) build, so **no D2 fallbacks were needed**. This touches `next.config.js`, which the plan gives to TASK-13. It's logged here as part of TASK-1's environment fix.\n   The pin is kept, because the alias targets the 9.1.0 file.\n2. **Decimal source:** `grading-math.ts` imports `Decimal` from `@prisma/client/runtime/index-browser.js`, which is Prisma's bundled decimal.js. The plain `decimal.js` package is only a transitive\n   **devDependency** (via jsdom), so it would be missing in a production install. ADR-1 (no new dependencies) holds. Values go to Prisma as 2 dp strings, so the two Decimal classes never mix.\n3. **Decimal serialization:** done in explicit typed mappers (`serializeDecimal` helper → `\"14.40\"`), not a generic walker. Same output as D5.\n4. **`GET /api/me/assignments`:** when `tab` is omitted, all rows come back, each with its server-computed `group`. The `/assignments` page groups them on the client (one fetch for all four tabs). With `tab`, the filter works as contracted.\n   The contract said `default UPCOMING`.\n5. **DateTimePicker + school timezone:** `AdapterDateFns` has no timezone support. The form converts UTC ↔ school wall clock with `toZonedTime`/`fromZonedTime` (NFR-9).\n6. **Reminders robustness:** `claim()` treats P2003 (assignment hard-deleted mid-pass) like P2002. Found because the global pass touched another test's assignment during parallel runs.\n7. **Rubric edits keep criterion ids** (upsert by id), so saved `rubricScores` stay valid after an edit.\n8. **TO_GRADE list** is capped at 200 rows (`ponytail:` note). The manager course table pages client-side (`ponytail:` note).\n9. `GET /api/assignments/:id` also returns `studentId` (the viewed child), so parent links stay on the same child.\n\n### Pre-existing issues seen (not caused by SH-9 and not in scope)\n- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 2 failures (FR-22 notification count, FR-10/FR-19 EXCUSED save). These exercise attendance code that SH-9 doesn't touch. They look time-of-day dependent.\n- `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx` (focus assertion), `tests/unit/useToast.test.tsx` (timer/provider), and `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts` (next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM) fail.\n  None of them import SH-9 code. There is no baseline to compare against, because the old `vitest/config.js` import couldn't load at all (blocker 3, now fixed).\n- `next build` prints \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines for every existing GET route. That's build-time log noise, not a failure. `/api/me/assignments` is marked `force-dynamic` to stay quiet.\n- **A stale `next-server` from 27 Oct (PID 63666) is still listening on :3000 for this project, serving old code.** Playwright's `reuseExistingServer` would reuse it, so e2e was run on :3100.\n  I didn't kill it. Restart it before manual testing or QA.\n- The repo's git root is the home directory and the whole project is untracked, so `git stash`/diff can't serve as a baseline.\n\n### Known gaps carried forward (from the design; not new scope)\n- There's no `studentTabs` renderer, so `/students/[id]/assignments` is reachable by URL only (FR-41, blocker 5).\n- The platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true` (ADR-4).\n- D11 changes a security header narrowly (`X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + `frame-ancestors 'self'` only on `/api/files/:id`). Reviewer sign-off is recommended.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5bdbc6d-8407-44d1-9b1e-f6d173da0eb5","uuid":"f147742f-40f4-4782-a403-1ae5785340ef","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:41:46.134Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"src/app/(app)/assignments/AssignmentList.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/assignments/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/edit/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade/GradingWorkspace.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[