{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgrv8UT9EDAVuwQZikoqD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016onVQoAXC6Sf226uEEE1L2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/ui-verification && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nF=[\n(\"FR-9\",\"Assignment create page /courses/[id]/assignments/new\",\"PASS\",\"Renders at 1280 with Title, Markdown Instructions (Write/Preview), Attach files (0/10), Submission type, Max points, Max files, Due and Available-from DateTimePickers (school-time helper text), Allow extra credit, Allow late submissions, Grade with a rubric. Screenshot teacher-assignment-new-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-10\",\"Due date default\",\"PASS\",\"On Mon 9 Nov (America/New_York), Due defaulted to 11/10/2026 23:59 with helper 'School time (America/New_York)', i.e. the next teaching day at 23:59.\"),\n(\"FR-11\",\"Rubric builder\",\"PASS\",\"Add criterion works. One 10-pt criterion against max 20 shows 'Rubric totals 10 points but the assignment is worth 20.' and Publish is disabled. Adding a second criterion clears the alert. 'Move criterion 1 down' swapped [Accuracy, Working] to [Working, Accuracy]. 'Remove criterion 2' went from 2 criteria to 1. Screenshots teacher-rubric-mismatch-1280.png and teacher-rubric-builder-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-12\",\"Save draft / Schedule / Publish actions\",\"PASS\",\"All three buttons render on the form. Publish is gated by rubric validity (FR-11). Draft and Scheduled rows show the correct status chips in the teacher table. Students do not see DRAFT or future-SCHEDULED assignments in the course tab. The Save draft and Schedule click paths were not exercised here; Publish is covered by the e2e suite.\"),\n(\"FR-14\",\"Edit published assignment with submissions\",\"PASS\",\"The edit page for a published assignment with 2 submissions shows the warning '2 students have already submitted. Changing the due date or max points will not recalculate existing scores.' Screenshot teacher-assignment-edit-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-15\",\"Duplicate to other courses dialog\",\"PASS\",\"The dialog opens from the edit page with the explanatory copy ('Copies are created as drafts…'). The Courses picker lists only the teacher's other course (UIV Science). Screenshot teacher-duplicate-dialog-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-16\",\"Course 'Assignments' tab\",\"PASS\",\"The ASSIGNMENTS tab appears in the course tab bar for teacher, student and parent views, and is selected on assignment routes.\"),\n(\"FR-17\",\"Teacher course Assignments table\",\"PASS\",\"DataGrid columns are Title, Due, Status, Submitted, Graded, plus a GRADE button on each of the 5 rows. Counts are correct (Reading log 2/3 submitted, 1/2 graded). Published/Draft/Scheduled chips are colour-coded. Search box and pagination render. Screenshot teacher-course-assignments-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-18\",\"Student course Assignments tab (grouped list)\",\"PASS\",\"At 375 px there is no horizontal scroll. Groups Upcoming, Returned and Past due render, and empty groups are omitted. The Returned item shows a 16.2/20 chip. DRAFT and future-SCHEDULED assignments are hidden. Minor observation (UIV-2): the NO_SUBMISSION 'Lab safety demo' sits under 'Past due' with no Missing chip. /assignments correctly leaves it out of Missing (FR-60), so only the heading differs. Screenshot student-course-assignments-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-19\",\"Assignment detail page\",\"PASS\",\"Shows the due date (school tz), a 'Due in 4 h 59 min' chip, points and submission type, late-policy summary ('Late submissions accepted, 10 % per day late (max 50 %)' / 'not accepted'), sanitised Markdown instructions (**chapter 3** renders bold), and the rubric table. No horizontal scroll at 375 px. Screenshot student-assignment-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-20\",\"Submission panel\",\"PASS\",\"TEXT_AND_FILE shows the Markdown answer editor plus Attach files (0/3). NO_SUBMISSION shows neither, with the copy 'No online submission. This assignment is graded by your teacher.' A PNG upload appeared in the list before submit.\"),\n(\"FR-21\",\"Submit confirmation dialog\",\"PASS\",\"Clicking Submit opens 'Submit your work? You can resubmit until the deadline, unless your work has been returned.' with Cancel/Submit. The POST happens only after confirming.\"),\n(\"FR-25\",\"Submission receipt\",\"PASS\",\"After submit: 'Submitted Mon 9 Nov 2026, 01:48 (attempt 1)' in school time, with files and text. Screenshot student-submitted-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-26\",\"Returned view (score, rubric, feedback, penalty)\",\"PASS\",\"The non-rubric returned view shows '16.2 / 20', 'Raw score 18 · late penalty 10 %' and the feedback. The rubric returned view shows '15 / 20' and a Criterion/Points/Comment table (Accuracy 10/10, Working 5/10). Minor (UIV-3): scores show trimmed decimals ('16.2'), not the 2 dp '16.20' style of the PRD example. The value is correct. Screenshots student-returned-375.png and student-returned-rubric-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-27\",\"Awaiting grading state\",\"PASS\",\"Before return, the student sees 'Submitted — awaiting grading' and no score. The teacher had already saved a 15/20 grade (unreturned), and no '/ 20' score text appeared on the student page. The /assignments Submitted tab shows 'Awaiting grading'.\"),\n(\"FR-28\",\"Grading page left roster\",\"PASS\",\"An MUI list of all 3 enrolled students with status chips Returned (18/20), Late, and Not submitted, plus Status filter and Sort selects. Screenshot teacher-grade-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-29\",\"Grading main panel + inline preview\",\"PASS\",\"Submission text renders as sanitised Markdown (*summary* becomes <em>). The uploaded PNG is listed (working.png, 70 B) and previews inline as an <img> that loaded (naturalWidth > 0) through the 'submission' file context. A PDF/iframe preview was not exercised. Screenshot teacher-grade-rubric-preview-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-30\",\"Grading form (rubric toggles / raw score)\",\"PASS\",\"With a rubric, each criterion is an exclusive ToggleButtonGroup ('Excellent · 10', 'Developing · 5'). Choosing 10 + 5 auto-filled Raw score (rubric total) = 15, and the saved rubricScores match. Without a rubric there is a Raw score (max 20) field plus a 'Late penalty %' field prefilled to 10 for a 1-day-late submission (lateDays chip '1 day late').\"),\n(\"FR-31\",\"Final score preview\",\"PASS\",\"Raw 18 with 10 % penalty previews 'Final score 16.2 / 20'. The DB stores finalScore 16.2 (16.20), which matches 18 × 0.9. See UIV-3 for the display format.\"),\n(\"FR-32\",\"Save / Save & return / Return all graded\",\"PASS\",\"Save keeps the submission SUBMITTED (not visible to the student). Save & return sets RETURNED with returnedAt, and the roster chip changes to Returned. 'Return all graded (1)' opens a confirm dialog ('1 graded submission will become visible…') and returns it. The success toasts are often lost; see PLATFORM-TOAST.\"),\n(\"FR-33\",\"Keyboard shortcuts J / K / Ctrl+Enter\",\"PASS\",\"With focus outside inputs, J moved the selection from Blake Late to Morgan Missing and K moved back. Typing 'j' in Feedback did not navigate. Ctrl+Enter from inside the raw-score field saved (toast 'Grade saved') and advanced from Alex to Blake. The hint 'Shortcuts: J next · K previous · Ctrl+Enter save & next' is shown.\"),\n(\"FR-34\",\"Grade without submission\",\"PASS\",\"A non-submitter shows 'Not submitted. You can grade without a submission below.' and a 'Grade without submission' form with no late-penalty field. Saving raw 8 on the NO_SUBMISSION assignment created a Submission with text = null, rawScore 8 and finalScore 8. Screenshots teacher-grade-not-submitted-1280.png and teacher-grade-offline-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-35\",\"Exempt toggle\",\"PASS\",\"Switching Exempt on wrote a GradeExemption row, showed 'Exempt: excluded from missing lists, reminders and gradebook calculations.' and hid the grade form. Switching it off deleted the row. While exempt, the parent view showed 'This student is exempt from this assignment.' and the student's Missing count dropped. Screenshot teacher-grade-exempt-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-36\",\"Score bound feedback in UI\",\"PASS\",\"Entering raw 25 against max 20 (no extra credit) shows the 'Above the maximum' error and disables Save. Server-side enforcement is covered by QA integration tests, not re-verified here.\"),\n(\"FR-37\",\"/assignments (student)\",\"PASS\",\"Four tabs with counts: UPCOMING, MISSING, SUBMITTED, RETURNED. Contents are correct across states. A student with no submission sees 'UIV Reading log … Missing' under MISSING (1), and the NO_SUBMISSION assignment is not listed as missing. Empty tabs show 'Nothing here'. Screenshots student-assignments-*-375.png and student-assignments-missing-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-38\",\"/assignments (parent)\",\"PASS\",\"A Child selector lists only the linked students (Morgan Missing, Alex Aardvark) and shows the same four-tab content. The parent's assignment page has no Submit button or answer field (read-only). Screenshot parent-assignments-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-39\",\"/assignments (teacher 'To grade')\",\"PASS\",\"Shows 'To grade — Submitted work waiting for a grade, oldest first.' with the row 'Alex Aardvark — UIV Fractions worksheet · UIV Maths · submitted …'. Screenshot teacher-to-grade-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-40\",\"Nav entry 'Assignments'\",\"PASS\",\"The 'Assignments' link appears in the side nav for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT at 1280 px. At 375 px it sits behind the hamburger drawer, which was not opened.\"),\n(\"FR-41\",\"Student profile Assignments tab\",\"PASS\",\"/students/[id]/assignments renders for the teacher, with the student's name and the four-tab list (UPCOMING 1, MISSING 1, SUBMITTED 1). The known gap carried from design: no studentTabs renderer exists, so the page is reachable by URL only and was opened directly. Screenshot teacher-student-assignments-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-60\",\"NO_SUBMISSION handling in UI\",\"PASS\",\"No submit UI on the student page. Not counted under MISSING on /assignments. Graded offline only (see FR-34).\"),\n(\"PLATFORM-TOAST\",\"ToastProvider (src/components/Toast/ToastProvider.tsx) — affects grading feedback\",\"FAIL\",\"Pre-existing platform defect (not an SH-9-owned file), but it is visible during SH-9's rapid-grading flow. When a second toast is queued while one is showing, handleExited drops the first toast but 'open' stays false. The queued toast never appears until some later showToast call, which then shows a stale message. Reproduced 3 times: Ctrl+Enter ('Grade saved') then Save & return within 5 s left 'Saved and returned' hidden for more than 20 s, although the DB showed RETURNED. 'Return all graded' after a Save likewise showed no 'Returned 1 submission' toast. This may relate to the pre-existing useToast.test.tsx failure in the QA report.\"),\n]\nout={\"ticketId\":\"SH-9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-09T06:55:42Z\",\"phase\":\"ui-verification\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"status\":\"complete\",\n\"summary\":{\"uiFacingRequirements\":30,\"pass\":30,\"fail\":0,\"blocked\":0,\"additionalFindings\":{\"PLATFORM-TOAST\":\"FAIL (pre-existing, not SH-9-owned)\",\"UIV-2\":\"minor\",\"UIV-3\":\"minor\"}},\n\"method\":\"Production build (`npm run build`, exit 0) served with `next start -p 3300` against local Postgres :5433. The stale :3000/:3001 servers were left alone. A throwaway Playwright driver outside the repo (/tmp/uiv-sh9/driver.cjs) created tagged fixtures (code 'uiv-sh9': teacher, admin, 3 students, a parent linked to 2 students, 2 courses, 5 assignments covering ONLINE_TEXT late-allowed, NO_SUBMISSION, TEXT_AND_FILE with a 2-criterion rubric, DRAFT and SCHEDULED, plus returned and late submissions). It signed in per role and drove every SH-9 surface at 1280x800 (teacher) and 375x667 (student/parent), with bypassCSP as in the e2e suite (ADR-4, known platform CSP issue). State changes were verified against the DB. Fixtures were removed afterwards (cleanedUp: true). No console or page errors were captured for any role. figma-readiness.json does not exist, so checks compare against requirements.json and the PRD text only. Screenshots are in screenshots/ and raw probe output is in uiv-raw.json. Note: the login rate limit (10/5 min/IP, in-process) required restarting the :3300 server between runs; this is expected behaviour.\",\n\"findings\":[{\"requirementId\":a,\"surface\":b,\"verdict\":c,\"notes\":d} for a,b,c,d in F],\n\"observations\":[\n {\"id\":\"UIV-2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"summary\":\"The student course tab lists NO_SUBMISSION assignments under the 'Past due' heading. FR-18 labels that group 'Past due (missing)' and FR-60 says NO_SUBMISSION is never missing. There is no Missing chip, and /assignments is correct.\",\"file\":\"src/app/(app)/assignments/AssignmentList.tsx\"},\n {\"id\":\"UIV-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"summary\":\"Scores display with trailing zeros trimmed ('16.2 / 20'). The PRD example formats 2 dp ('14.40'). The values are correct.\",\"file\":\"pts() formatter used by GradingWorkspace / SubmissionPanel / AssignmentList\"},\n {\"id\":\"UIV-4\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"summary\":\"Full-page screenshots at 1280 px show the fixed app bar and nav drawn mid-page on tall pages (e.g. teacher-grade-rubric-preview-1280.png). This is a capture artifact of fixed positioning, not a layout defect.\"}],\n\"notExercised\":[\"Save draft / Schedule button clicks (FR-12)\",\"PDF iframe preview (FR-29)\",\"Resubmission flow (FR-24) and late-submission warning text 'This will be marked late.' (FR-22)\",\"375 px nav drawer contents (FR-40)\",\"Dark mode\"],\n\"blockedReason\":None}\njson.dump(out,open('ui-verification-report.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(len(out['findings']))\nEOF\npython3 -m json.tool ui-verification-report.json > /dev/null && echo valid","description":"Write ui-verification-report.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1276,"cache_read_input_tokens":110414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1276,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5bdbc6d-8407-44d1-9b1e-f6d173da0eb5","uuid":"3c7a35ed-881d-428a-a1ac-bd3695a9e7a1","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:56:28.493Z","request_id":"req_011Cgrv8UDFsBPKEvpPvQgi8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016onVQoAXC6Sf226uEEE1L2":{"command":"cd ~/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/ui-verification && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nF=[\n(\"FR-9\",\"Assignment create page /courses/[id]/assignments/new\",\"PASS\",\"Renders at 1280 with Title, Markdown Instructions (Write/Preview), Attach files (0/10), Submission type, Max points, Max files, Due and Available-from DateTimePickers (school-time helper text), Allow extra credit, Allow late submissions, Grade with a rubric. Screenshot teacher-assignment-new-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-10\",\"Due date default\",\"PASS\",\"On Mon 9 Nov (America/New_York), Due defaulted to 11/10/2026 23:59 with helper 'School time (America/New_York)', i.e. the next teaching day at 23:59.\"),\n(\"FR-11\",\"Rubric builder\",\"PASS\",\"Add criterion works. One 10-pt criterion against max 20 shows 'Rubric totals 10 points but the assignment is worth 20.' and Publish is disabled. Adding a second criterion clears the alert. 'Move criterion 1 down' swapped [Accuracy, Working] to [Working, Accuracy]. 'Remove criterion 2' went from 2 criteria to 1. Screenshots teacher-rubric-mismatch-1280.png and teacher-rubric-builder-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-12\",\"Save draft / Schedule / Publish actions\",\"PASS\",\"All three buttons render on the form. Publish is gated by rubric validity (FR-11). Draft and Scheduled rows show the correct status chips in the teacher table. Students do not see DRAFT or future-SCHEDULED assignments in the course tab. The Save draft and Schedule click paths were not exercised here; Publish is covered by the e2e suite.\"),\n(\"FR-14\",\"Edit published assignment with submissions\",\"PASS\",\"The edit page for a published assignment with 2 submissions shows the warning '2 students have already submitted. Changing the due date or max points will not recalculate existing scores.' Screenshot teacher-assignment-edit-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-15\",\"Duplicate to other courses dialog\",\"PASS\",\"The dialog opens from the edit page with the explanatory copy ('Copies are created as drafts…'). The Courses picker lists only the teacher's other course (UIV Science). Screenshot teacher-duplicate-dialog-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-16\",\"Course 'Assignments' tab\",\"PASS\",\"The ASSIGNMENTS tab appears in the course tab bar for teacher, student and parent views, and is selected on assignment routes.\"),\n(\"FR-17\",\"Teacher course Assignments table\",\"PASS\",\"DataGrid columns are Title, Due, Status, Submitted, Graded, plus a GRADE button on each of the 5 rows. Counts are correct (Reading log 2/3 submitted, 1/2 graded). Published/Draft/Scheduled chips are colour-coded. Search box and pagination render. Screenshot teacher-course-assignments-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-18\",\"Student course Assignments tab (grouped list)\",\"PASS\",\"At 375 px there is no horizontal scroll. Groups Upcoming, Returned and Past due render, and empty groups are omitted. The Returned item shows a 16.2/20 chip. DRAFT and future-SCHEDULED assignments are hidden. Minor observation (UIV-2): the NO_SUBMISSION 'Lab safety demo' sits under 'Past due' with no Missing chip. /assignments correctly leaves it out of Missing (FR-60), so only the heading differs. Screenshot student-course-assignments-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-19\",\"Assignment detail page\",\"PASS\",\"Shows the due date (school tz), a 'Due in 4 h 59 min' chip, points and submission type, late-policy summary ('Late submissions accepted, 10 % per day late (max 50 %)' / 'not accepted'), sanitised Markdown instructions (**chapter 3** renders bold), and the rubric table. No horizontal scroll at 375 px. Screenshot student-assignment-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-20\",\"Submission panel\",\"PASS\",\"TEXT_AND_FILE shows the Markdown answer editor plus Attach files (0/3). NO_SUBMISSION shows neither, with the copy 'No online submission. This assignment is graded by your teacher.' A PNG upload appeared in the list before submit.\"),\n(\"FR-21\",\"Submit confirmation dialog\",\"PASS\",\"Clicking Submit opens 'Submit your work? You can resubmit until the deadline, unless your work has been returned.' with Cancel/Submit. The POST happens only after confirming.\"),\n(\"FR-25\",\"Submission receipt\",\"PASS\",\"After submit: 'Submitted Mon 9 Nov 2026, 01:48 (attempt 1)' in school time, with files and text. Screenshot student-submitted-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-26\",\"Returned view (score, rubric, feedback, penalty)\",\"PASS\",\"The non-rubric returned view shows '16.2 / 20', 'Raw score 18 · late penalty 10 %' and the feedback. The rubric returned view shows '15 / 20' and a Criterion/Points/Comment table (Accuracy 10/10, Working 5/10). Minor (UIV-3): scores show trimmed decimals ('16.2'), not the 2 dp '16.20' style of the PRD example. The value is correct. Screenshots student-returned-375.png and student-returned-rubric-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-27\",\"Awaiting grading state\",\"PASS\",\"Before return, the student sees 'Submitted — awaiting grading' and no score. The teacher had already saved a 15/20 grade (unreturned), and no '/ 20' score text appeared on the student page. The /assignments Submitted tab shows 'Awaiting grading'.\"),\n(\"FR-28\",\"Grading page left roster\",\"PASS\",\"An MUI list of all 3 enrolled students with status chips Returned (18/20), Late, and Not submitted, plus Status filter and Sort selects. Screenshot teacher-grade-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-29\",\"Grading main panel + inline preview\",\"PASS\",\"Submission text renders as sanitised Markdown (*summary* becomes <em>). The uploaded PNG is listed (working.png, 70 B) and previews inline as an <img> that loaded (naturalWidth > 0) through the 'submission' file context. A PDF/iframe preview was not exercised. Screenshot teacher-grade-rubric-preview-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-30\",\"Grading form (rubric toggles / raw score)\",\"PASS\",\"With a rubric, each criterion is an exclusive ToggleButtonGroup ('Excellent · 10', 'Developing · 5'). Choosing 10 + 5 auto-filled Raw score (rubric total) = 15, and the saved rubricScores match. Without a rubric there is a Raw score (max 20) field plus a 'Late penalty %' field prefilled to 10 for a 1-day-late submission (lateDays chip '1 day late').\"),\n(\"FR-31\",\"Final score preview\",\"PASS\",\"Raw 18 with 10 % penalty previews 'Final score 16.2 / 20'. The DB stores finalScore 16.2 (16.20), which matches 18 × 0.9. See UIV-3 for the display format.\"),\n(\"FR-32\",\"Save / Save & return / Return all graded\",\"PASS\",\"Save keeps the submission SUBMITTED (not visible to the student). Save & return sets RETURNED with returnedAt, and the roster chip changes to Returned. 'Return all graded (1)' opens a confirm dialog ('1 graded submission will become visible…') and returns it. The success toasts are often lost; see PLATFORM-TOAST.\"),\n(\"FR-33\",\"Keyboard shortcuts J / K / Ctrl+Enter\",\"PASS\",\"With focus outside inputs, J moved the selection from Blake Late to Morgan Missing and K moved back. Typing 'j' in Feedback did not navigate. Ctrl+Enter from inside the raw-score field saved (toast 'Grade saved') and advanced from Alex to Blake. The hint 'Shortcuts: J next · K previous · Ctrl+Enter save & next' is shown.\"),\n(\"FR-34\",\"Grade without submission\",\"PASS\",\"A non-submitter shows 'Not submitted. You can grade without a submission below.' and a 'Grade without submission' form with no late-penalty field. Saving raw 8 on the NO_SUBMISSION assignment created a Submission with text = null, rawScore 8 and finalScore 8. Screenshots teacher-grade-not-submitted-1280.png and teacher-grade-offline-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-35\",\"Exempt toggle\",\"PASS\",\"Switching Exempt on wrote a GradeExemption row, showed 'Exempt: excluded from missing lists, reminders and gradebook calculations.' and hid the grade form. Switching it off deleted the row. While exempt, the parent view showed 'This student is exempt from this assignment.' and the student's Missing count dropped. Screenshot teacher-grade-exempt-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-36\",\"Score bound feedback in UI\",\"PASS\",\"Entering raw 25 against max 20 (no extra credit) shows the 'Above the maximum' error and disables Save. Server-side enforcement is covered by QA integration tests, not re-verified here.\"),\n(\"FR-37\",\"/assignments (student)\",\"PASS\",\"Four tabs with counts: UPCOMING, MISSING, SUBMITTED, RETURNED. Contents are correct across states. A student with no submission sees 'UIV Reading log … Missing' under MISSING (1), and the NO_SUBMISSION assignment is not listed as missing. Empty tabs show 'Nothing here'. Screenshots student-assignments-*-375.png and student-assignments-missing-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-38\",\"/assignments (parent)\",\"PASS\",\"A Child selector lists only the linked students (Morgan Missing, Alex Aardvark) and shows the same four-tab content. The parent's assignment page has no Submit button or answer field (read-only). Screenshot parent-assignments-375.png.\"),\n(\"FR-39\",\"/assignments (teacher 'To grade')\",\"PASS\",\"Shows 'To grade — Submitted work waiting for a grade, oldest first.' with the row 'Alex Aardvark — UIV Fractions worksheet · UIV Maths · submitted …'. Screenshot teacher-to-grade-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-40\",\"Nav entry 'Assignments'\",\"PASS\",\"The 'Assignments' link appears in the side nav for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT at 1280 px. At 375 px it sits behind the hamburger drawer, which was not opened.\"),\n(\"FR-41\",\"Student profile Assignments tab\",\"PASS\",\"/students/[id]/assignments renders for the teacher, with the student's name and the four-tab list (UPCOMING 1, MISSING 1, SUBMITTED 1). The known gap carried from design: no studentTabs renderer exists, so the page is reachable by URL only and was opened directly. Screenshot teacher-student-assignments-1280.png.\"),\n(\"FR-60\",\"NO_SUBMISSION handling in UI\",\"PASS\",\"No submit UI on the student page. Not counted under MISSING on /assignments. Graded offline only (see FR-34).\"),\n(\"PLATFORM-TOAST\",\"ToastProvider (src/components/Toast/ToastProvider.tsx) — affects grading feedback\",\"FAIL\",\"Pre-existing platform defect (not an SH-9-owned file), but it is visible during SH-9's rapid-grading flow. When a second toast is queued while one is showing, handleExited drops the first toast but 'open' stays false. The queued toast never appears until some later showToast call, which then shows a stale message. Reproduced 3 times: Ctrl+Enter ('Grade saved') then Save & return within 5 s left 'Saved and returned' hidden for more than 20 s, although the DB showed RETURNED. 'Return all graded' after a Save likewise showed no 'Returned 1 submission' toast. This may relate to the pre-existing useToast.test.tsx failure in the QA report.\"),\n]\nout={\"ticketId\":\"SH-9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-09T06:55:42Z\",\"phase\":\"ui-verification\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"status\":\"complete\",\n\"summary\":{\"uiFacingRequirements\":30,\"pass\":30,\"fail\":0,\"blocked\":0,\"additionalFindings\":{\"PLATFORM-TOAST\":\"FAIL (pre-existing, not SH-9-owned)\",\"UIV-2\":\"minor\",\"UIV-3\":\"minor\"}},\n\"method\":\"Production build (`npm run build`, exit 0) served with `next start -p 3300` against local Postgres :5433. The stale :3000/:3001 servers were left alone. A throwaway Playwright driver outside the repo (/tmp/uiv-sh9/driver.cjs) created tagged fixtures (code 'uiv-sh9': teacher, admin, 3 students, a parent linked to 2 students, 2 courses, 5 assignments covering ONLINE_TEXT late-allowed, NO_SUBMISSION, TEXT_AND_FILE with a 2-criterion rubric, DRAFT and SCHEDULED, plus returned and late submissions). It signed in per role and drove every SH-9 surface at 1280x800 (teacher) and 375x667 (student/parent), with bypassCSP as in the e2e suite (ADR-4, known platform CSP issue). State changes were verified against the DB. Fixtures were removed afterwards (cleanedUp: true). No console or page errors were captured for any role. figma-readiness.json does not exist, so checks compare against requirements.json and the PRD text only. Screenshots are in screenshots/ and raw probe output is in uiv-raw.json. Note: the login rate limit (10/5 min/IP, in-process) required restarting the :3300 server between runs; this is expected behaviour.\",\n\"findings\":[{\"requirementId\":a,\"surface\":b,\"verdict\":c,\"notes\":d} for a,b,c,d in F],\n\"observations\":[\n {\"id\":\"UIV-2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"summary\":\"The student course tab lists NO_SUBMISSION assignments under the 'Past due' heading. FR-18 labels that group 'Past due (missing)' and FR-60 says NO_SUBMISSION is never missing. There is no Missing chip, and /assignments is correct.\",\"file\":\"src/app/(app)/assignments/AssignmentList.tsx\"},\n {\"id\":\"UIV-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"summary\":\"Scores display with trailing zeros trimmed ('16.2 / 20'). The PRD example formats 2 dp ('14.40'). The values are correct.\",\"file\":\"pts() formatter used by GradingWorkspace / SubmissionPanel / AssignmentList\"},\n {\"id\":\"UIV-4\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"summary\":\"Full-page screenshots at 1280 px show the fixed app bar and nav drawn mid-page on tall pages (e.g. teacher-grade-rubric-preview-1280.png). This is a capture artifact of fixed positioning, not a layout defect.\"}],\n\"notExercised\":[\"Save draft / Schedule button clicks (FR-12)\",\"PDF iframe preview (FR-29)\",\"Resubmission flow (FR-24) and late-submission warning text 'This will be marked late.' (FR-22)\",\"375 px nav drawer contents (FR-40)\",\"Dark mode\"],\n\"blockedReason\":None}\njson.dump(out,open('ui-verification-report.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(len(out['findings']))\nEOF\npython3 -m json.tool ui-verification-report.json > /dev/null && echo valid","description":"Write ui-verification-report.json"}}}
