{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrvCniqx5TirKppFZF7A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran the SH-9 UI verification phase. All 30 screens and requirements that show up in the UI pass, and none are blocked. I found one bug that sits outside the SH-9 code but affects the grading screen.\n\n**How I checked:** I built the app for production (build passed) and ran it on port 3300. A Playwright browser script created test data: a teacher, three students, a parent, two courses and five assignments covering every submission type, draft/scheduled states, and late and returned work. It signed in as each role and used every SH-9 page at desktop width (teacher) and phone width (student and parent). Every change I made through the screens — grading, returning, exempting, grading without a submission, submitting — was confirmed in the database. No browser console errors appeared, and the test data was deleted afterwards. There is no Figma design file, so I compared against the requirements and the PRD only.\n\n**The bug: success messages go missing.** The app's pop-up message component (`src/components/Toast/ToastProvider.tsx`) drops a message if it arrives while another one is still showing. It never appears unless some later action triggers it, and then it shows the old text.\n- **When it happens:** in fast grading, Ctrl+Enter followed by \"Save & return\" within 5 seconds left the \"Saved and returned\" message hidden for over 20 seconds. \"Return all graded\" right after a save likewise showed no message.\n- **Impact:** the saves themselves worked (the database showed the work returned), but the teacher gets no confirmation.\n- **Likely fix:** reopen the message box in `handleExited` when more messages are waiting. This may also explain the `useToast.test.tsx` failure that QA already listed as existing before SH-9.\n\n**Minor notes:**\n- On the course's Assignments tab, students see a \"no submission\" assignment under \"Past due\". The main `/assignments` page correctly leaves it out of Missing.\n- Scores show as `16.2 / 20` rather than the PRD's 2-decimal style (`16.20`). The numbers themselves are correct.\n\n**Not tested:** clicking \"Save draft\" and \"Schedule\", PDF previews (image previews work), resubmitting, the late-submission warning, and the phone-size navigation menu. These are listed in both reports.\n\nThe earlier report files in that folder were left over from SH-8, so I replaced them. The script's login limit (10 per 5 minutes) meant restarting my port-3300 server between runs; that's expected behaviour. I stopped that server when done and left the other dev servers on 3000 and 3001 running. The 3000 one is still serving old code, as the dev log noted.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/ui-verification/`:\n- `ui-verification-report.json`\n- `ui-verification-report.md`\n- `uiv-raw.json`\n- `screenshots/` (25 images)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1413,"cache_read_input_tokens":117205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1413,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5bdbc6d-8407-44d1-9b1e-f6d173da0eb5","uuid":"389c2c09-c3cb-4df9-bd8a-7894775d9af6","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:56:50.953Z","request_id":"req_011CgrvCnNGmvuDfSYnWKMxu"}
