{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AUCs5vMxfmbAQNHPkQCtNZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Dev Log — SH-10 (PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams)\n\n> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-9 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-9's).\n> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-10. This is SH-10's first dev iteration.\n> `dev-rerun-count.json` was left untouched (engine-owned).\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)\n\nAll 23 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in\n`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 51 matrix paths were verified on disk.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma schema + migration 20261110000000_add_quizzes (partial unique index) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: Pure grading core grading.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Student serializers + no-`correct`-key unit test — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: quiz.published / quiz.results_released types + 'quiz' file context — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: access.ts assertCanAccessAttempt — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: attempt-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: quiz-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: analytics.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: maintenance.ts + dispatch route wiring — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Quiz & question CRUD route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: Regrade / release / analytics / accommodation routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Attempt route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: Integration tests (attempts, regrade) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: Course Quizzes tab, list page, view, new page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: Quiz player, take page, useAutosave — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: QuestionList + QuestionEditor — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: Builder shell (edit page, QuizBuilder, QuizSettingsPanel) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Attempt result page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Manual grading page + workspace — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: Analytics page + x-charts BarChart — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: Seed: three quizzes (FR-36) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: Playwright e2e quizzes.spec.ts — ✓ complete\n\n### Verification\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm run lint` | ✔ no warnings/errors |\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | ✔ clean |\n| `tests/unit/quiz/*` (validators, grading, serializers) | 37/37 pass |\n| `tests/integration/quiz/*` against Postgres (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`) | 8/8 pass; rerun 6× to shake out races (see bug 1 below) |\n| Full `vitest run` | 361/366. The 5–6 failures are the **same pre-existing ones recorded in the SH-9 QA report** (attendance-qa FR-22 / FR-10, auth-forms, useToast, lockout under Node 24, auth rate-limit flake). None import quiz code. |\n| `next build` | ✔ (the \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines are pre-existing static-render noise from other routes) |\n| `tests/e2e/quizzes.spec.ts` on a prod build (port 3100) | 4/4 pass on two consecutive runs. A third back-to-back run fails at `signInAs` because the 10-per-IP login rate limiter trips — helper limitation, not quiz code. |\n| Seed | Verified against temporary MATH-7A / ENG-7A fixtures: creates Fractions Check (8 q, CLOSED, every enrolled student GRADED), Unit 1 Test (12 q incl. 2 essays, AFTER_CLOSE, open 3 days, no attempts), Parts of Speech (5 q, practice, 3 attempts, HIGHEST). A rerun creates 0 (idempotent). Fixtures removed afterwards. The dev DB has no courses, so `npm run db:seed` skips quizzes with a message, same as the assignments seed. |\n\n### Bugs found and fixed during verification\n1. **Concurrent start → false \"attempts used up\" (FR-19).** Tab B could miss tab A's attempt in its in-progress check, then count it and hit the attempt limit. `startOrResumeAttempt` now re-checks for an IN_PROGRESS attempt before refusing.\n2. **Reload inside the 800 ms debounce lost the last answer (FR-15/FR-19, AC-2).** `useAutosave` now writes each change to `localStorage['quiz-attempt:<id>']` immediately and removes it on a 2xx. The pill shows \"Saving…\" during the debounce, and \"Offline\" only after a send has failed. Before this, \"All answers saved\" appeared while the debounce was still pending. Caught by the e2e reload step.\n3. **DecimalError 500 on non-numeric points.** zod runs chained `.refine`s even after one fails, so `dec('')` threw. `halfStep` in `validators/quiz.ts` is now a single short-circuiting `superRefine`, with a regression test. Caught by the e2e grading step.\n4. **Save-status chip contrast.** The theme's `success` chip measured 3.53:1 (axe, serious). The pill is now an outlined default-colour chip with Cloud icons.\n\n### Decisions / deviations (for QA)\n- **Migration generation:** `prisma migrate dev --create-only` failed because the DB role can't create a shadow database. The SQL came from `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` against the up-to-date DB instead. The raw partial unique index was appended, and the migration was applied with `migrate deploy`; there was no `db push` (ADR-2). The post-apply diff is empty.\n- **NOT_FOUND hiding (NFR-5):** `course-access.ts` throws FORBIDDEN, so `quiz/access.ts` wraps it (`viewCourseOrNotFound` / `manageCourseOrNotFound`) and maps it to NOT_FOUND for every quiz resource.\n- **Lazy auto-submit uses the 30 s grace** (`deadlineAt + ANSWER_GRACE_MS`), the same as the maintenance sweep. A GET inside the grace window therefore doesn't race the client's final save.\n- **Edit lock compares values, not keys:** the builder sends the whole question, so the lock only rejects keys whose values actually changed.\n- **Prompt images (FR-39):** they are uploaded with context `'quiz'` and embedded as `![](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. On question save, the service attaches the referenced unattached `quiz` files the caller owns (contextId = quizId), so `quizResolver` controls who can read them.\n- **Accommodations table and analytics per-question table use MUI `Table`, not the shared `DataTable`.** DataTable is URL-paginated and server-driven, and these are small in-memory lists that need editable cells. Both are documented MUI components (NFR-4).\n- **Extra service exports beyond the plan's lists** (all in owned files): `listManagerAttempts`, `listOwnAttempts`, `listAccommodations`, `getAttemptView`, `submitForStudent`, `ensureQuizAttemptsNotExpired`, `notifyResultsReleased`, and manager serializers (`toManagerQuestion/Answer/Attempt`). These are what the server pages need. No new files or dependencies were added.\n- **Attempt ids** are cuid-shaped (`c` + base36 time + 16 hex chars) and generated up front for the shuffle seed. No cuid package is installed (marked with a `ponytail:` comment).\n- **mui-mcp (ADR-7):** reachable. Docs fetched: x-charts Bars (first x-charts use), RadioGroup, LinearProgress, Tooltip. The other components follow the usage already established in the codebase.\n- **E2E:** the window, title and visibility are set through Prisma after `/new` creates the draft, because the DateTimePicker is fiddly to drive. Questions, publish, take, reload, submit and grading all go through the UI. The axe scan is scoped to `<main>`, because the app-shell sidebar `<ul>` has a pre-existing `list` violation.\n\n### Observed, not in SH-10 scope\n- `renderEmail` (PRD-04) sometimes emits NUL bytes in react-email's preview padding. Postgres then rejects the `EmailOutbox` insert (`22021`). `notify()` logs and swallows the error, so in-app notifications still land. This appeared in integration runs for `quiz.results_released` emails.\n- `validators/assignments.ts` `decimal()` uses the same chained-refine pattern as bug 3, so it probably throws a DecimalError on non-numeric input too.\n- The app-shell sidebar has an axe `list` violation (serious).\n- `saveAnswer` vs submit race: an upsert landing after the submit claim is left ungraded until a Regrade. Marked with a `ponytail:` comment.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-10\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T14:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"completed\": [\n    \"TASK-1\",\n    \"TASK-2\",\n    \"TASK-3\",\n    \"TASK-4\",\n    \"TASK-5\",\n    \"TASK-6\",\n    \"TASK-7\",\n    \"TASK-8\",\n    \"TASK-9\",\n    \"TASK-10\",\n    \"TASK-11\",\n    \"TASK-12\",\n    \"TASK-13\",\n    \"TASK-14\",\n    \"TASK-15\",\n    \"TASK-16\",\n    \"TASK-17\",\n    \"TASK-18\",\n    \"TASK-19\",\n    \"TASK-20\",\n    \"TASK-21\",\n    \"TASK-22\",\n    \"TASK-23\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-10\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T07:52:39.548Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"count\": 1,\n  \"firstPassAccepted\": true\n}# QA Report — SH-10 (PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-10\n- timestamp: 2026-11-09T07:57:09Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 49\n- requirementsPassed: 47\n- requirementsFailed: 2\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-9 QA report.\n> **All 39 functional requirements PASS. The feature works end to end.**\n> Two non-functional requirements FAIL, and neither is a feature defect:\n> - **NFR-7:** two new `console.log` calls in the quiz seed (`prisma/seed.ts:463`, `:526`). The fix is to change them to `logger.info`, which the file already imports.\n> - **NFR-8:** the full `npm run test` run is still not green. It has the **same 6 failing tests that were already failing before SH-10** (the SH-9 report lists them). None of them import quiz code.\n>\n> The verdict is consistent with SH-9, where the same two kinds of finding also produced FAIL. The feature is ready for review once the 2-line seed fix lands and the pre-existing failures are accepted as known or fixed separately.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n### 1. The build and tests run, and every quiz test is green\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npx prisma migrate status` | ✅ 11 migrations, schema up to date (incl. `20261110000000_add_quizzes`) |\n| `npm run lint` | ✅ no warnings/errors |\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | ✅ clean (incl. the new QA test) |\n| Quiz unit + integration (`tests/unit/quiz`, `tests/integration/quiz`) | ✅ **53/53**: 37 unit, 8 dev integration, 8 new QA integration |\n| E2E `tests/e2e/quizzes.spec.ts` (QA rerun on `next start -p 3100`) | ✅ **4/4** (build → publish → take with reload → grade essay → see results) |\n| Full `vitest run` | ⚠️ 360/366. 6 failures, all pre-existing (see below) |\n\n### 2. Full-suite failures are pre-existing and do not touch quiz code\n| Failing test | Status before SH-10 |\n|---|---|\n| `attendance-qa.test.ts` FR-22, FR-10/FR-19 | Listed in the SH-9 report (time-of-day / attendance service) |\n| `auth.test.ts` rate limit | Listed in SH-9 (flaky) |\n| `auth-forms.test.tsx`, `useToast.test.tsx` | Listed in SH-9 |\n| `lockout.test.ts` | Listed in SH-9 (next-auth ESM resolution under Node 24) |\n| `email-dispatch.test.ts` AC-4 (concurrent dispatchers) | Flaky when run alongside other DB suites. Passed **3/3** when run alone. It tests `server/email/dispatch`, which SH-10 did not change; SH-10 only added two try/catch'd calls in the dispatch *route*. |\n\n### 3. Dev's self-reported completion matches the code\n- All 51 paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist and contain real implementations.\n- There are no `TODO` or `FIXME` markers and no stub functions in the quiz code.\n- The two `ponytail:` notes in `attempt-service.ts` are documented trade-offs, not missing features: a hand-rolled cuid-shaped id, and a rare save-vs-submit race that a Regrade fixes.\n- All 23 tasks are marked complete, and each maps to the code that implements it.\n\n### 4. New QA tests (`tests/integration/quiz/qa-sh10.test.ts`, 8 tests) fill the gaps in dev's coverage\n- **NFR-1:** asserts that the JSON from the student `getQuiz`, the in-progress attempt and the pre-release result never contains `\"correct\"`, `\"explanation\"` or the explanation text. Manager `getQuiz` does include them.\n- **FR-11 / FR-31:** the course list is shaped by role (manager / student / parent). Drafts are hidden from students. A student outside the course and a teacher of another course get NOT_FOUND. A quiz with no attempts can be deleted.\n- **FR-26 / FR-27:** checks the analytics summary (avg / median / high / low), the 10-bucket histogram, the option distribution, the most-chosen wrong option, and the CSV header and rows. Non-managers get NOT_FOUND.\n- **FR-34 / NFR-5:** a parent sees a linked child's result only after release. An unlinked parent, another student and another teacher get NOT_FOUND. Cross-student autosave and cross-course grading are refused.\n- **FR-28 / FR-38:** extra time feeds the deadline (10 + 15 = 25 min). An accommodation for a student not enrolled in the course gets NOT_FOUND. Accommodation, grade, regrade and release each write an `AuditLog` row.\n- **FR-31:** reorder rejects a partial or duplicate id list.\n- **NFR-2:** the median of 50 concurrent saves is under 50 ms. Saves are upserts: 2 rows after 51 saves.\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | `prisma/schema.prisma` (5 enums, 5 models, back-relations); `prisma/migrations/20261110000000_add_quizzes/migration.sql`; `migrate status` up to date; all integration tests use the models |\n| FR-2 | PASS | `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`; `tests/unit/quiz/quiz-validators.test.ts` (window, 1–300, 1–10, 0.5–100, 2–8 options, 1–10 accepted, 10,000 chars, accommodation limits) |\n| FR-3 | PASS | `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`; `grading.test.ts` \"MULTIPLE_CHOICE partial credit — FR-2 example\" ({A,B}=0, {A}=2), SINGLE_CHOICE/TF all-or-nothing |\n| FR-4 | PASS | `grading.test.ts` \"SHORT_ANSWER normalises; ' Photosynthesis ' is correct\"; `needsReview` test; override in `regrade.test.ts` |\n| FR-5 | PASS | `grading.test.ts` \"ESSAY is manual\"; guidance in `correct.guidance` (`regrade.test.ts`) |\n| FR-6 | PASS | `edit/QuizSettingsPanel.tsx`; time-limit ≤ window rule in `quiz-validators.test.ts` \"rejects a time limit longer than the window\" |\n| FR-7 | PASS | `edit/QuestionList.tsx` (dnd-kit `useSortable`, Duplicate, Delete), `edit/QuestionEditor.tsx` (per-type editors); e2e adds 4 question types; server reorder tested in `qa-sh10.test.ts` |\n| FR-8 | PASS | `edit/QuizBuilder.tsx` L112 (running points total), L115/187 (Preview as student, `QuizPlayer mode='preview'` skips saves, L259/279) |\n| FR-9 | PASS | `grading.test.ts` \"canPublish\"; `regrade.test.ts` (publish with 0 questions → VALIDATION_ERROR) |\n| FR-10 | PASS | `regrade.test.ts` (edit lock: add/delete/points/essay-correct → CONFLICT; accepted answers editable; regrade keeps manual grades) |\n| FR-11 | PASS | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` L18; `CourseQuizzesView.tsx`; `qa-sh10.test.ts` role-shaped list test |\n| FR-12 | PASS | `take/page.tsx` + `QuizPlayer.tsx` start screen (time limit, attempts, confirm dialog L128); e2e student step |\n| FR-13 | PASS | `grading.test.ts` \"computeDeadline\" (AC-1) + \"seededShuffle\"; `serializers.test.ts` frozen order and seeded option shuffle |\n| FR-14 | PASS | `QuizPlayer.tsx` (RadioGroup/Checkbox/TextField, LinearProgress L332, navigator L336, sticky header L308, red timer under 2 min L319) |\n| FR-15 | PASS | `take/useAutosave.ts` (800 ms debounce, localStorage queue, 5 s retry); status pill labels `QuizPlayer.tsx` L221; e2e reload mid-attempt keeps answers |\n| FR-16 | PASS | `attempts.test.ts` \"autosave within grace succeeds; after deadline + 30 s it is 409 and the attempt is auto-submitted\" |\n| FR-17 | PASS | `regrade.test.ts` (essay → NEEDS_GRADING); `attempts.test.ts` double submit; unanswered count `QuizPlayer.tsx` L301 |\n| FR-18 | PASS | `attempts.test.ts` \"GET auto-submits an expired attempt\" + maintenance auto-submit test |\n| FR-19 | PASS | `attempts.test.ts` \"resume returns the same attempt; concurrent starts produce one attempt\"; e2e reload |\n| FR-20 | PASS | `grading.test.ts` \"resultsVisible\"; `regrade.test.ts` manual release (idempotent); `qa-sh10.test.ts` parent hidden until release |\n| FR-21 | PASS | `serializers.test.ts` (score, percent, correct + exp