{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014YqWK8JuW4xvsDAEYVPrKG","type":"tool_result","content":"FR-9 {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Build the /messages inbox: two panes, collapsing to a single pane with back navigation below 768px. The conversation list is sorted by lastMessageAt and shows participant names or subject, a 'sender: text' preview, time and an unread badge. It has search by participant name/subject and Inbox/Archived tabs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\"}\n\nFR-10 {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Build the message thread: sender avatar and name, timestamps grouped by day (school timezone), attachments via FileList, an 'edited' marker, deleted messages shown as 'This message was deleted', and upward infinite scroll at 30 messages per page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\"}\n\nFR-13 {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Polling: the visible active thread polls GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?after=<lastId> every 5s. The conversation list and the sidebar unread badge poll every 30s.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criterion 8\"}\n\nFR-14 {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Opening a thread updates lastReadAt. A per-conversation menu offers mute, archive/unarchive (per user), view participants, and leave group. The creator of a group that contains students cannot leave it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\"}\n\nFR-18 {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar 'Messages' entry with an unread count for all roles in src/config/navigation.ts, backed by GET /api/messaging/unread-count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table\"}\n\nFR-22 {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Any participant can report a message with a reason (max 1,000 chars) via POST /api/messages/:id/report. The reporter sees 'Reported \\u2014 the school will review this.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; FR-1 MessageReport.reason comment\"}\n\nFR-23 {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/safeguarding Reports queue (ADMIN with isSafeguardingLead only, others get 403). Open reports come first, each with the message, context of 5 messages before and after, and participants. Actions: Mark reviewed (with note) and Dismiss.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\"}\n\nFR-24 {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Build the safeguarding Conversations search: lists conversations with involvesStudent = true, filterable by participant and date, with a read-only view that includes deleted content and the original text of edited messages.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\"}\n\n['NFR-1: Security: every messaging and safeguarding endpoint and server page checks participation, role or isSafeguardingLead on ', 'NFR-2: Performance: polling endpoints respond in under 100 ms using the (conversationId, createdAt) index and return empty arra', 'NFR-3: Retention: users never hard-delete messages. Soft-deleted content and edit revisions stay available to safeguarding.', 'NFR-4: Rate limit: POST /api/conversations/:id/messages allows 30 messages/min/user and returns 429 RATE_LIMITED beyond that (r', 'NFR-5: UI component rule: every visible element uses only MUI (@mui/material v9, icons-material, MUI X packages), looked up thr', 'NFR-6: Conventions: thin Zod-validated handlers (src/lib/validators/messaging.ts), services in src/server/messaging/, standard ', 'NFR-7: Responsive: below 768 px the inbox switches to a single pane with back navigation.', 'NFR-8: Near-real-time: a message sent in one browser appears in another open thread within 6 seconds via polling. No websockets', 'NFR-9: Scope guard: no voice/video, typing indicators, reactions, E2E encryption, websockets or broadcast messaging. Do not mod', 'NFR-10: Tests: unit tests for the full contact-rule matrix (groups, ended relationships); integration tests for notification col', 'NFR-11: Mutations on records owned by someone else (e.g. safeguarding review of reports) write an AuditLog row via audit().']","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b6c7657-2cc6-421d-a978-c6af55a2d9a6","uuid":"ef417203-a6b5-4850-8b71-5b88e95a438b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:19:42.106Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FR-9 {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Build the /messages inbox: two panes, collapsing to a single pane with back navigation below 768px. The conversation list is sorted by lastMessageAt and shows participant names or subject, a 'sender: text' preview, time and an unread badge. It has search by participant name/subject and Inbox/Archived tabs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\"}\n\nFR-10 {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Build the message thread: sender avatar and name, timestamps grouped by day (school timezone), attachments via FileList, an 'edited' marker, deleted messages shown as 'This message was deleted', and upward infinite scroll at 30 messages per page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\"}\n\nFR-13 {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Polling: the visible active thread polls GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?after=<lastId> every 5s. The conversation list and the sidebar unread badge poll every 30s.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criterion 8\"}\n\nFR-14 {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Opening a thread updates lastReadAt. A per-conversation menu offers mute, archive/unarchive (per user), view participants, and leave group. The creator of a group that contains students cannot leave it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\"}\n\nFR-18 {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar 'Messages' entry with an unread count for all roles in src/config/navigation.ts, backed by GET /api/messaging/unread-count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table\"}\n\nFR-22 {\"id\": \"FR-2