ary script covers the safeguarding drawer and a student conversation with edited and deleted messages.\n- **Fixtures:** tagged `uiv-sh13*`:\n  - a safeguarding-lead admin and a non-lead admin\n  - a teacher, and a parent linked to student 1\n  - 2 students and 1 course\n- **Viewports:** 1280×800 and 375×667. DB state was checked after mutations. All fixtures were removed (0 remaining).\n- **Design reference:** `figma-readiness.json` does not exist, so the comparison is against `requirements.json` only.\n\n## Findings\n\n| Req | Surface | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FR-9 | `/messages` inbox | PASS | Two panes, Inbox/Archived tabs, search and an empty state. Rows show avatar, subject, relative time and a \"Pam: …\" preview. Unread rows are bold (700) with a count badge. (UIV-4) |\n| FR-10 | Message thread | PASS | Avatar, name and time on each message. Day divider in the school timezone (America/New_York). FileList attachment, \"(edited)\" and *This message was deleted* all render. Infinite scroll not exercised (UIV-6). |\n| FR-11 | Composer | PASS | Enter sends and Shift+Enter adds a newline. The counter \"4600 / 5000\" appears past 4,500. Send is disabled at 5,001. Attach files works (\"0 / 5\" indicator), and the attachment is delivered. |\n| FR-12 | New-message dialog | PASS | Grouped \"To\" picker, optional subject and a message field. Send closes the dialog and navigates to the new thread. |\n| FR-8 | Contact groups | PASS | Parent sees \"My child's teachers (Sam)\" and \"School office\". Student sees \"My teachers\" and \"School office\". Another student isn't offered (\"No one you can message matches\"). Student-to-student API create returns 403. |\n| FR-6 | Staff-created group | PASS | A student can reply in a teacher-created group. |\n| FR-7 | Ended relationship | PASS | A dropped student sees an info Alert, \"You can no longer send messages in this conversation.\". The API returns 403. The teacher can still send. |\n| FR-13 | Thread polling | PASS | The new message appeared in the other open thread after about 5.35 s. |\n| FR-14 | Conversation menu | PASS | Mute adds a bell-off icon and changes the menu item to \"Unmute\". Archive moves the conversation to the Archived tab; Unarchive works. The Participants dialog shows role chips. Opening the thread sets `lastReadAt` and clears the badge. (UIV-3, UIV-5) |\n| FR-14 | Leave group | PASS | Confirm dialog, then the conversation leaves the list. Reopening it gives 404. The creator of a group with students isn't offered \"Leave group\". |\n| FR-15 | Edit/delete own message | PASS | Inline edit shows \"(edited)\". Delete has a confirm dialog and leaves the deleted placeholder. Messages older than 15 minutes have no options button, and a late PATCH returns 403. |\n| FR-16 | Student page actions | PASS | Teacher: \"Message parents\" opens the dialog prefilled with Pam Parent. Parent: \"Message teacher\" is limited to the \"My child's teachers (Sam)\" group. |\n| FR-17 | Roster selection | PASS | The button is disabled until a student is selected. Select all prefills both students. The new group has 3 participants and `involvesStudent=true`. |\n| FR-18 | Sidebar Messages and badge | PASS | Shown for all roles at 1280 px and in the 375 px nav. The badge appears for unread conversations and clears after reading. |\n| FR-21 | Quiet hours | PASS | Start/End time fields with a timezone hint. 22:00–07:00 (wrapping past midnight) saves and persists. No horizontal scroll at 375 px. |\n| FR-22 | Report message | PASS | Reason dialog, then the toast \"Reported — the school will review this.\". No Report option on your own messages. |\n| FR-23 | Safeguarding reports queue | PASS | The lead sees the nav entry and the OPEN report. The drawer shows the reason, participants and ±5 messages of context with the reported message highlighted. \"Mark reviewed\" requires a note, and the status changes to REVIEWED. A non-lead admin gets no nav entry, `/forbidden` and an API 403. |\n| FR-23 | Report drawer header | **FAIL** | **UIV-1:** the title and Close button are hidden under the AppBar. |\n| FR-24 | Safeguarding conversations | PASS | Participant and date filters. Only conversations with a student are listed. The read-only view has no composer and shows deleted bodies (with a \"Deleted\" chip), an \"Edited\" chip and \"Earlier versions\" with the original text. |\n| FR-25 | View audit | PASS | Each view writes a `safeguarding.conversation.view` audit row. |\n| FR-26 | Lead notification | PASS | The lead's bell shows an unread badge after the report. |\n| FR-2 | Admin user form flag | BLOCKED | No admin user form exists (ADR-11, accepted at intake), so there was no UI to render. QA verified the flag via `PATCH /api/users/:id`. |\n| NFR-7 | < 768 px single pane | PASS | At 375 px the list and the thread show one at a time, the back arrow returns to the list, and there is no horizontal scroll. |\n| NFR-5 | MUI-only | PASS | Every rendered surface uses MUI components. |\n| NFR-8 | Near-real-time | PASS | About 5.35 s via polling. |\n\n## Evidence\n\nAll files are in `screenshots/`:\n\n- **Parent:**\n  - `parent-messages-empty-1280`\n  - `parent-new-message-{contacts,filled}-1280`\n  - `parent-after-send-1280`\n  - `parent-composer-counter-1280`\n  - `parent-thread-attachment-1280`\n  - `parent-delete-confirm-1280`\n  - `parent-thread-edited-deleted-1280`\n  - `parent-student-message-teacher-1280`\n  - `parent-quiet-hours-{1280,375}`\n- **Teacher:**\n  - `teacher-inbox-unread-1280`\n  - `teacher-thread-1280`\n  - `teacher-report-dialog-1280`\n  - `teacher-reported-toast-1280`\n  - `teacher-conversation-menu-1280`\n  - `teacher-after-mute-1280`\n  - `teacher-participants-1280`\n  - `teacher-archived-tab-1280`\n  - `teacher-roster-{selected,dialog}-1280`\n  - `teacher-student-message-parents-1280`\n- **Student:**\n  - `student-new-message-contacts-375`\n  - `student-inbox-375`\n  - `student-thread-375`\n  - `student-leave-confirm-375`\n  - `student-left-not-found-375`\n  - `student-relationship-ended-1280`\n- **Safeguarding lead:**\n  - `lead-safeguarding-reports-1280`\n  - `lead-report-drawer-1280`\n  - `lead-report-drawer-student-1280` (UIV-1)\n  - `lead-report-reviewed-1280`\n  - `lead-safeguarding-conversations-1280`\n  - `lead-safeguarding-conversation-view-1280`\n  - `lead-safeguarding-student-view-1280`\n  - `lead-reported-conversation-view-1280`\n- **Non-lead admin:** `admin-nonlead-safeguarding-1280`\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":99,"newStart":1,"newLines":126,"lines":["-# UI Verification Report — SH-11 (PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards)","+# UI Verification Report — SH-13 (PRD-13 Direct Messaging)"," ","-- **Ticket:** SH-11","-- **Timestamp:** 2026-11-09T15:23:52Z","+- **Ticket:** SH-13"," - **Status:** complete","-- **Result:** 34 findings across 31 UI-facing requirements: **32 PASS, 2 FAIL, 0 BLOCKED**","+- **Result:** 25 findings: **23 PASS, 1 FAIL, 1 BLOCKED**"," ","-> This file replaces the stale SH-10 report. `ui-verification-report.json` has the same findings in machine-readable form, and `uiv-raw.json` has the raw probe output.","+> This replaces the stale SH-11 report and screenshots, which are still in git history. `ui-verification-report.json` has the same findings in machine-readable form, and `uiv-raw.json` has the raw probe output."," "," ## Headline"," ","-Every SH-11 surface rendered and behaved as specified. That covers the gradebook grid, settings, dialogs, column menu, CSV export, student/parent grades, the admin and homeroom report-card flows, the print views and access control. The FR-15 golden case renders **78.0% C+**.","+Every SH-13 surface rendered and behaved as specified:"," ","-Two visual defects need fixing:","+- the inbox, thread and composer","+- the new-message dialog and its contact groups","+- editing, deleting and reporting messages","+- mute, archive, view participants and leave group","+- the actions on the student page and the course roster","+- quiet hours","+- the 375 px single-pane layout","+- the safeguarding reports and conversations views"," ","-| ID | Severity | Surface | Problem | Suggested fix |","+A message sent in one browser appeared in the other browser's open thread in about **5.35 s**, within the 6 s limit.","+","+One visual defect needs fixing:","+","+| ID | Severity | Surface | Problem | Fix |"," |---|---|---|---|---|","-| **UIV-1** | moderate | Report card on-screen view at 375 px (`/report-cards/[id]/print`) | The Courses table is wider than the card. The Grade and Comment columns spill past the card border and the page scrolls horizontally. Students and parents open this page from their phones. A4 printing is unaffected. | Wrap the table in `TableContainer` (`overflowX: auto`) or stack the columns below `sm` in `ReportCardDocument.tsx` |","-| **UIV-2** | minor | Gradebook settings → Grading scale | The Select renders **blank** when the course uses the school default (`scaleId ''`). The \"School default (Standard A–F)\" option exists but isn't displayed, because MUI Select hides an empty value without `displayEmpty`. | `slotProps={{ select: { displayEmpty: true }, inputLabel: { shrink: true } }}` in `GradebookSettingsClient.tsx` |","+| **UIV-1** | moderate | `/admin/safeguarding` report drawer | The right-hand Drawer (z-index 1200) opens **under** the fixed AppBar (z-index drawer+1). The drawer's header, with the \"Report\" title and the **Close button**, is covered and can't be clicked: `elementFromPoint` returns the app bar and the click times out. Users can only close the drawer with Esc or a backdrop click. | Add `sx={{ zIndex: (t) => t.zIndex.modal }}` to the `<Drawer>` in `src/components/messaging/SafeguardingReports.tsx:181` |"," "," ## Minor observations"," ","-- **UIV-3 (a11y):** the invalid \"Weights total 90 / 100\" chip is pale red on pale red and nearly unreadable. axe reports color-contrast (serious) ×2. The red helper text next to Save still explains the problem.","-- **UIV-4 (a11y/layout):** at 375 px, the expanded `/grades` item table puts % and Comment off-screen in a scroll region that can't take keyboard focus. axe reports scrollable-region-focusable (serious).","-- **UIV-5:** axe reports empty-table-header (minor) on the DataGrids. This is the same pattern seen in SH-10.","-- **UIV-6 (not exercised in the UI; QA tests cover them):**","-  - arrow-key cell navigation","-  - a quiz-synced cell opening its attempt","-  - virtualisation at 60×120 and the NFR-2 timings","-  - DRAFT-only regeneration (FR-31)","-  - the roster's grade-level filter","-  - the `grade.posted` notification","-  - the green (≥80) card colour","-- **ENV-1:** the dev DB's current year (2026-2027) has **no terms**, so the feature is unusable in dev until an admin adds them. In that state the gradebook shows a clear info Alert. Verification used a temporary tagged term.","-- **ENV-2 (for QA/dev, not UI):** 9 orphaned `TermGradeOverride` rows predate this phase. Their courses were deleted, but the rows remain because the model has no FK to Course and `tests/e2e/report-cards.spec.ts` cleanup doesn't delete overrides. They were left in place.","+- **UIV-2 (a11y):** axe flags `list` (serious) on `/messages` and `/account/notifications`. `ListItemButton` renders as an `<a>` directly inside a `<ul>`. It also flags `heading-order` and `region` (moderate); `region` is an app-wide pattern. One run showed `color-contrast` ×1 on `/admin/safeguarding`.","+- **UIV-3 (a11y):** the muted icon in a conversation row has `aria-label=\"Muted\"`, but MUI's SvgIcon sets `aria-hidden` unless `titleAccess` is set, so screen readers never hear about it. Use `titleAccess=\"Muted\"` instead.","+- **UIV-4:** when the last message in a conversation is deleted, the list preview reads \"This message was deleted\" with no `sender:` prefix. Product should confirm whether that's intended.","+- **UIV-5:** the \"Conversation muted\" toast didn't appear while an earlier toast was still on screen. The mute itself succeeded.","+- **UIV-6 (not exercised in the UI; QA covers these at service level):**","+  - upward infinite scroll at 30 messages per page","+  - the 30 s list/badge poll timing","+  - the error shown at the 25-participant cap","+  - deferred email (FR-20)","+- **ENV-1:** the production CSP (`script-src 'self'`) blocks Next's inline hydration scripts under `next start`, so no client UI hydrates. This predates SH-13 (ADR-4), and the existing E2E specs use `bypassCSP`, as this run did. Production still needs a nonce.","+- **ENV-2:** the in-memory per-IP login rate limit forced a server restart between driver runs. This is expected behaviour."," "," ## Method"," ","-- Production build (`npm run build`, exit 0) served by `next start -p 3300` against Postgres :5433. The :3000/:3001 servers were left alone.","-- Throwaway Playwright driver `/tmp/uiv-sh11/driver.cjs`, outside the repo, with tagged fixtures `uiv-sh11`:","-  - users: an admin, a homeroom teacher, 2 section students, an outsider student, and a parent linked to both students","-  - courses: UIV Maths (Homework 40 / Exams 60, with manual items, a hidden item and a late synced assignment) and UIV English (no categories)","-  - a temporary term","-- Viewports: teacher/admin at 1280×800, student/parent at 375×667, plus cross-checks at the other width. Print media was emulated and PDFs were rendered to check A4 size and page count.","-- DB state was checked after each mutation.","-- The nav probe `/tmp/uiv-sh11/nav.cjs` confirmed sidebar entries per role.","-- All fixtures were removed (verified: 0 tagged users, courses, terms or sections remain).","-- The only console errors were the expected 404s from the access-denial checks.","-- `figma-readiness.json` does not exist, so the comparison is against `requirements.json` only.","+- **Build and server:** `npm run build` (exit 0), served with `next start -p 3300` against Postgres :5433. The :3000 and :3001 servers were left alone.","+- **Drivers:** throwaway Playwright scripts outside the repo: `/tmp/uiv-sh13/driver.cjs` and `supp.cjs`. The supplementary script covers the safeguarding drawer and a student conversation with edited and deleted messages.","+- **Fixtures:** tagged `uiv-sh13*`:","+  - a safeguarding-lead admin and a non-lead admin","+  - a teacher, and a parent linked to student 1","+  - 2 students and 1 course","+- **Viewports:** 1280×800 and 375×667. DB state was checked after mutations. All fixtures were removed (0 remaining).","+- **Design reference:** `figma-readiness.json` does not exist, so the comparison is against `requirements.json` only."," "," ## Findings"," "," | Req | Surface | Verdict | Notes |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| FR-2 | Assignment and quiz editor category select | PASS | None / Homework / Exams. The saved value displays. |","-| FR-9 | Synced vs manual cells | PASS | Synced cells aren't editable. The API rejects a synced score edit (400 \"Only the comment can be changed here…\"). |","-| FR-14 | Letter-only override | PASS | `78.0% B *`. Percent kept, letter B, comment saved. |","-| FR-15 | Golden case | PASS | 18/20 + 9/10 (HW 40%) and 70/100 (Exams 60%) give 90.0 / 70.0 → **78.0% C+**. The student view shows the same percent. |","-| FR-16 | `/admin/grading-scales` | PASS | Default chip, 12-band editor. Inline errors \"Letters must be unique\" and \"Must be lower than the band above\". Create and delete work. Deleting the default is disabled. Admin nav entries are present. |","-| FR-17 | Gradebook settings | **FAIL** | The live weight sum works, Save is disabled at 90, and the API returns 400. **UIV-2:** the scale select is blank. UIV-3: low-contrast chip. |","-| FR-18 | Gradebook grid | PASS | Category column groups and Averages group. Headers show icon, title, due date and /max. Hidden items are dimmed with an eye-off icon. Bold Term column, sorted by last name, no pinned columns. The grid scrolls horizontally at 375 and the page does not. |","-| FR-19 | Cell rendering | PASS | Score, `EX`, red bold `M`, `—`, and a clock icon on the late synced score. |","-| FR-20 | Keyboard editing | PASS | Digits+Enter, E, M and Delete each save with a PUT. 6 `grade.update` audit rows. Out-of-range input gives a red outline and a toast, and nothing is saved. |","-| FR-21 | Synced cell click | PASS | Opens `/assignments/<id>/grade?studentId=…`. |","-| FR-22 | Add manual item | PASS | Title, Category, Max points, Date, Term. Required validation works. The new column appears right away. |","-| FR-23 | Override dialog | PASS | Percent, Letter, Teacher comment. Saving shows a toast and `*` in the Term cell. |","-| FR-24 | Column menu | PASS | Hide/Show (eye-off icon, `isVisible` toggled), Set ungraded to missing (→ M, term 32.0% F, correct), Item statistics (avg/median/high/low). |","-| FR-25 | Export CSV | PASS | `text/csv` attachment that matches the grid, including EX, M and the override letter. |","-| FR-26 | Student Grades tab | PASS | Course cards with red (50.0 F) and amber (78.0 B) chips. The expanded view shows category subtotals and the item table. The hidden item is absent. (UIV-4) |","-| FR-27 | `/grades` + nav | PASS | Parent child selector switches between children. The \"Grades\" nav entry is present for STUDENT and PARENT at 1280 and 375. |","-| FR-28 | Course Grades tab (student) | PASS | Only that course's card. No Gradebook or Attendance tabs. |","-| FR-29 | Admin report-cards roster | PASS | Term, grade-level and section filters. Status chips and warning text. Count buttons. axe clean. |","-| FR-30 | Generate drafts / snapshot | PASS | All required fields render, including attendance and the scale legend. No logo because `logoUrl` is null. |","-| FR-31 | Regeneration | PASS | Confirm copy and published snapshots checked. Draft refresh after grade edits wasn't re-driven in the UI. |","-| FR-32 | Review page | PASS | Homeroom teacher can edit only the homeroom comment. Admin can edit both. Saves persist. The teacher has no publish controls. |","-| FR-33 | `/report-cards` homeroom list | PASS | TEACHER nav entry. Lists section drafts with warnings. |","-| FR-34 | Publish / Unpublish | PASS | Single and bulk publish. Unpublish requires a reason and writes an audit row. Notifications go to students and the parent. |","-| FR-35 | Print views | PASS | Letterhead, tables, signature lines. Chrome and the print button are hidden under print media. A4 portrait, 1 page per card. Print all: 2 pages with a page break. |","-| FR-35 | On-screen card at 375 | **FAIL** | **UIV-1:** the table overflows the card and the page. |","-| FR-36 | Student Report cards tab | PASS | Draft hidden (\"No report cards yet\"). Once published, listed with a link to the print view. |","-| FR-37 | Access control | PASS | Own draft → 404. Outsider → 404 on the page and the API. Parent and teacher allowed. |","-| FR-42 | Student grades API | PASS | Hidden item absent from the API and UI. The outsider gets 404. |","-| NFR-5 | Privacy | PASS | Same evidence as FR-37 and FR-42. |","-| NFR-7 | MUI-only UI | PASS | All surfaces use MUI components. No raw unstyled HTML seen. |","-| NFR-8 | DataGrid MIT tier | PASS | Column groups and editing only. No pinned columns, no Pro watermark. |","-| NFR-11 | Print layout | PASS | A4 portrait PDFs: `screenshots/parent-report-card.pdf` and `screenshots/print-all.pdf`. |","-| FR-26 | `/grades` table at 375 | PASS | Minor observation UIV-4 (scroll region not keyboard-focusable). |","-| FR-18 | Gradebook with no terms | PASS | ENV-1: info Alert instead of a crash. |","+| FR-9 | `/messages` inbox | PASS | Two panes, Inbox/Archived tabs, search and an empty state. Rows show avatar, subject, relative time and a \"Pam: …\" preview. Unread rows are bold (700) with a count badge. (UIV-4) |","+| FR-10 | Message thread | PASS | Avatar, name and time on each message. Day divider in the school timezone (America/New_York). FileList attachment, \"(edited)\" and *This message was deleted* all render. Infinite scroll not exercised (UIV-6). |","+| FR-11 | Composer | PASS | Enter sends and Shift+Enter adds a newline. The counter \"4600 / 5000\" appears past 4,500. Send is disabled at 5,001. Attach files works (\"0 / 5\" indicator), and the attachment is delivered. |","+| FR-12 | New-message dialog | PASS | Grouped \"To\" picker, optional subject and a message field. Send closes the dialog and navigates to the new thread. |","+| FR-8 | Contact groups | PASS | Parent sees \"My child's teachers (Sam)\" and \"School office\". Student sees \"My teachers\" and \"School office\". Another student isn't offered (\"No one you can message matches\"). Student-to-student API create returns 403. |","+| FR-6 | Staff-created group | PASS | A student can reply in a teacher-created group. |","+| FR-7 | Ended relationship | PASS | A dropped student sees an info Alert, \"You can no longer send messages in this conversation.\". The API returns 403. The teacher can still send. |","+| FR-13 | Thread polling | PASS | The new message appeared in the other open thread after about 5.35 s. |","+| FR-14 | Conversation menu | PASS | Mute adds a bell-off icon and changes the menu item to \"Unmute\". Archive moves the conversation to the Archived tab; Unarchive works. The Participants dialog shows role chips. Opening the thread sets `lastReadAt` and clears the badge. (UIV-3, UIV-5) |","+| FR-14 | Leave group | PASS | Confirm dialog, then the conversation leaves the list. Reopening it gives 404. The creator of a group with students isn't offered \"Leave group\". |","+| FR-15 | Edit/delete own message | PASS | Inline edit shows \"(edited)\". Delete has a confirm dialog and leaves the deleted placeholder. Messages older than 15 minutes have no options button, and a late PATCH returns 403. |","+| FR-16 | Student page actions | PASS | Teacher: \"Message parents\" opens the dialog prefilled with Pam Parent. Parent: \"Message teacher\" is limited to the \"My child's teachers (Sam)\" group. |","+| FR-17 | Roster selection | PASS | The button is disabled until a student is selected. Select all prefills both students. The new group has 3 participants and `involvesStudent=true`. |","+| FR-18 | Sidebar Messages and badge | PASS | Shown for all roles at 1280 px and in the 375 px nav. The badge appears for unread conversations and clears after reading. |","+| FR-21 | Quiet hours | PASS | Start/End time fields with a timezone hint. 22:00–07:00 (wrapping past midnight) saves and persists. No horizontal scroll at 375 px. |","+| FR-22 | Report message | PASS | Reason dialog, then the toast \"Reported — the school will review this.\". No Report option on your own messages. |","+| FR-23 | Safeguarding reports queue | PASS | The lead sees the nav entry and the OPEN report. The drawer shows the reason, participants and ±5 messages of context with the reported message highlighted. \"Mark reviewed\" requires a note, and the status changes to REVIEWED. A non-lead admin gets no nav entry, `/forbidden` and an API 403. |","+| FR-23 | Report drawer header | **FAIL** | **UIV-1:** the title and Close button are hidden under the AppBar. |","+| FR-24 | Safeguarding conversations | PASS | Participant and date filters. Only conversations with a student are listed. The read-only view has no composer and shows deleted bodies (with a \"Deleted\" chip), an \"Edited\" chip and \"Earlier versions\" with the original text. |","+| FR-25 | View audit | PASS | Each view writes a `safeguarding.conversation.view` audit row. |","+| FR-26 | Lead notification | PASS | The lead's bell shows an unread badge after the report. |","+| FR-2 | Admin user form flag | BLOCKED | No admin user form exists (ADR-11, accepted at intake), so there was no UI to render. QA verified the flag via `PATCH /api/users/:id`. |","+| NFR-7 | < 768 px single pane | PASS | At 375 px the list and the thread show one at a time, the back arrow returns to the list, and there is no horizontal scroll. |","+| NFR-5 | MUI-only | PASS | Every rendered surface uses MUI components. |","+| NFR-8 | Near-real-time | PASS | About 5.35 s via polling. |"," "," ## Evidence"," ","-The screenshots are in `screenshots/`:","+All files are in `screenshots/`:"," ","-- teacher: `teacher-gradebook-*`, `teacher-assignment-editor-category-1280`, `teacher-quiz-editor-category-1280`, `teacher-report-card*`","-- admin: `admin-grading-scale*`, `admin-report-cards-*`, `admin-report-card-*`","-- student: `student-grades*`, `student-course-grades-375`, `student-tab-*`, `student-report-card-print-375`","-- parent: `parent-grades*`, `parent-report-card-print-{375,1280}`","-- other: `outsider-report-card-375`, `nav-{student,parent}-{1280,375}`","-- PDFs: `parent-report-card.pdf`, `print-all.pdf`","+- **Parent:**","+  - `parent-messages-empty-1280`","+  - `parent-new-message-{contacts,filled}-1280`","+  - `parent-after-send-1280`","+  - `parent-composer-counter-1280`","+  - `parent-thread-attachment-1280`","+  - `parent-delete-confirm-1280`","+  - `parent-thread-edited-deleted-1280`","+  - `parent-student-message-teacher-1280`","+  - `parent-quiet-hours-{1280,375}`","+- **Teacher:**","+  - `teacher-inbox-unread-1280`","+  - `teacher-thread-1280`","+  - `teacher-report-dialog-1280`","+  - `teacher-reported-toast-1280`","+  - `teacher-conversation-menu-1280`","+  - `teacher-after-mute-1280`","+  - `teacher-participants-1280`","+  - `teacher-archived-tab-1280`","+  - `teacher-roster-{selected,dialog}-1280`","+  - `teacher-student-message-parents-1280`","+- **Student:**","+  - `student-new-message-contacts-375`","+  - `student-inbox-375`","+  - `student-thread-375`","+  - `student-leave-confirm-375`","+  - `student-left-not-found-375`","+  - `student-relationship-ended-1280`","+- **Safeguarding lead:**","+  - `lead-safeguarding-reports-1280`","+  - `lead-report-drawer-1280`","+  - `lead-report-drawer-student-1280` (UIV-1)","+  - `lead-report-reviewed-1280`","+  - `lead-safeguarding-conversations-1280`","+  - `lead-safeguarding-conversation-view-1280`","+  - `lead-safeguarding-student-view-1280`","+  - `lead-reported-conversation-view-1280`","+- **Non-lead admin:** `admin-nonlead-safeguarding-1280`"]}],"originalFile":"# UI Verification Report — SH-11 (PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards)\n\n- **Ticket:** SH-11\n- **Timestamp:** 2026-11-09T15:23:52Z\n- **Status:** complete\n- **Result:** 34 findings across 31 UI-facing requirements: **32 PASS, 2 FAIL, 0 BLOCKED**\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-10 report. `ui-verification-report.json` has the same findings in machine-readable form, and `uiv-raw.json` has the raw probe output.\n\n## Headline\n\nEvery SH-11 surface rendered and behaved as specified. That covers the gradebook grid, settings, dialogs, column menu, CSV export, student/parent grades, the admin and homeroom report-card flows, the print views and access control. The FR-15 golden case renders **78.0% C+**.\n\nTwo visual defects need fixing:\n\n| ID | Severity | Surface | Problem | Suggested fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **UIV-1** | moderate | Report card on-screen view at 375 px (`/report-cards/[id]/print`) | The Courses table is wider than the card. The Grade and Comment columns spill past the card border and the page scrolls horizontally. Students and parents open this page from their phones. A4 printing is unaffected. | Wrap the table in `TableContainer` (`overflowX: auto`) or stack the columns below `sm` in `ReportCardDocument.tsx` |\n| **UIV-2** | minor | Gradebook settings → Grading scale | The Select renders **blank** when the course uses the school default (`scaleId ''`). The \"School default (Standard A–F)\" option exists but isn't displayed, because MUI Select hides an empty value without `displayEmpty`. | `slotProps={{ select: { displayEmpty: true }, inputLabel: { shrink: true } }}` in `GradebookSettingsClient.tsx` |\n\n## Minor observations\n\n- **UIV-3 (a11y):** the invalid \"Weights total 90 / 100\" chip is pale red on pale red and nearly unreadable. axe reports color-contrast (serious) ×2. The red helper text next to Save still explains the problem.\n- **UIV-4 (a11y/layout):** at 375 px, the expanded `/grades` item table puts % and Comment off-screen in a scroll region that can't take keyboard focus. axe reports scrollable-region-focusable (serious).\n- **UIV-5:** axe reports empty-table-header (minor) on the DataGrids. This is the same pattern seen in SH-10.\n- **UIV-6 (not exercised in the UI; QA tests cover them):**\n  - arrow-key cell navigation\n  - a quiz-synced cell opening its attempt\n  - virtualisation at 60×120 and the NFR-2 timings\n  - DRAFT-only regeneration (FR-31)\n  - the roster's grade-level filter\n  - the `grade.posted` notification\n  - the green (≥80) card colour\n- **ENV-1:** the dev DB's current year (2026-2027) has **no terms**, so the feature is unusable in dev until an admin adds them. In that state the gradebook shows a clear info Alert. Verification used a temporary tagged term.\n- **ENV-2 (for QA/dev, not UI):** 9 orphaned `TermGradeOverride` rows predate this phase. Their courses were deleted, but the rows remain because the model has no FK to Course and `tests/e2e/report-cards.spec.ts` cleanup doesn't delete overrides. They were left in place.\n\n## Method\n\n- Production build (`npm run build`, exit 0) served by `next start -p 3300` against Postgres :5433. The :3000/:3001 servers were left alone.\n- Throwaway Playwright driver `/tmp/uiv-sh11/driver.cjs`, outside the repo, with tagged fixtures `uiv-sh11`:\n  - users: an admin, a homeroom teacher, 2 section students, an outsider student, and a parent linked to both students\n  - courses: UIV Maths (Homework 40 / Exams 60, with manual items, a hidden item and a late synced assignment) and UIV English (no categories)\n  - a temporary term\n- Viewports: teacher/admin at 1280×800, student/parent at 375×667, plus cross-checks at the other width. Print media was emulated and PDFs were rendered to check A4 size and page count.\n- DB state was checked after each mutation.\n- The nav probe `/tmp/uiv-sh11/nav.cjs` confirmed sidebar entries per role.\n- All fixtures were removed (verified: 0 tagged users, courses, terms or sections remain).\n- The only console errors were the expected 404s from the access-denial checks.\n- `figma-readiness.json` does not exist, so the comparison is against `requirements.json` only.\n\n## Findings\n\n| Req | Surface | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FR-2 | Assignment and quiz editor category select | PASS | None / Homework / Exams. The saved value displays. |\n| FR-9 | Synced vs manual cells | PASS | Synced cells aren't editable. The API rejects a synced score edit (400 \"Only the comment can be changed here…\"). |\n| FR-14 | Letter-only override | PASS | `78.0% B *`. Percent kept, letter B, comment saved. |\n| FR-15 | Golden case | PASS | 18/20 + 9/10 (HW 40%) and 70/100 (Exams 60%) give 90.0 / 70.0 → **78.0% C+**. The student view shows the same percent. |\n| FR-16 | `/admin/grading-scales` | PASS | Default chip, 12-band editor. Inline errors \"Letters must be unique\" and \"Must be lower than the band above\". Create and delete work. Deleting the default is disabled. Admin nav entries are present. |\n| FR-17 | Gradebook settings | **FAIL** | The live weight sum works, Save is disabled at 90, and the API returns 400. **UIV-2:** the scale select is blank. UIV-3: low-contrast chip. |\n| FR-18 | Gradebook grid | PASS | Category column groups and Averages group. Headers show icon, title, due date and /max. Hidden items are dimmed with an eye-off icon. Bold Term column, sorted by last name, no pinned columns. The grid scrolls horizontally at 375 and the page does not. |\n| FR-19 | Cell rendering | PASS | Score, `EX`, red bold `M`, `—`, and a clock icon on the late synced score. |\n| FR-20 | Keyboard editing | PASS | Digits+Enter, E, M and Delete each save with a PUT. 6 `grade.update` audit rows. Out-of-range input gives a red outline and a toast, and nothing is saved. |\n| FR-21 | Synced cell click | PASS | Opens `/assignments/<id>/grade?studentId=…`. |\n| FR-22 | Add manual item | PASS | Title, Category, Max points, Date, Term. Required validation works. The new column appears right away. |\n| FR-23 | Override dialog | PASS | Percent, Letter, Teacher comment. Saving shows a toast and `*` in the Term cell. |\n| FR-24 | Column menu | PASS | Hide/Show (eye-off icon, `isVisible` toggled), Set ungraded to missing (→ M, term 32.0% F, correct), Item statistics (avg/median/high/low). |\n| FR-25 | Export CSV | PASS | `text/csv` attachment that matches the grid, including EX, M and the override letter. |\n| FR-26 | Student Grades tab | PASS | Course cards with red (50.0 F) and amber (78.0 B) chips. The expanded view shows category subtotals and the item table. The hidden item is absent. (UIV-4) |\n| FR-27 | `/grades` + nav | PASS | Parent child selector switches between children. The \"Grades\" nav entry is present for STUDENT and PARENT at 1280 and 375. |\n| FR-28 | Course Grades tab (student) | PASS | Only that course's card. No Gradebook or Attendance tabs. |\n| FR-29 | Admin report-cards roster | PASS | Term, grade-level and section filters. Status chips and warning text. Count buttons. axe clean. |\n| FR-30 | Generate drafts / snapshot | PASS | All required fields render, including attendance and the scale legend. No logo because `logoUrl` is null. |\n| FR-31 | Regeneration | PASS | Confirm copy and published snapshots checked. Draft refresh after grade edits wasn't re-driven in the UI. |\n| FR-32 | Review page | PASS | Homeroom teacher can edit only the homeroom comment. Admin can edit both. Saves persist. The teacher has no publish controls. |\n| FR-33 | `/report-cards` homeroom list | PASS | TEACHER nav entry. Lists section drafts with warnings. |\n| FR-34 | Publish / Unpublish | PASS | Single and bulk publish. Unpublish requires a reason and writes an audit row. Notifications go to students and the parent. |\n| FR-35 | Print views | PASS | Letterhead, tables, signature lines. Chrome and the print button are hidden under print media. A4 portrait, 1 page per card. Print all: 2 pages with a page break. |\n| FR-35 | On-screen card at 375 | **FAIL** | **UIV-1:** the table overflows the card and the page. |\n| FR-36 | Student Report cards tab | PASS | Draft hidden (\"No report cards yet\"). Once published, listed with a link to the print view. |\n| FR-37 | Access control | PASS | Own draft → 404. Outsider → 404 on the page and the API. Parent and teacher allowed. |\n| FR-42 | Student grades API | PASS | Hidden item absent from the API and UI. The outsider gets 404. |\n| NFR-5 | Privacy | PASS | Same evidence as FR-37 and FR-42. |\n| NFR-7 | MUI-only UI | PASS | All surfaces use MUI components. No raw unstyled HTML seen. |\n| NFR-8 | DataGrid MIT tier | PASS | Column groups and editing only. No pinned columns, no Pro watermark. |\n| NFR-11 | Print layout | PASS | A4 portrait PDFs: `screenshots/parent-report-card.pdf` and `screenshots/print-all.pdf`. |\n| FR-26 | `/grades` table at 375 | PASS | Minor observation UIV-4 (scroll region not keyboard-focusable). |\n| FR-18 | Gradebook with no terms | PASS | ENV-1: info Alert instead of a crash. |\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe screenshots are in `screenshots/`:\n\n- teacher: `teacher-gradebook-*`, `teacher-assignment-editor-category-1280`, `teacher-quiz-editor-category-1280`, `teacher-report-card*`\n- admin: `admin-grading-scale*`, `admin-report-cards-*`, `admin-report-card-*`\n- student: `student-grades*`, `student-course-grades-375`, `student-tab-*`, `student-report-card-print-375`\n- parent: `parent-grades*`, `parent-report-card-print-{375,1280}`\n- other: `outsider-report-card-375`, `nav-{student,parent}-{1280,375}`\n- PDFs: `parent-report-card.pdf`, `print-all.pdf`\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017HhRQapSt8tVkauhHeFhMk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
