se the drawer are Esc or clicking outside it.\n\nThe fix is one line: add `sx={{ zIndex: (t) => t.zIndex.modal }}` to the `<Drawer>` at `src/components/messaging/SafeguardingReports.tsx:181`. I haven't changed any product code.\n\n**What was checked:** I built and ran the app in production mode on port 3300 and drove it in a browser at 1280 px and 375 px wide, logged in as a parent, teacher, students, a safeguarding-lead admin and a non-lead admin. All test users and data were deleted afterwards.\n- **Messaging:** the inbox, conversation view and message box, starting a new conversation and who you can message, editing and deleting your own messages, reporting a message, and muting, archiving, viewing participants and leaving a group.\n- **Other screens:** the \"Message parents\" / \"Message teacher\" buttons on student pages, \"Message selected students\" on the course roster, quiet hours, and the single-pane layout on phones.\n- **Safeguarding:** the reports queue, the conversation search and read-only view, the audit log entries, and the lead's notification.\n- **Speed:** a message sent in one browser showed up in the other's open conversation in about 5.35 s, within the 6 s limit.\n\n**Not checked:** setting the safeguarding-lead flag on the admin user form. That form doesn't exist (a decision accepted at intake); QA checked the flag through the API instead.\n\n**Minor issues:**\n- **List markup:** the accessibility checker flags the conversation list as serious because its rows are links placed directly inside a list, without list items.\n- **Muted icon:** the icon's \"Muted\" label is hidden from screen readers. Setting `titleAccess=\"Muted\"` fixes it.\n- **Deleted-message preview:** when the last message is deleted, the conversation preview reads \"This message was deleted\" without the sender's name. Product should decide whether that's intended.\n- **Mute toast:** the \"Conversation muted\" toast didn't show while an earlier toast was still on screen. The mute itself worked.\n\n**Two problems that predate this ticket:**\n- In production mode, the security policy blocks the scripts Next.js needs to make pages interactive, so no client UI works there. I bypassed it for testing, as the existing end-to-end tests do.\n- The login rate limit meant I had to restart the server between test runs.\n\nThere's no design file for this ticket, so the comparison was against the written requirements only. This run replaced the old SH-11 reports and screenshots in the folder; those are still in git history.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/ui-verification/`:\n- `ui-verification-report.json`\n- `ui-verification-report.md`\n- `uiv-raw.json`\n- `screenshots/` (37 files)","ttft_ms":2051,"type":"result","duration_ms":1369905,"uuid":"de4ad3d3-b10b-4fff-89e7-2b50c9261cc3","ttft_stream_ms":1887,"time_to_request_ms":126,"first_content_frame_ms":1887,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":94,"outputTokens":50212,"cacheReadInputTokens":4275950,"cacheCreationInputTokens":231103,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.059373,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":9103,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":216419,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":14684,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
