lendar entries.\n\nThis agrees with the QA report: overall FAIL, with 32 requirements NOT-IMPLEMENTED.\n\n**What needs to happen:** re-run Dev for TASK-8 to TASK-27, then QA, then this phase.\n\n## The environment also blocked rendering\n\nEven for pages that already exist, nothing could be rendered after login:\n\n- **:3001 server:** the `next dev` server for this repo serves `/login` without styles (serif fallback fonts, no MUI theme), and the page never hydrates. Playwright fills the form and the value reads back correctly. The native form POST then reloads the page empty, so login failed for **all four seeded roles** (admin, teacher, parent, student). The `*-error.png` screenshots show this.\n  - A likely cause is that the dev server is stale after the TASK-1 dependency and override changes to `@mui/x-scheduler` and `@mui/x-internals`. This is not confirmed.\n  - I did not restart the server because it is shared.\n  - **Restart the dev server before the next UI-verification run.**\n- **:3000 server:** this one runs from a different checkout (`~/Documents/forge/schoolhub`) and returns 500 for every route, so it was not used.\n- **Signed-out requests:** without a session, `/calendar` and `/account/calendar` return 307 to `/login`, and `/api/calendar` and `/api/school-day` return 401. That is only the auth middleware answering, not evidence that a page or route exists.\n- **Design reference:** there is no `figma-readiness.json`, so the PRD text was the only reference.\n\n## Findings\n\nAll verdicts are **FAIL**. Each surface is missing from source, which I confirmed with a file check and `git diff`. None was marked PASS, because nothing was rendered.\n\n| Req | Surface | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FR-9 | `/calendar` (month, week and agenda views, navigation) | FAIL | `calendar/page.tsx` and `CalendarView.tsx` do not exist (TASK-20). |\n| NFR-12 | Default view (month at 768 px or wider, agenda below 768 px) | FAIL | Depends on the missing `/calendar` page. |\n| FR-10 | Source chips | FAIL | `SourceChips.tsx` and `sources.ts` do not exist. |\n| FR-11 | Parent child filter and child-name labels | FAIL | There is no calendar page or sources code. |\n| FR-12 | Event drawer, including the \"Add to my calendar\" .ics download | FAIL | `EventDrawer.tsx` and `/api/events/[id]/ics` do not exist. |\n| FR-13 | Clicking a deadline opens the assignment or quiz | FAIL | There is no calendar page. |\n| FR-14 | \"New event\" button, editor dialog and audience builder | FAIL | `EventEditorDialog.tsx` and `AudienceBuilder.tsx` do not exist. |\n| FR-21 | RSVP controls, disabled after the deadline | FAIL | There is no drawer and no RSVP API. |\n| FR-22 | Own RSVP and totals; full list and CSV export for the creator and admins | FAIL | There is no drawer and no `rsvps` API. |\n| FR-24 | `/account/calendar` Subscribe card | FAIL | The page, `SubscribeCard.tsx` and `/api/me/calendar-feed` do not exist. |\n| FR-35 | Calendar entries in the sidebar | FAIL | `navigation.ts` has 0 calendar entries. |\n| FR-17 | Holiday name shown in Today and timetable views | FAIL | `getScheduleForDate` is unchanged and only has a \"holidays hook in here\" comment. `isSchoolDay` does not exist. |\n| FR-18 | Holiday banner and confirmation on the attendance register | FAIL | The register page and `RegisterForm.tsx` are unchanged. |\n| FR-19 | Holiday warning in the assignment editor and quiz settings | FAIL | `AssignmentForm.tsx` and `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` are unchanged. |\n| FR-20 | \"Add term breaks\" admin button | FAIL | The page, the button and the API do not exist. |\n\nThe other requirements have no UI surface, so they are out of scope for this phase. QA covers them:\n\n- FR-1 to FR-8\n- FR-15 and FR-16\n- FR-23\n- FR-25 to FR-34\n- FR-36 and FR-37\n\n## Method\n\n1. I listed the requirements that have a user-visible surface, using `requirements.json` and the UI tasks in `implementation-plan.json`.\n2. I checked whether each planned UI file exists, and ran `git diff HEAD -- src` and a grep of `navigation.ts`.\n3. I sent signed-out HTTP requests to the :3000 and :3001 servers.\n4. I ran a Playwright driver, `/tmp/uiv-sh14/d2.cjs` (outside the repo, `bypassCSP` per ADR-4), against :3001. It tried to log in as each seeded role, then open `/calendar`, `/account/calendar` and `/admin/academic-years/x` and call the calendar APIs. Login failed for every role, as described above.\n5. I created no fixtures and made no changes to the database or product code.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":126,"newStart":1,"newLines":84,"lines":["-# UI Verification Report — SH-13 (PRD-13 Direct Messaging)","+# UI Verification Report: SH-14 (PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays)"," ","-- **Ticket:** SH-13","-- **Status:** complete","-- **Result:** 25 findings: **23 PASS, 1 FAIL, 1 BLOCKED**","+- **Ticket:** SH-14","+- **Status:** blocked","+- **Result:** 15 UI-facing findings: **0 PASS, 15 FAIL (not implemented), 0 BLOCKED**"," ","-> This replaces the stale SH-11 report and screenshots, which are still in git history. `ui-verification-report.json` has the same findings in machine-readable form, and `uiv-raw.json` has the raw probe output.","+> This report replaces the SH-13 report. The SH-13 screenshots in `screenshots/` are left as they were and are also in git history. SH-14 evidence is in `screenshots-sh14/` and `uiv-raw-sh14.log`. `ui-verification-report.json` has the same findings in machine-readable form."," "," ## Headline"," ","-Every SH-13 surface rendered and behaved as specified:","+**SH-14 has no UI to verify.** The Dev phase finished only TASK-1 to TASK-7, the backend foundation:"," ","-- the inbox, thread and composer","-- the new-message dialog and its contact groups","-- editing, deleting and reporting messages","-- mute, archive, view participants and leave group","-- the actions on the student page and the course roster","-- quiet hours","-- the 375 px single-pane layout","-- the safeguarding reports and conversations views","+- dependencies","+- Prisma models and migration","+- validators","+- recurrence expansion","+- iCal builder","+- audience resolver","+- notification types"," ","-A message sent in one browser appeared in the other browser's open thread in about **5.35 s**, within the 6 s limit.","+None of the user-facing tasks has code on disk: TASK-13 and TASK-17 to TASK-23. These files are missing:"," ","-One visual defect needs fixing:","+- `/calendar`: `page.tsx`, `CalendarView.tsx`, `SourceChips.tsx`","+- `EventDrawer.tsx`","+- `EventEditorDialog.tsx`","+- `AudienceBuilder.tsx`","+- `/account/calendar`: `page.tsx`, `SubscribeCard.tsx`","+- `/admin/academic-years/[id]`: the page and `TermBreaksButton.tsx`"," ","-| ID | Severity | Surface | Problem | Fix |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| **UIV-1** | moderate | `/admin/safeguarding` report drawer | The right-hand Drawer (z-index 1200) opens **under** the fixed AppBar (z-index drawer+1). The drawer's header, with the \"Report\" title and the **Close button**, is covered and can't be clicked: `elementFromPoint` returns the app bar and the click times out. Users can only close the drawer with Esc or a backdrop click. | Add `sx={{ zIndex: (t) => t.zIndex.modal }}` to the `<Drawer>` in `src/components/messaging/SafeguardingReports.tsx:181` |","+None of the existing screens was changed for holidays either: the timetable Today view, the attendance register, the assignment editor and the quiz settings. `src/config/navigation.ts` has no calendar entries."," ","-## Minor observations","+This agrees with the QA report: overall FAIL, with 32 requirements NOT-IMPLEMENTED."," ","-- **UIV-2 (a11y):** axe flags `list` (serious) on `/messages` and `/account/notifications`. `ListItemButton` renders as an `<a>` directly inside a `<ul>`. It also flags `heading-order` and `region` (moderate); `region` is an app-wide pattern. One run showed `color-contrast` ×1 on `/admin/safeguarding`.","-- **UIV-3 (a11y):** the muted icon in a conversation row has `aria-label=\"Muted\"`, but MUI's SvgIcon sets `aria-hidden` unless `titleAccess` is set, so screen readers never hear about it. Use `titleAccess=\"Muted\"` instead.","-- **UIV-4:** when the last message in a conversation is deleted, the list preview reads \"This message was deleted\" with no `sender:` prefix. Product should confirm whether that's intended.","-- **UIV-5:** the \"Conversation muted\" toast didn't appear while an earlier toast was still on screen. The mute itself succeeded.","-- **UIV-6 (not exercised in the UI; QA covers these at service level):**","-  - upward infinite scroll at 30 messages per page","-  - the 30 s list/badge poll timing","-  - the error shown at the 25-participant cap","-  - deferred email (FR-20)","-- **ENV-1:** the production CSP (`script-src 'self'`) blocks Next's inline hydration scripts under `next start`, so no client UI hydrates. This predates SH-13 (ADR-4), and the existing E2E specs use `bypassCSP`, as this run did. Production still needs a nonce.","-- **ENV-2:** the in-memory per-IP login rate limit forced a server restart between driver runs. This is expected behaviour.","+**What needs to happen:** re-run Dev for TASK-8 to TASK-27, then QA, then this phase."," ","-## Method","+## The environment also blocked rendering"," ","-- **Build and server:** `npm run build` (exit 0), served with `next start -p 3300` against Postgres :5433. The :3000 and :3001 servers were left alone.","-- **Drivers:** throwaway Playwright scripts outside the repo: `/tmp/uiv-sh13/driver.cjs` and `supp.cjs`. The supplementary script covers the safeguarding drawer and a student conversation with edited and deleted messages.","-- **Fixtures:** tagged `uiv-sh13*`:","-  - a safeguarding-lead admin and a non-lead admin","-  - a teacher, and a parent linked to student 1","-  - 2 students and 1 course","-- **Viewports:** 1280×800 and 375×667. DB state was checked after mutations. All fixtures were removed (0 remaining).","-- **Design reference:** `figma-readiness.json` does not exist, so the comparison is against `requirements.json` only.","+Even for pages that already exist, nothing could be rendered after login:"," ","+- **:3001 server:** the `next dev` server for this repo serves `/login` without styles (serif fallback fonts, no MUI theme), and the page never hydrates. Playwright fills the form and the value reads back correctly. The native form POST then reloads the page empty, so login failed for **all four seeded roles** (admin, teacher, parent, student). The `*-error.png` screenshots show this.","+  - A likely cause is that the dev server is stale after the TASK-1 dependency and override changes to `@mui/x-scheduler` and `@mui/x-internals`. This is not confirmed.","+  - I did not restart the server because it is shared.","+  - **Restart the dev server before the next UI-verification run.**","+- **:3000 server:** this one runs from a different checkout (`~/Documents/forge/schoolhub`) and returns 500 for every route, so it was not used.","+- **Signed-out requests:** without a session, `/calendar` and `/account/calendar` return 307 to `/login`, and `/api/calendar` and `/api/school-day` return 401. That is only the auth middleware answering, not evidence that a page or route exists.","+- **Design reference:** there is no `figma-readiness.json`, so the PRD text was the only reference.","+"," ## Findings"," ","+All verdicts are **FAIL**. Each surface is missing from source, which I confirmed with a file check and `git diff`. None was marked PASS, because nothing was rendered.","+"," | Req | Surface | Verdict | Notes |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| FR-9 | `/messages` inbox | PASS | Two panes, Inbox/Archived tabs, search and an empty state. Rows show avatar, subject, relative time and a \"Pam: …\" preview. Unread rows are bold (700) with a count badge. (UIV-4) |","-| FR-10 | Message thread | PASS | Avatar, name and time on each message. Day divider in the school timezone (America/New_York). FileList attachment, \"(edited)\" and *This message was deleted* all render. Infinite scroll not exercised (UIV-6). |","-| FR-11 | Composer | PASS | Enter sends and Shift+Enter adds a newline. The counter \"4600 / 5000\" appears past 4,500. Send is disabled at 5,001. Attach files works (\"0 / 5\" indicator), and the attachment is delivered. |","-| FR-12 | New-message dialog | PASS | Grouped \"To\" picker, optional subject and a message field. Send closes the dialog and navigates to the new thread. |","-| FR-8 | Contact groups | PASS | Parent sees \"My child's teachers (Sam)\" and \"School office\". Student sees \"My teachers\" and \"School office\". Another student isn't offered (\"No one you can message matches\"). Student-to-student API create returns 403. |","-| FR-6 | Staff-created group | PASS | A student can reply in a teacher-created group. |","-| FR-7 | Ended relationship | PASS | A dropped student sees an info Alert, \"You can no longer send messages in this conversation.\". The API returns 403. The teacher can still send. |","-| FR-13 | Thread polling | PASS | The new message appeared in the other open thread after about 5.35 s. |","-| FR-14 | Conversation menu | PASS | Mute adds a bell-off icon and changes the menu item to \"Unmute\". Archive moves the conversation to the Archived tab; Unarchive works. The Participants dialog shows role chips. Opening the thread sets `lastReadAt` and clears the badge. (UIV-3, UIV-5) |","-| FR-14 | Leave group | PASS | Confirm dialog, then the conversation leaves the list. Reopening it gives 404. The creator of a group with students isn't offered \"Leave group\". |","-| FR-15 | Edit/delete own message | PASS | Inline edit shows \"(edited)\". Delete has a confirm dialog and leaves the deleted placeholder. Messages older than 15 minutes have no options button, and a late PATCH returns 403. |","-| FR-16 | Student page actions | PASS | Teacher: \"Message parents\" opens the dialog prefilled with Pam Parent. Parent: \"Message teacher\" is limited to the \"My child's teachers (Sam)\" group. |","-| FR-17 | Roster selection | PASS | The button is disabled until a student is selected. Select all prefills both students. The new group has 3 participants and `involvesStudent=true`. |","-| FR-18 | Sidebar Messages and badge | PASS | Shown for all roles at 1280 px and in the 375 px nav. The badge appears for unread conversations and clears after reading. |","-| FR-21 | Quiet hours | PASS | Start/End time fields with a timezone hint. 22:00–07:00 (wrapping past midnight) saves and persists. No horizontal scroll at 375 px. |","-| FR-22 | Report message | PASS | Reason dialog, then the toast \"Reported — the school will review this.\". No Report option on your own messages. |","-| FR-23 | Safeguarding reports queue | PASS | The lead sees the nav entry and the OPEN report. The drawer shows the reason, participants and ±5 messages of context with the reported message highlighted. \"Mark reviewed\" requires a note, and the status changes to REVIEWED. A non-lead admin gets no nav entry, `/forbidden` and an API 403. |","-| FR-23 | Report drawer header | **FAIL** | **UIV-1:** the title and Close button are hidden under the AppBar. |","-| FR-24 | Safeguarding conversations | PASS | Participant and date filters. Only conversations with a student are listed. The read-only view has no composer and shows deleted bodies (with a \"Deleted\" chip), an \"Edited\" chip and \"Earlier versions\" with the original text. |","-| FR-25 | View audit | PASS | Each view writes a `safeguarding.conversation.view` audit row. |","-| FR-26 | Lead notification | PASS | The lead's bell shows an unread badge after the report. |","-| FR-2 | Admin user form flag | BLOCKED | No admin user form exists (ADR-11, accepted at intake), so there was no UI to render. QA verified the flag via `PATCH /api/users/:id`. |","-| NFR-7 | < 768 px single pane | PASS | At 375 px the list and the thread show one at a time, the back arrow returns to the list, and there is no horizontal scroll. |","-| NFR-5 | MUI-only | PASS | Every rendered surface uses MUI components. |","-| NFR-8 | Near-real-time | PASS | About 5.35 s via polling. |","+| FR-9 | `/calendar` (month, week and agenda views, navigation) | FAIL | `calendar/page.tsx` and `CalendarView.tsx` do not exist (TASK-20). |","+| NFR-12 | Default view (month at 768 px or wider, agenda below 768 px) | FAIL | Depends on the missing `/calendar` page. |","+| FR-10 | Source chips | FAIL | `SourceChips.tsx` and `sources.ts` do not exist. |","+| FR-11 | Parent child filter and child-name labels | FAIL | There is no calendar page or sources code. |","+| FR-12 | Event drawer, including the \"Add to my calendar\" .ics download | FAIL | `EventDrawer.tsx` and `/api/events/[id]/ics` do not exist. |","+| FR-13 | Clicking a deadline opens the assignment or quiz | FAIL | There is no calendar page. |","+| FR-14 | \"New event\" button, editor dialog and audience builder | FAIL | `EventEditorDialog.tsx` and `AudienceBuilder.tsx` do not exist. |","+| FR-21 | RSVP controls, disabled after the deadline | FAIL | There is no drawer and no RSVP API. |","+| FR-22 | Own RSVP and totals; full list and CSV export for the creator and admins | FAIL | There is no drawer and no `rsvps` API. |","+| FR-24 | `/account/calendar` Subscribe card | FAIL | The page, `SubscribeCard.tsx` and `/api/me/calendar-feed` do not exist. |","+| FR-35 | Calendar entries in the sidebar | FAIL | `navigation.ts` has 0 calendar entries. |","+| FR-17 | Holiday name shown in Today and timetable views | FAIL | `getScheduleForDate` is unchanged and only has a \"holidays hook in here\" comment. `isSchoolDay` does not exist. |","+| FR-18 | Holiday banner and confirmation on the attendance register | FAIL | The register page and `RegisterForm.tsx` are unchanged. |","+| FR-19 | Holiday warning in the assignment editor and quiz settings | FAIL | `AssignmentForm.tsx` and `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` are unchanged. |","+| FR-20 | \"Add term breaks\" admin button | FAIL | The page, the button and the API do not exist. |"," ","-## Evidence","+The other requirements have no UI surface, so they are out of scope for this phase. QA covers them:"," ","-All files are in `screenshots/`:","+- FR-1 to FR-8","+- FR-15 and FR-16","+- FR-23","+- FR-25 to FR-34","+- FR-36 and FR-37"," ","-- **Parent:**","-  - `parent-messages-empty-1280`","-  - `parent-new-message-{contacts,filled}-1280`","-  - `parent-after-send-1280`","-  - `parent-composer-counter-1280`","-  - `parent-thread-attachment-1280`","-  - `parent-delete-confirm-1280`","-  - `parent-thread-edited-deleted-1280`","-  - `parent-student-message-teacher-1280`","-  - `parent-quiet-hours-{1280,375}`","-- **Teacher:**","-  - `teacher-inbox-unread-1280`","-  - `teacher-thread-1280`","-  - `teacher-report-dialog-1280`","-  - `teacher-reported-toast-1280`","-  - `teacher-conversation-menu-1280`","-  - `teacher-after-mute-1280`","-  - `teacher-participants-1280`","-  - `teacher-archived-tab-1280`","-  - `teacher-roster-{selected,dialog}-1280`","-  - `teacher-student-message-parents-1280`","-- **Student:**","-  - `student-new-message-contacts-375`","-  - `student-inbox-375`","-  - `student-thread-375`","-  - `student-leave-confirm-375`","-  - `student-left-not-found-375`","-  - `student-relationship-ended-1280`","-- **Safeguarding lead:**","-  - `lead-safeguarding-reports-1280`","-  - `lead-report-drawer-1280`","-  - `lead-report-drawer-student-1280` (UIV-1)","-  - `lead-report-reviewed-1280`","-  - `lead-safeguarding-conversations-1280`","-  - `lead-safeguarding-conversation-view-1280`","-  - `lead-safeguarding-student-view-1280`","-  - `lead-reported-conversation-view-1280`","-- **Non-lead admin:** `admin-nonlead-safeguarding-1280`","+## Method","+","+1. I listed the requirements that have a user-visible surface, using `requirements.json` and the UI tasks in `implementation-plan.json`.","+2. I checked whether each planned UI file exists, and ran `git diff HEAD -- src` and a grep of `navigation.ts`.","+3. I sent signed-out HTTP requests to the :3000 and :3001 servers.","+4. I ran a Playwright driver, `/tmp/uiv-sh14/d2.cjs` (outside the repo, `bypassCSP` per ADR-4), against :3001. It tried to log in as each seeded role, then open `/calendar`, `/account/calendar` and `/admin/academic-years/x` and call the calendar APIs. Login failed for every role, as described above.","+5. I created no fixtures and made no changes to the database or product code."]}],"originalFile":"# UI Verification Report — SH-13 (PRD-13 Direct Messaging)\n\n- **Ticket:** SH-13\n- **Status:** complete\n- **Result:** 25 findings: **23 PASS, 1 FAIL, 1 BLOCKED**\n\n> This replaces the stale SH-11 report and screenshots, which are still in git history. `ui-verification-report.json` has the same findings in machine-readable form, and `uiv-raw.json` has the raw probe output.\n\n## Headline\n\nEvery SH-13 surface rendered and behaved as specified:\n\n- the inbox, thread and composer\n- the new-message dialog and its contact groups\n- editing, deleting and reporting messages\n- mute, archive, view participants and leave group\n- the actions on the student page and the course roster\n- quiet hours\n- the 375 px single-pane layout\n- the safeguarding reports and conversations views\n\nA message sent in one browser appeared in the other browser's open thread in about **5.35 s**, within the 6 s limit.\n\nOne visual defect needs fixing:\n\n| ID | Severity | Surface | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **UIV-1** | moderate | `/admin/safeguarding` report drawer | The right-hand Drawer (z-index 1200) opens **under** the fixed AppBar (z-index drawer+1). The drawer's header, with the \"Report\" title and the **Close button**, is covered and can't be clicked: `elementFromPoint` returns the app bar and the click times out. Users can only close the drawer with Esc or a backdrop click. | Add `sx={{ zIndex: (t) => t.zIndex.modal }}` to the `<Drawer>` in `src/components/messaging/SafeguardingReports.tsx:181` |\n\n## Minor observations\n\n- **UIV-2 (a11y):** axe flags `list` (serious) on `/messages` and `/account/notifications`. `ListItemButton` renders as an `<a>` directly inside a `<ul>`. It also flags `heading-order` and `region` (moderate); `region` is an app-wide pattern. One run showed `color-contrast` ×1 on `/admin/safeguarding`.\n- **UIV-3 (a11y):** the muted icon in a conversation row has `aria-label=\"Muted\"`, but MUI's SvgIcon sets `aria-hidden` unless `titleAccess` is set, so screen readers never hear about it. Use `titleAccess=\"Muted\"` instead.\n- **UIV-4:** when the last message in a conversation is deleted, the list preview reads \"This message was deleted\" with no `sender:` prefix. Product should confirm whether that's intended.\n- **UIV-5:** the \"Conversation muted\" toast didn't appear while an earlier toast was still on screen. The mute itself succeeded.\n- **UIV-6 (not exercised in the UI; QA covers these at service level):**\n  - upward infinite scroll at 30 messages per page\n  - the 30 s list/badge poll timing\n  - the error shown at the 25-participant cap\n  - deferred email (FR-20)\n- **ENV-1:** the production CSP (`script-src 'self'`) blocks Next's inline hydration scripts under `next start`, so no client UI hydrates. This predates SH-13 (ADR-4), and the existing E2E specs use `bypassCSP`, as this run did. Production still needs a nonce.\n- **ENV-2:** the in-memory per-IP login rate limit forced a server restart between driver runs. This is expected behaviour.\n\n## Method\n\n- **Build and server:** `npm run build` (exit 0), served with `next start -p 3300` against Postgres :5433. The :3000 and :3001 servers were left alone.\n- **Drivers:** throwaway Playwright scripts outside the repo: `/tmp/uiv-sh13/driver.cjs` and `supp.cjs`. The supplementary script covers the safeguarding drawer and a student conversation with edited and deleted messages.\n- **Fixtures:** tagged `uiv-sh13*`:\n  - a safeguarding-lead admin and a non-lead admin\n  - a teacher, and a parent linked to student 1\n  - 2 students and 1 course\n- **Viewports:** 1280×800 and 375×667. DB state was checked after mutations. All fixtures were removed (0 remaining).\n- **Design reference:** `figma-readiness.json` does not exist, so the comparison is against `requirements.json` only.\n\n## Findings\n\n| Req | Surface | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| FR-9 | `/messages` inbox | PASS | Two panes, Inbox/Archived tabs, search and an empty state. Rows show avatar, subject, relative time and a \"Pam: …\" preview. Unread rows are bold (700) with a count badge. (UIV-4) |\n| FR-10 | Message thread | PASS | Avatar, name and time on each message. Day divider in the school timezone (America/New_York). FileList attachment, \"(edited)\" and *This message was deleted* all render. Infinite scroll not exercised (UIV-6). |\n| FR-11 | Composer | PASS | Enter sends and Shift+Enter adds a newline. The counter \"4600 / 5000\" appears past 4,500. Send is disabled at 5,001. Attach files works (\"0 / 5\" indicator), and the attachment is delivered. |\n| FR-12 | New-message dialog | PASS | Grouped \"To\" picker, optional subject and a message field. Send closes the dialog and navigates to the new thread. |\n| FR-8 | Contact groups | PASS | Parent sees \"My child's teachers (Sam)\" and \"School office\". Student sees \"My teachers\" and \"School office\". Another student isn't offered (\"No one you can message matches\"). Student-to-student API create returns 403. |\n| FR-6 | Staff-created group | PASS | A student can reply in a teacher-created group. |\n| FR-7 | Ended relationship | PASS | A dropped student sees an info Alert, \"You can no longer send messages in this conversation.\". The API returns 403. The teacher can still send. |\n| FR-13 | Thread polling | PASS | The new message appeared in the other open thread after about 5.35 s. |\n| FR-14 | Conversation menu | PASS | Mute adds a bell-off icon and changes the menu item to \"Unmute\". Archive moves the conversation to the Archived tab; Unarchive works. The Participants dialog shows role chips. Opening the thread sets `lastReadAt` and clears the badge. (UIV-3, UIV-5) |\n| FR-14 | Leave group | PASS | Confirm dialog, then the conversation leaves the list. Reopening it gives 404. The creator of a group with students isn't offered \"Leave group\". |\n| FR-15 | Edit/delete own message | PASS | Inline edit shows \"(edited)\". Delete has a confirm dialog and leaves the deleted placeholder. Messages older than 15 minutes have no options button, and a late PATCH returns 403. |\n| FR-16 | Student page actions | PASS | Teacher: \"Message parents\" opens the dialog prefilled with Pam Parent. Parent: \"Message teacher\" is limited to the \"My child's teachers (Sam)\" group. |\n| FR-17 | Roster selection | PASS | The button is disabled until a student is selected. Select all prefills both students. The new group has 3 participants and `involvesStudent=true`. |\n| FR-18 | Sidebar Messages and badge | PASS | Shown for all roles at 1280 px and in the 375 px nav. The badge appears for unread conversations and clears after reading. |\n| FR-21 | Quiet hours | PASS | Start/End time fields with a timezone hint. 22:00–07:00 (wrapping past midnight) saves and persists. No horizontal scroll at 375 px. |\n| FR-22 | Report message | PASS | Reason dialog, then the toast \"Reported — the school will review this.\". No Report option on your own messages. |\n| FR-23 | Safeguarding reports queue | PASS | The lead sees the nav entry and the OPEN report. The drawer shows the reason, participants and ±5 messages of context with the reported message highlighted. \"Mark reviewed\" requires a note, and the status changes to REVIEWED. A non-lead admin gets no nav entry, `/forbidden` and an API 403. |\n| FR-23 | Report drawer header | **FAIL** | **UIV-1:** the title and Close button are hidden under the AppBar. |\n| FR-24 | Safeguarding conversations | PASS | Participant and date filters. Only conversations with a student are listed. The read-only view has no composer and shows deleted bodies (with a \"Deleted\" chip), an \"Edited\" chip and \"Earlier versions\" with the original text. |\n| FR-25 | View audit | PASS | Each view writes a `safeguarding.conversation.view` audit row. |\n| FR-26 | Lead notification | PASS | The lead's bell shows an unread badge after the report. |\n| FR-2 | Admin user form flag | BLOCKED | No admin user form exists (ADR-11, accepted at intake), so there was no UI to render. QA verified the flag via `PATCH /api/users/:id`. |\n| NFR-7 | < 768 px single pane | PASS | At 375 px the list and the thread show one at a time, the back arrow returns to the list, and there is no horizontal scroll. |\n| NFR-5 | MUI-only | PASS | Every rendered surface uses MUI components. |\n| NFR-8 | Near-real-time | PASS | About 5.35 s via polling. |\n\n## Evidence\n\nAll files are in `screenshots/`:\n\n- **Parent:**\n  - `parent-messages-empty-1280`\n  - `parent-new-message-{contacts,filled}-1280`\n  - `parent-after-send-1280`\n  - `parent-composer-counter-1280`\n  - `parent-thread-attachment-1280`\n  - `parent-delete-confirm-1280`\n  - `parent-thread-edited-deleted-1280`\n  - `parent-student-message-teacher-1280`\n  - `parent-quiet-hours-{1280,375}`\n- **Teacher:**\n  - `teacher-inbox-unread-1280`\n  - `teacher-thread-1280`\n  - `teacher-report-dialog-1280`\n  - `teacher-reported-toast-1280`\n  - `teacher-conversation-menu-1280`\n  - `teacher-after-mute-1280`\n  - `teacher-participants-1280`\n  - `teacher-archived-tab-1280`\n  - `teacher-roster-{selected,dialog}-1280`\n  - `teacher-student-message-parents-1280`\n- **Student:**\n  - `student-new-message-contacts-375`\n  - `student-inbox-375`\n  - `student-thread-375`\n  - `student-leave-confirm-375`\n  - `student-left-not-found-375`\n  - `student-relationship-ended-1280`\n- **Safeguarding lead:**\n  - `lead-safeguarding-reports-1280`\n  - `lead-report-drawer-1280`\n  - `lead-report-drawer-student-1280` (UIV-1)\n  - `lead-report-reviewed-1280`\n  - `lead-safeguarding-conversations-1280`\n  - `lead-safeguarding-conversation-view-1280`\n  - `lead-safeguarding-student-view-1280`\n  - `lead-reported-conversation-view-1280`\n- **Non-lead admin:** `admin-nonlead-safeguarding-1280`\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017TgaKUzckyRaCxyrCq68qy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
