cription\": \"Seed data: one pending and one approved absence note for Grade 7; 'Autumn conferences' 3 weeks out for Grade 7 with Tom and Tina slots 15:00–17:00 (10 min), two booked; consent form 'Science Museum Trip' for Grade 7 due in 10 days linked to a calendar event with 40% responses.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Seed Data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-46\",\n      \"description\": \"Tests: unit (absence coverage matching whole-day/periods/multi-day, slot generation, signature match); integration (approval updates/pre-fill, concurrent atomic booking, notification suppression); Playwright (absence note → approve → register EXCUSED; book conference slot; sign consent).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Test Requirements\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Concurrency: two simultaneous bookings of the same slot → exactly one succeeds; the other gets 'That slot was just taken' (409 CONFLICT) and refreshed slots.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-1; AC-5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Performance: child overview first section paints < 1 s; full page < 2 s.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Auditability: absence approvals, consent responses and changes write AuditLog entries including IP address.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"UI component rule: Material UI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X data-grid/date-pickers/charts/scheduler); every component looked up via mui-mcp (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs) before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, Chakra, lucide-react, notistack, etc.) never imported; toasts via shared useToast(), confirmations via Dialog, pickers via Autocomplete; MCP unreachable = blocker. QA must verify.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 mandates recording as NFR)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Security/access: every handler and server page enforces access server-side; parents only for linked students, homeroom teachers only for their section, consent tracking only creator/admin.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Roles; code conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models/services/components/helpers (audit(), notify(), files contexts, attendance-service, AudienceType/audience.ts, DataTable, FileUpload, MarkdownView, ConfirmDialog, UserAvatar); new services in src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts; no renames, no re-scaffolding.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Code layout and conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"Quality gates: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test stay green; TypeScript strict; Zod validators in src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts shared by forms and handlers; no console.log (use logger).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Constraints; conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Date handling: timestamps stored UTC, displayed and date rules (absence windows, 'today', due dates, 48h reminder) evaluated in SchoolSettings.timezone; date-only fields use @db.Date.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — conventions; Assumptions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Scope: deliver in a single forge run; no payments, pickup/transport, or parent self-registration; do not modify behaviour owned by PRD-16+.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Out of Scope; Constraints\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Lists use standard pagination (?page, ?pageSize ≤100), sorting and ?q search where applicable.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Pagination conventions\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"PRD-12 Announcement model/read-state is absent from the workspace (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts). Should the overview Announcements card render an empty state, or must SH-15 add a minimal Announcement read model? (FR-13)\",\n        \"PRD-14 dev phase failed (run-summary SH-14 dev failedCount=1): CalendarEvent models exist but no calendar pages/API. How should 'My meetings' (FR-35), 'Upcoming events' (FR-14), calendar studentId filter (FR-5) and ConsentForm.eventId linking be satisfied?\",\n        \"Shared wrappers live under src/components/<Name>/ (e.g. src/components/Toast/useToast.ts), not src/components/shared/ as the PRD states. Confirm reuse in place rather than moving.\",\n        \"Student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]); confirm overview 'View all' links target existing tabs.\",\n        \"No parent timetable/grades page with a child selector found under src/app/(app) (only /grades, /assignments and /api/me/timetable). Which pages must adopt the sh_child default (FR-5)?\",\n        \"Notification key name for the 48h consent reminder and the manual 'Remind non-responders' is not specified (FR-44).\",\n        \"Does 'block individual slots' need a new ConferenceSlot field (schema has none), or is a blocked slot represented by deleting it? (FR-29)\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"PRD-12 Announcement model/read-state is absent from the workspace (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts). Should the overview Announcements card render an empty state, or must SH-15 add a minimal Announcement read model? (FR-13)\",\n        \"PRD-14 dev phase failed (run-summary SH-14 dev failedCount=1): CalendarEvent models exist but no calendar pages/API. How should 'My meetings' (FR-35), 'Upcoming events' (FR-14), calendar studentId filter (FR-5) and ConsentForm.eventId linking be satisfied?\",\n        \"Shared wrappers live under src/components/<Name>/ (e.g. src/components/Toast/useToast.ts), not src/components/shared/ as the PRD states. Confirm reuse in place rather than moving.\",\n        \"Student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]); confirm overview 'View all' links target existing tabs.\",\n        \"No parent timetable/grades page with a child selector found under src/app/(app) (only /grades, /assignments and /api/me/timetable). Which pages must adopt the sh_child default (FR-5)?\",\n        \"Notification key name for the 48h consent reminder and the manual 'Remind non-responders' is not specified (FR-44).\",\n        \"Does 'block individual slots' need a new ConferenceSlot field (schema has none), or is a blocked slot represented by deleting it? (FR-29)\"\n      ],\n      \"note\": \"No interactive user available; aggregate confidence (95%) exceeds 80% threshold so no further rounds run. Items forwarded to Architect as flagged assumptions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-14\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T02:59:22Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"blocked\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"surface\": \"/calendar page (EventCalendar month/week/agenda, Today/prev/next/date picker)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"NOT IMPLEMENTED: src/app/(app)/calendar/page.tsx and CalendarView.tsx (TASK-20) do not exist. Signed out, GET /calendar on :3001 just redirects to /login (middleware), so no page is behind it. Nothing to render.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"NFR-12\",\n      \"surface\": \"/calendar default view (month at 768 px or wider, agenda below 768 px)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"NOT IMPLEMENTED: Depends on the /calendar page (TASK-20), which does not exist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"surface\": \"Calendar source chips (School events, My assignments, My quizzes, My timetable, Holidays)\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"NOT IMPLEMENTED: SourceChips.tsx and src/server/calendar/sources.ts (TASK-9/20) do not exist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"surface\": \"Parent child filter and child-name labels on deadlines\",\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n      \"notes\": \"NOT IMPLEMENTED: There is no calendar page or sources.ts. The audience resolver's studentIds filter exists, but no UI uses it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirementId\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"surface\": \"Event drawer (title, category badge, school-tz time, loctotal 5344\ndrwxr-xr-x  39 ikramaansari  staff    1248 Nov  9 23:26 .\ndrwxr-xr-x   7 ikramaansari  staff     224 Nov 10 08:11 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   16917 Nov  9 23:24 admin-nonlead-safeguarding-1280.png\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  133590 Nov  9 23:24 lead-report-drawer-1280.png\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  122834 Nov  9 23:25 lead-report-drawer-student-1280.png\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  126206 Nov  9 23:24 lead-report-reviewed-1280.png\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   10942 Nov  9 23:24 lead-reported-conversation-view-1280.png\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   86220 Nov  9 23:24 lead-safeguarding-conversation-view-1280.png\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   76984 Nov  9 23:24 lead-safeguarding-conversations-1280.png\n# Dev Log — SH-15 (PRD-15 Parent Portal)\n\n> Before this run, this file held SH-14's log and `task-completion-markers.json` held SH-14's markers. Both are replaced for SH-15, following the precedent from earlier tickets. `dev-rerun-count.json` was left untouched because the engine owns it.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-10)\n\nAll 27 tasks were implemented in one iteration, in dependency order. Every file in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exists at its exact path. No dependencies were added (ADR-1).\n\n### Verification\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm run typecheck` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | clean |\n| Unit tests (FR-46) | 11/11 new tests pass: coverage, slots, signature |\n| SH-15 integration tests (local DB, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) | 7/7 pass: approval, pre-fill, suppression, concurrent booking, one-per-teacher |\n| `npm run build` | succeeds |\n| SH-15 Playwright specs | 4/4 pass, run with `PORT=3100 APP_URL=http://localhost:3100` because another process holds :3000 |\n| `npm run db:seed` | runs, and runs again idempotently |\n\nThe migration `20261114000000_prd15_parent_portal` was generated with `prisma migrate diff`; it drops nothing that already exists. The raw-SQL partial unique index is appended to it. The migration is applied (`migrate deploy`) and the Prisma client is regenerated. The mui-mcp lookup (NFR-4) worked: `useMuiDocs` returned docs for @mui/material@9.5.0.\n\n### Failures that already existed (not caused by SH-15)\n- **`attendance-qa: FR-22 A → P → A`** fails on the pre-SH-15 baseline. I checked this with `git stash`. It is out of SH-15 scope.\n- **Teacher re-saving an EXCUSED row an admin set** also failed on the baseline. It is now fixed, as part of the FR-25 EXCUSED rule change.\n- **The full parallel `vitest run` against the shared DB** is flaky in existing suites: attendance-qa, email-dispatch and assignments-qa. The same failures happen with the SH-15 tests excluded.\n- **Unrelated unit tests** in `useToast`, `auth-forms` and `lockout` (module resolution) fail independently of this ticket.\n- **`dashboard.spec.ts`** fails on CSP/hydration timing, the known QA blocker 1. With a short wait, admin `/dashboard` renders the heading and has 0 serious/critical axe violations.\n\n### Implementation notes and deviations\n- **`AbsenceReason` values.** The PRD's exact values were not available, so the enum is `ILLNESS, MEDICAL_APPOINTMENT, FAMILY, RELIGIOUS, OTHER`.\n- **Eligible grade levels.** `ConferenceEvent` stores them as `gradeLevelIds String[]`. `ConferenceSlot.bookedAt` is an extra audit column.\n- **Absence-note date window (−14/+60).** `absenceNoteSchemaFor(today)` is a factory used by the form. The service re-checks the window with `schoolToday()`.\n- **Lazy import of `files-service`.** `absence-notes-service` imports it lazily, so importers of attendance-service (tests and scripts) don't load env/storage. `contexts.ts` imports `homeroomTeacherOf` lazily to avoid a cycle.\n- **FR-25 EXCUSED rule.** A teacher may mark EXCUSED when an APPROVED note covers the record. A teacher may also re-save a row that is already EXCUSED unchanged. Anything else returns 403 `NO_APPROVED_NOTE`.\n- **Nav \"Absence notes\" for parents.** It points at `/attendance/absence-notes`, which redirects a parent to the selected child's list. A teacher sees the entry only with a current-year homeroom section.\n- **Simple lists use server-rendered MUI `Table`.** These are the parent absence list, `/conferences` and `/consent-forms`. `DataTable` needs client-side column functions, and the matrix gives these routes only a `page.tsx`. The review queue, admin conferences and consent tracking use `DataTable`.\n- **Pagination.** Parent consent lists and tracking rows are filtered and paginated in memory, marked with a `ponytail:` comment. A family sees few forms, and tracking is bounded by the audience size.\n- **Booking notifications.** `conference.booked` links to `/conferences/:id`, and its body carries the `/api/conference-slots/:id/ics` link. A notification link pointing at a download would be odd.\n- **Teachers card \"Message\" link.** It uses `/messages?to=<id>`. `/messages` has no recipient prefill yet, so this is a ponytail note and a follow-up.\n- **Remind throttle.** The 429 response carries `Retry-After`, set in the remind route.\n- **Seed (FR-45).** Conference event, slots, the Science Museum calendar event and the consent form are always seeded. Absence notes, bookings and consent responses need Grade 7 students with linked parents. Those come from other seeds and are absent from the current local DB, so these parts are skipped with a log, matching the existing seed convention of never creating another PRD's data.\n- **E2E specs** build their own fixtures, like `attendance.spec.ts`, so they don't depend on seed data.\n- **Partial by design (ADR-11).**\n  - FR-13: the Announcements card is an EmptyState.\n  - FR-35: \"My meetings\" appear only in the overview cards.\n  - FR-5: there is no calendar `studentId` filter.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma models + migration 20261114000000_prd15_parent_portal — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Zod validators (absence-notes, conferences, consent-forms) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: pure helpers + FR-46 unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: notification types, absence-note file context, upload restriction — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: getSelectedChild + POST /api/me/selected-child — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: ChildSwitcher, shell, layout, navigation — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: absence-notes-service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: absence notes API — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: attendance integration (pre-fill, EXCUSED rule, absent suppression, badge) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: parent absence form + list — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: absence-note review queue — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: conferences-service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: conferences API — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: admin conferences UI — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: conference list, availability, printable day view — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: parent booking page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: consent-forms-service + cron wiring — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: consent forms API — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: consent list + create UI — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: consent detail/respond + tracking UI — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: overview-service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: overview API — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: overview UI (/my-children, streaming cards, dashboard redirect) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-24: sh_child default on /assignments, /grades, /api/me/timetable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-25: seed (parent portal) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-26: integration tests (approval, pre-fill, suppression, concurrent booking) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-27: Playwright specs (absence → approve → EXCUSED; book slot; sign consent) — ✓ complete\n\n### Blockers\nNone.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TKaDSE2ci6FvkYSj5RU5tt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
