{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtcPjqh7qmep9DH2trPN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've finished the SH-15 UI verification. One real defect needs fixing before release: several pages show dates and times in the computer's timezone instead of the school's.\n\n**Result:** 38 checks: 31 PASS, 5 FAIL, 2 BLOCKED.\n\n**What works:** every SH-15 screen renders correctly with Material UI. All three main flows also work in a real browser:\n- Absence note → approve → the attendance register shows EXCUSED with an \"Absence note\" badge.\n- A parent books a conference slot with a note.\n- A parent signs a consent form, including the error when the signature doesn't match.\n\nThe child switcher works, an invalid `sh_child` cookie falls back to the first child, the child overview cards lay out properly on desktop and at 390 px wide, and each role sees the right menu entries.\n\n**The defect (NFR-8):** about 10 components use `toLocaleString`/`toLocaleTimeString`, which use the browser's or server's timezone. Two places where it matters:\n- **Teacher availability page:** the saved range reads 3:00–5:00 PM, but the slots are listed as 01:00–03:00 (`AvailabilityClient.tsx:25`).\n- **Consent due date:** the seeded form is due 19 Nov at 23:59 school time but shows \"Due 11/20/2026, 9:59 AM\", which is the wrong day.\n\nThe fix is to use the existing `formatInSchoolTz` helper; the report lists every affected line.\n\n**Other FAILs:** the remaining three are the partial items the Architect already accepted (ADR-11): no calendar `studentId` filter (FR-5), the Announcements card is always empty (FR-13), and booked meetings don't appear in a calendar (FR-35).\n\n**BLOCKED:**\n- The absence form's period checkboxes couldn't be checked because the local database has no bell-schedule periods.\n- The overlapping-booking error message has no test data that would trigger it in the UI.\n\n**How I checked it:**\n- **Dev server:** the production build doesn't work in a browser: its security policy (`next.config.js`) blocks Next's inline scripts, so pages never become interactive. That setting dates from the project's first commit, not SH-15. I ran `next dev` on :3201 instead, because the shared :3000 server returns 500 and :3001 hangs.\n- **Two-child parent:** to test the switcher I briefly added a second parent–child link to the shared database and deleted it afterwards.\n- **E2E specs:** I ran the three SH-15 specs against :3201 with screenshots on; all 4 tests passed. They set up and remove their own test data.\n- **Cleanup:** I stopped both servers I started and deleted my temporary scripts.\n\n**Minor visual issues:** empty tables cut off their \"No results\" message, some avatars have no background colour, and an empty \"Periods\" group shows no hint.\n\n**Next step:** re-run Dev for the timezone fix, then re-check the availability and consent pages.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/ui-verification/`:\n- `ui-verification-report.json`\n- `ui-verification-report.md`\n- `uiv-raw-sh15.log`\n- `screenshots-sh15/`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":133524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":491,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7a9e320-e452-45a7-a288-8e7e1a1228c9","uuid":"a6ac4c6a-d53b-4fdb-8656-25fa1be3a36d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:24:27.922Z","request_id":"req_011CgtcPjeHJaCmm4S1RcTYP"}
