{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JczjKfL9YL7jqAkHnjr2z7","type":"tool_result","content":"FR-1 Add Prisma enums InvoiceStatus (DRAFT, ISSUED, PARTIALLY_PAID, PAID, OVERDUE, VOID), PaymentMethod (CASH, BANK_TRANSFER, CHEQUE, CARD_TERMINAL, OTHER) and DiscountKind (PERCENT, FIXED).\nFR-2 Add models FeeItem, FeePlan, FeePlanLine, StudentOptionalFee, Discount, StudentDiscount, Invoice, InvoiceLine, Payment, PaymentAllocation and DocumentSequence with the fields, Decimal(10,2) money columns, uniques and indexes given\nFR-3 Add an InvoiceReminder model { invoiceId, kind, sentAt } to track overdue and pre-due reminders sent per invoice.\nFR-4 Add currency String @default(\"USD\") (ISO 4217) and invoiceFooter String? (bank details or payment instructions) to SchoolSettings.\nFR-5 Add isBursar Boolean @default(false) to User. It is meaningful only for ADMIN.\nFR-6 Fee setup page /admin/fees/setup, Fee items tab: list and create/edit/archive fee items (name, unique code, description, defaultAmount > 0, isOptional).\nFR-7 Fee plans tab: create and edit plans per academic year and term (termId null = annual) × grade level, with a line editor (fee item + amount), a computed total and dueDays (default 30). PUT replaces all lines.\nFR-8 Discounts tab: create, edit and archive discounts (name, kind PERCENT 0–100 or FIXED amount, optional autoRule SIBLING_2ND | SIBLING_3RD_PLUS, or null for manual).\nFR-9 Optional fees tab: assign optional fee items (for example Bus) to students per academic year with an amount, including a bulk assign for every student in a section.\nFR-10 Student discounts tab: assign manual discounts such as scholarships to students per academic year, with an optional note.\nFR-11 Sibling auto rules: SIBLING_2ND applies to the second and later enrolled siblings who share the same primary parent (ParentStudentLink.isPrimary). SIBLING_3RD_PLUS applies to the third and later siblings.\nFR-12 Invoice generation page /admin/fees/invoices/generate: choose a term (or annual) and one or more grade levels, then preview one row per student with plan lines, optional fees, manual and auto-sibling discounts, and the total.\nFR-13 The preview lists students who already have an invoice for the selected term as 'Skipped — already invoiced', and generation never creates a second invoice for them.\nFR-14 'Create drafts' creates DRAFT invoices. 'Create and issue' also issues them: assigns a number, sets issue date to today and due date to today + plan.dueDays (school timezone), sets status ISSUED and notifies parents (fees.invoice_\nFR-15 Discount calculation: percent discounts apply to the subtotal of non-optional lines, then fixed discounts apply. The total never goes below 0. Each discount is stored as a negative InvoiceLine with isDiscount=true. Rounding is 2 d\nFR-16 Invoice and receipt numbers (INV-YYYY-NNNNNN, RCT-YYYY-NNNNNN, sequential per year) come from DocumentSequence inside the issuing or saving transaction with a row lock (SELECT … FOR UPDATE). Numbers are unique and gap-free under c\nFR-17 Invoices list /admin/fees/invoices: server-side DataTable with number, student, grade/section, term, issue date, due date, total, paid, balance and a status badge.\nFR-18 Invoice list filters: status, term, grade level, section, overdue only, and q search by student name or invoice number. A totals row shows total billed, paid and outstanding for the whole filtered set.\nFR-19 Invoice detail shows the header, lines, allocations (payments applied), balance and an activity timeline from the audit log.\nFR-20 DRAFT invoice actions: edit lines, issue, delete. The API is PATCH/DELETE /api/fees/invoices/:id (DRAFT only) and POST /issue.\nFR-21 ISSUED, PARTIALLY_PAID and OVERDUE invoice actions: record payment, add an adjustment line (a negative credit-note-style line with a required reason, audited) and void. Void requires a reason and is allowed only when the invoice h\nFR-22 PAID invoice action: view the receipt(s) of the payments allocated to it.\nFR-23 Manual invoice: a bursar can create a one-off invoice for a student with free-form lines (for example a trip fee) via POST /api/fees/invoices.\nFR-24 Status recomputation in the same transaction after every allocation, reversal or adjustment: amountPaid >= total → PAID; 0 < amountPaid < total → PARTIALLY_PAID; issued with amountPaid = 0 → ISSUED; ISSUED or PARTIALLY_PAID past d\nFR-25 The OVERDUE transition runs both in the daily maintenance run and on read, so lists and details never show a stale non-overdue status.\nFR-26 Record payment page /admin/fees/payments/new: select a parent or student, then load all open invoices of the family (every child linked to that parent) with balances via GET /api/fees/families/:parentId/open-invoices.\nFR-27 Payment form fields: amount (> 0), method, reference, received date/time, payer name (defaults to the primary parent) and notes.\nFR-28 Allocation: auto-allocate oldest due date first by default. The bursar can edit per-invoice allocations. The sum of allocations must equal the payment amount, and no allocation may exceed the invoice balance.\nFR-29 Overpayment is refused with 'Amount exceeds the family's outstanding balance of <formatted amount>', and nothing is saved. Credit balances are out of scope.\nFR-30 Saving a payment assigns a receipt number, updates the invoices' amountPaid and status in the same transaction, notifies the family's parents (fees.payment_received with a receipt link) and opens the receipt.\nFR-31 Payment reversal (bursar, reason required): sets reversedAt and reversalReason, removes the effect of its allocations by recomputing the affected invoices, and is audited. The payment row is never deleted and shows a 'Reversed' st\nFR-32 Payments list and detail APIs (GET /api/fees/payments, /:id) for ADMIN, and for PARENT limited to payments allocated to their own children's invoices.\nFR-33 Printable invoice page /fees/invoices/[id]/print: A4 layout with school letterhead, number, dates, student, lines, totals and the invoice footer from settings, plus a 'Print / Save as PDF' button that calls window.print().\nFR-34 Printable receipt page /fees/receipts/[paymentId]/print: A4 layout with letterhead, receipt number, dates, payer, allocations, totals and the amount in words (for example 'One thousand two hundred forty dollars and 00/100'), plus \nFR-35 All money is formatted with Intl.NumberFormat in the school currency (SchoolSettings.currency).\nFR-36 Register notification types fees.invoice_issued, fees.payment_received (includes a receipt link) and fees.overdue_reminder in src/server/notifications/types.ts. All three default to email on and use the existing FINANCE category, \nFR-37 The maintenance run sends automatic reminders to the primary parent and the other linked parents 3 days before the due date, on due date + 1 day, and every 14 days after that while the invoice is overdue. Each send is recorded in \nFR-38 A bursar can send a manual reminder from the invoice (POST /api/fees/invoices/:id/remind), limited to once per 24 hours per invoice (429/CONFLICT when throttled).\nFR-39 Parent fees page /fees (PARENT): a summary card (total outstanding across children, next due date, overdue amount in red), an invoice list across children with status and balance, invoice detail and print, payment history with rec\nFR-40 The PRD-15 child overview shows a 'Fees' card when the child has an outstanding balance.\nFR-41 Students have no Fees navigation entry and no access to fee pages or APIs.\nFR-42 Fees dashboard /admin/fees: KPI cards (billed this term, collected, outstanding, overdue, collection rate %), a weekly collection trend chart, aging buckets (current, 1–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+ days overdue) and the top 10 overdue fa\nFR-43 Add an 'Outstanding fees' StatCard to the PRD-16 admin dashboard.\nFR-44 CSV exports: invoices (current filters), payments (date range and method filters) and the aging report.\nFR-45 Permissions: every fee write action requires ADMIN with isBursar=true. Other admins get read-only fee pages and read APIs. Teachers get 403 on every fee page and API. Parents read only their own children's data. Every check is ser\nFR-46 Add sidebar entries in src/config/navigation.ts: admin Fees (/admin/fees) with subpages for setup, invoices and payments, and parent Fees (/fees). There is no entry for TEACHER or STUDENT.\nFR-47 Seed: Alice Admin is a bursar; currency USD; an invoice footer with sample bank details; fee items Tuition, Lab fee, Bus service (optional) and Activity fee; Semester 1 plans for Grades 6–8.\nFR-48 Seed discounts Sibling (SIBLING_2ND 5%) and Merit scholarship (10%, manual, assigned to Sam). Seed issued Semester 1 invoices for Grade 7 with a mix of PAID, PARTIALLY_PAID, ISSUED and 3 OVERDUE, and 12 payments across methods.\nFR-49 Unit tests: discount calculation order, sibling rule detection, oldest-first auto-allocation, amount in words, status transitions.\nFR-50 Integration tests: concurrent number allocation, reversal recomputation, and an amountPaid integrity check across random sequences of payments and reversals.\nFR-51 Playwright e2e test: a bursar generates term invoices, records a payment and prints the receipt, then the parent sees the updated balance.\ndict_keys(['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prd', 'runMode', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'brownfieldNotes', 'status'])\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T04:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"ui-verification\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"pass\": 31,\n    \"fail\": 5,\n    \"blocked\": 2,\n    \"headline\": \"Every SH-15 UI surface renders under MUI, and all three PRD flows work end to end (absence note → approve → EXCUSED, book a slot, sign consent). One defect affects several screens: dates and times are formatted in the browser or server timezone instead of SchoolSettings.timezone (NFR-8). On the teacher availability page, slots for a 3:00–5:00 PM range are listed as 01:00–03:00. FR-13 and FR-35 (and FR-5's calendar part) are the partial items ADR-11 accepted.\",\n    \"environment\": \"Rendered with `next dev` on :3201 (Chromium via Playwright, 1280 px and 390 px). The `next start` production build on :3200 serves pages, but nothing hydrates: next.config.js sends `script-src 'self'` with no nonce, so Next's inline bootstrap scripts are blocked. That config dates from the project-startup commit, not SH-15, and is the same issue as the known QA blocker 1. The shared :3000 (500 on every route) and :3001 (hangs) servers were not used. No figma-readiness.json exists, so the PRD text was the only design reference.\",\n    \"evidence\": \"artifacts/ui-verification/screenshots-sh15/ (38 PNGs, including 4 e2e end-of-flow captures in e2e/) and artifacts/ui-verification/uiv-raw-sh15.log\"\n  },\n  \"findings\": [\n    { \"requirementId\": \"FR-3\", \"surface\": \"Top-bar child switcher (2+ children)\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"notes\": \"To get a two-child parent, a second ParentStudentLink was added temporarily and removed afterwards. The switcher renders as a Select with avatar and first name, and the menu lists Sam and Sara. Choosing Sara navigated to /my-children/<Sara> and set the sh_child cookie to Sara's id. Screenshots: parent2-switcher-open, parent2-after-switch.\" },\n    { \"requirementId\": \"FR-4\", \"surface\": \"sh_child cookie fallback\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"notes\": \"With sh_child=bogus-id, /assignments rendered for the first child (Sam Student) and threw no error. Screenshot: parent2-bogus-cookie.\" },\n    { \"requirementId\": \"FR-5\", \"surface\": \"/assignments, /grades default to the selected child; calendar filter\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"notes\": \"/assignments and /grades show the selected child's name. After switching to Sara, /grades showed 'Sara Scholar' (parent2-grades-default). The calendar studentId filter has no UI because no PRD-14 calendar page exists. ADR-11 accepted this as partial.\" },\n    { \"requirementId\": \"FR-6\", \"surface\": \"Top bar with one child\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"notes\": \"A one-child parent sees the avatar and 'Sam' as plain text with no dropdown (parent-overview-1280).\" },\n    { \"requirementId\": \"FR-7\", \"surface\": \"/my-children (redirect when one child, cards when 2+)\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"notes\": \"With one child, /dashboard lands on /my-children/<id>. With two children, /my-children shows a card per child with avatar, name, term attendance, missing-work count and average grade. These show '—', 0 and '—' because the local DB has no enrollments. Also checked at 390 px.\" },\nadmin-nonlead-safeguarding-1280.png\nlead-report-drawer-1280.png\nlead-report-drawer-student-1280.png\nlead-report-reviewed-1280.png\nlead-reported-conversation-view-1280.png\nlead-safeguarding-conversation-view-1280.png\nlead-safeguarding-conversations-1280.png\nlead-safeguarding-reports-1280.png\nlead-safeguarding-student-view-1280.png\nparent-after-send-1280.png","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bdae3a7-5bc6-4a4f-b701-fedb2c55b2b8","uuid":"e9fe93a0-2d4f-4af5-8b3e-afaccfd8b601","timestamp":"2026-11-10T11:44:31.754Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FR-1 Add Prisma enums InvoiceStatus (DRAFT, ISSUED, PARTIALLY_PAID, PAID, OVERDUE, VOID), PaymentMethod (CASH, BANK_TRANSFER, CHEQUE, CARD_TERMINAL, OTHER) and DiscountKind (PERCENT, FIXED).\nFR-2 Add models FeeItem, FeePlan, FeePlanLine, StudentOptionalFee, Discount, StudentDiscount, Invoice, InvoiceLine, Payment, PaymentAllocation and DocumentSequence with the fields, Decimal(10,2) money columns, uniques and indexes given\nFR-3 Add an InvoiceReminder model { invoiceId, kind, sentAt } to track overdue and pre-due reminders sent per invoice.\nFR-4 Add currency Str