{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FCL1xENwSf6wCJUZThX3dW","type":"tool_result","content":"# Dev Log — SH-17 (PRD-17 Fees, Invoices & Payment Records)\n\n> Before this run, this file held the SH-15 log and `task-completion-markers.json` held SH-16 markers. Both are replaced for SH-17, following the precedent from earlier tickets. `dev-rerun-count.json` was left untouched because the engine owns it.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-10)\n\nAll 32 tasks were implemented in one iteration, in dependency order. All 91 entries in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist at their exact paths. No dependencies were added (ADR-1).\n\n### Verification\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm run typecheck` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | clean; `eslint tests/unit/fees tests/integration/fees` is also clean |\n| Unit tests (FR-49) | 23/23 pass: `fee-math` (AC1 `2235.00`, AC2 `-107.50`, clamp, half-up, siblings, allocation, status, reminder slots, aging, NY timezone) and `money` |\n| Integration tests (FR-50, real Postgres, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) | 11/11 pass: FR-45 permission matrix through the real route handlers, 8 parallel issues and 8 parallel payments each numbered exactly 1..8, reversal and recompute, overpayment message, D-10 guard, and a 25-step seeded-random pay/reverse integrity check |\n| `npm run build` | succeeds; every fee route is dynamic (only `/api/health` is prerendered) |\n| E2E `tests/e2e/fees.spec.ts` (FR-51) | passes; run with `APP_URL=http://localhost:3200` because other processes hold ports 3000 and 3100 |\n| `npm run db:seed` | runs and re-runs idempotently. Result: 9 Grade 7 invoices (3 PAID, 2 PARTIALLY_PAID, 1 ISSUED, 3 OVERDUE) and 12 payments across all 5 methods |\n| Manual smoke (`next start`) | All 11 admin and print fee pages, plus dashboard, aging and the 3 CSV exports, return 200 for a bursar admin. Parent: `/fees` and `/api/me/fees` return 200 and are scoped to the family; admin APIs return 403. Teacher: fee pages redirect to `/forbidden` and fee APIs return 403. |\n\nMigration `20261116000000_add_fees` was generated with `prisma migrate diff` and drops nothing. The raw SQL for the 3 partial unique indexes and 2 `CHECK (amount > 0)` constraints is appended to it. It is applied with `migrate deploy`, the client is regenerated, and there is no drift. The MUI MCP lookup (NFR-6) works: `useMuiDocs` returned the x-date-pickers 9.17 index. All components follow patterns already used in the repo against MUI 9.5.0, with system props in `sx` and `slotProps`. No banned imports.\n\n### Failures that already existed (not caused by SH-17)\n- `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts`, `auth-forms.test.tsx` and `useToast.test.tsx` fail on the pre-SH-17 baseline as well. I checked this with `git stash`.\n- `tests/integration/dashboards/risk.test.ts` fails only in the full parallel run against the shared DB. It passes alone, both with and without SH-17 changes. This is the shared-DB flakiness noted in earlier logs.\n\n### Implementation notes and deviations\n- **File outside the matrix: `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`.** One assertion changed. It expected the FINANCE category to have no types, and FR-36 deliberately adds three. Leaving it red would break the NFR-10 gate.\n- **`Invoice.dueDays` (extra column).** A draft must know its due period when it is issued later. Plan invoices copy `plan.dueDays`; manual invoices take it from the input.\n- **`nextDocumentNumber` is one statement.** It runs `INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET nextValue = nextValue + 1 RETURNING`. This takes the same row lock, and a rollback undoes the increment, so it is equally gap-free, in one round trip instead of three (ADR-3 intent). The numbering test proves 1..N under parallel transactions.\n- **`access.ts` loads `requireRole` lazily.** Auth.js / React `cache` cannot load outside Next, and the seed and tests call fees-service with an explicit actor.\n- **`reports.ts` holds shared pieces.** These are the where builders and row serializers, plus `freshFeeSettings()` (settings + `markOverdue`). fees-service imports them; there is no import cycle.\n- **Parent invoice detail hides the audit timeline.** `timeline` is `[]` for parents because it is internal. Payment detail and parent payment rows show only the parent's own children's allocations.\n- **Manual invoices get no discounts.** Draft PATCH recomputes discount lines server-side for plan invoices only.\n- **Seed: fee demo parents.** Payments need a payer family, and the local Grade 7 students (the risk cohort) have no parents. The seed creates `fees.parentN@schoolhub.test`, linked as primary parent only to Grade 7 students who have none. The first two share a parent, so the sibling rule shows (Hugo's invoice carries the 5% line). The 3 OVERDUE invoices come from `issue()` with `today − 45`, then `markOverdue`. Sam gets Merit 10% as a StudentDiscount. In this DB Sam has no grade profile, so Sam is not invoiced.\n- **Record-payment picker.** `/api/students/:id/parents` has no GET, so the page server-renders `listPayerOptions()` (parents plus their children's names). The Autocomplete searches by parent or child name. No new endpoint.\n- **Navigation.** The four admin entries sit under a \"Fees\" group (the nav has no nested children). Because the shell matches by prefix, `/admin/fees/*` also highlights \"Fees\".\n- **FR-40 Fees card.** The page only owns `OverviewCards.tsx`, so the Fees item renders inside the existing Action items card when the balance is > 0. `getFeesSummary` is also added to `OVERVIEW_CARDS`, so `GET /api/students/:id/overview` gains a `fees` key (an additive change).\n- **Admin KPI cache key bumped to `kpis-v2`.** A cache entry from before the deploy has no `outstandingFees` and crashed the KPI row during smoke testing; the new key avoids it.\n- **Fees dashboard term choice.** It uses Chips that link to `?termId=` (a server component, no client select).\n- **Open assumption (D-12).** Optional fees are billed on every plan invoice of the year. This is isolated in `buildInvoiceDrafts` and should be confirmed with the PRD owner.\n- **`ponytail:` notes.**\n  - Reminder scan covers all open invoices.\n  - CSV exports are built in memory.\n  - `/api/me/fees` returns the whole family history unpaginated.\n  - Generation is synchronous and chunked (ADR-6).\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma enums/models + migration 20261116000000_add_fees — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: src/lib/money.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: Zod schemas src/lib/validators/fees.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: pure fee-math.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: unit tests fee-math + money — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: ledger.ts (numbers, locks, recompute, issue) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: access.ts (FR-45 matrix) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: fees.* notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: User.isBursar via users validator/service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: fees-service setup functions — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: setup API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: maintenance.ts + dispatch hook — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: invoice services + reports.invoiceWhere — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: invoice API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: payment services — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: payment API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: reports (dashboard, aging, CSV, my fees, outstanding) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: report API routes + /api/me/fees — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: shared fee UI components — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: invoice/receipt documents + print pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: navigation entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: /admin/fees/setup tabs — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: /admin/fees/invoices list + manual dialog — ✓ complete\n- TASK-24: /admin/fees/invoices/generate — ✓ complete\n- TASK-25: /admin/fees/invoices/[id] + actions — ✓ complete\n- TASK-26: payment pages (list, new, detail + reverse) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-27: /admin/fees dashboard — ✓ complete\n- TASK-28: parent /fees page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-29: admin KPI + parent overview fees card — ✓ complete\n- TASK-30: seed — ✓ complete\n- TASK-31: integration tests (access, numbering, ledger) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-32: e2e fees.spec.ts — ✓ complete\n----\n# QA Report — SH-17 (PRD-17 Fees, Invoices & Payment Records)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-17\n- timestamp: 2026-11-10T11:45:00Z\n- overallStatus: PASS\n- requirementsChecked: 63\n- requirementsPassed: 63\n- requirementsFailed: 0\n\n> The 63 requirements are 51 FRs and 12 NFRs. Every verdict cites a file or test. A few PASS rows rest on code review rather than a running test, and their Evidence column says so. One defect was found that SH-17 did not cause but that affects fee emails (finding 1). This file replaces the SH-15 QA report.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n1. **Pre-existing platform defect: some notification emails are silently lost. This includes fee reminders.**\n   - **Cause.** `@react-email/render@1.0.1` decodes stream chunks with `TextDecoder.decode(chunk)` and doesn't pass `{ stream: true }`. When a multi-byte character from the `<Preview>` padding lands on a chunk boundary, the rendered HTML contains `U+0000`.\n   - **Effect.** Postgres rejects the `EmailOutbox` row (`22021 invalid byte sequence 0x00`). `notify()` logs the error and swallows it. The in-app notification is still written; only the email is lost.\n   - **When it happens.** It is reproducible with titles of 53–63 characters, for example `Fee reminder: invoice INV-2026-000123 for <student name>`. The QA integration run hit it on both manual reminders.\n   - **Scope.** It is not in SH-17 code (`src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx` and the renderer predate it). It hits every module that sends notifications.\n   - **Tracking.** `tests/unit/fees/qa-sh17-email.test.ts` pins it with `it.fails`; that test turns red when the bug is fixed.\n   - **Suggested fix.** Strip `\\0` from `html` in `renderEmail`, or upgrade `@react-email/render`. This is a new ticket, so FR-36/37/38 are not failed for it.\n2. **Fixed by QA: a dangerous test cleanup in Dev's integration suites.**\n   - **What happened.** `tests/integration/fees/access.test.ts` `afterAll` ran `payment.deleteMany({ where: { id: ids.payment } })`. Prisma reads `{ id: undefined }` as \"match all\". When `beforeAll` failed (here, because of leftover fixture users from an earlier QA run), the cleanup **deleted every Payment and PaymentAllocation in the dev DB**. That left the seeded Grade 7 invoices with `amountPaid` but no allocations.\n   - **Fix.** The cleanups in `access`, `ledger`, `numbering` and `qa-sh17` now resolve their fixtures by MARK email or name, so every filter is an id list.\n   - **Proof.** QA verified it by forcing a `beforeAll` failure: payments stayed at 12 and the leftover user was cleaned up.\n   - **Data repair.** The 9 corrupted seed invoices and the 2026 `DocumentSequence` rows were removed and `npm run db:seed` was re-run. The dev DB is back to 9 Grade 7 invoices (3 PAID, 2 PARTIALLY_PAID, 1 ISSUED, 3 OVERDUE) and 12 payments across 5 methods. `amountPaid` equals the sum of non-reversed allocations on every row.\n3. **Fixed by QA: a regression in the test gate caused by SH-17 that Dev missed.** `tests/integration/parent-portal/qa-sh15.test.ts` expected 8 overview cards. FR-40 deliberately adds `fees`, so the assertion is now 9.\n4. **Gates.**\n   - `npm run typecheck` is clean and `npm run lint` is clean.\n   - `npm run build` succeeds, and every fee route is dynamic.\n   - All fee suites pass: 44 SH-17 tests (unit, integration and e2e), stable across 5 runs.\n   - Full suite with files run one at a time: 733–735/738. Of the failures:\n     - `attendance-qa` FR-22, `auth-forms`, `lockout` and `useToast` already failed on the baseline (recorded in the SH-15 report and the Dev log).\n     - `email-dispatch` AC-4 and the `qa-sh10` 50 ms timing check failed once under load and pass in isolation.\n     - In the fully parallel run, shared-DB flakes also show up (`risk`, `gradebook-sync`), and they pass in isolation.\n5. **Dev's self-report matches reality.** All 32 tasks are marked complete. All 91 paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist, and a scan found no `TODO`/`FIXME`/stub markers in fee code. QA ran the e2e test (`tests/e2e/fees.spec.ts`) against a production build: it passed in 3.6 s.\n\n## Tests written or changed by QA\n- `tests/integration/fees/qa-sh17.test.ts` (new, 7 tests, real DB). It covers generation end to end, setup guards, the draft lifecycle, the reminder throttle, the on-read OVERDUE refresh, parent payment scope, the dashboard, CSV and outstanding by student. See `coverage-report.md`.\n- `tests/unit/fees/qa-sh17-email.test.ts` (new, 2 tests). It covers finding 1.\n- Cleanups hardened in `tests/integration/fees/{access,ledger,numbering}.test.ts` (finding 2).\n- `tests/integration/parent-portal/qa-sh15.test.ts`: card count 8 → 9 (finding 3).\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | `prisma/schema.prisma` enums InvoiceStatus/PaymentMethod/DiscountKind (+InvoiceReminderKind); migration `20261116000000_add_fees` applied; all fee integration suites write them |\n| FR-2 | PASS | 12 fee models in `schema.prisma`, Decimal(10,2); `qa-sh17.test.ts` creates FeeItem/FeePlan/Line/Discount/StudentOptionalFee/StudentDiscount/Invoice/Payment/Allocation; DocumentSequence via `numbering.test.ts` |\n| FR-3 | PASS | `InvoiceReminder` model with unique (invoiceId, kind, scheduledFor); `qa-sh17` \"manual reminder…\" asserts the P2002 on a duplicate slot |\n| FR-4 | PASS | `SchoolSettings.currency/invoiceFooter`; DB check: USD + seeded footer; `access.test` `/api/me/fees` returns footer |\n| FR-5 | PASS | `User.isBursar`; `access.test` \"a non-bursar flag revoked in the DB takes effect at once\"; `src/lib/validators/users.ts` |\n| FR-6 | PASS | `qa-sh17` setup test (createFeeItem ×3); `access.test` POST /api/fees/items 201 for bursar. Update/archive by code review (`fees-service.ts` updateFeeItem/archiveFeeItem) |\n| FR-7 | PASS | `qa-sh17` \"plan PUT replaces lines\" (lines replaced, total 2150.00) |\n| FR-8 | PASS | `qa-sh17` createDiscount PERCENT/FIXED/auto rules; percent 100.01 → VALIDATION_ERROR |\n| FR-9 | PASS | `qa-sh17` bulkAssignOptionalFee → `{assigned: 4}`; non-optional item refused |\n| FR-10 | PASS | `qa-sh17` manual merit assigned with note; auto discount assignment refused |\n| FR-11 | PASS | `fee-math.test` siblings; `qa-sh17` preview ranks 1/2/3/null, SIBLING_2ND only on rank 2, 3RD_PLUS only on rank 3 |\n| FR-12 | PASS | `qa-sh17` preview test (plan + optional + manual + auto lines per student); e2e generate page |\n| FR-13 | PASS | `qa-sh17` re-run: all rows `ALREADY_INVOICED`, 0 created; a manual term invoice does not skip |\n| FR-14 | PASS | `qa-sh17` create-and-issue: ISSUED, issueDate today, dueDate today+30 (leap year), 3 `fees.invoice_issued` notifications; `e2e/fees.spec.ts` |\n| FR-15 | PASS | `fee-math.test` AC1/AC2/clamp/half-up; `qa-sh17` AC1 2235.00 and AC2 −107.50 through the DB |\n| FR-16 | PASS | `numbering.test` parallel INV/RCT 1..N gap-free; `ledger.ts` nextDocumentNumber; `qa-sh17` INV-2096-NNNNNN unique |\n| FR-17 | PASS | `listInvoices` + `InvoicesTable.tsx`; `access.test` GET /api/fees/invoices; `qa-sh17` listInvoices |\n| FR-18 | PASS | `reports.ts invoiceWhere` (status/term/grade/section/overdue/q); `qa-sh17` overdue+student filter, CSV `q`+term filter; totals in `listInvoices` meta (code review) |\n| FR-19 | PASS | `getInvoice` lines/allocations/timeline from AuditLog; `ledger.test` reads lines and statuses; `qa-sh17` asserts `invoice.issue` audit rows |\n| FR-20 | PASS | `qa-sh17` draft lifecycle: edit → 80.00, issue, then edit/delete/issue → CONFLICT; draft delete removes row |\n| FR-21 | PASS | `ledger.test` adjust (negative isAdjustment line + reason, guard) and void refused with allocations |\n| FR-22 | PASS | `getInvoice.allocations` with receipt numbers + `InvoiceActions.tsx` receipt links; e2e prints the receipt |\n| FR-23 | PASS | `createManualInvoice` used by `ledger`, `access`, `qa-sh17` tests |\n| FR-24 | PASS | `fee-math.test` deriveStatus; `ledger.test` PAID/PARTIALLY_PAID/ISSUED transitions + integrity checker |\n| FR-25 | PASS | `qa-sh17` \"a past-due ISSUED invoice reads as OVERDUE\"; `markOverdue` hooked in `api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` |\n| FR-26 | PASS | `getFamilyOpenInvoices` + `RecordPaymentForm.tsx`; e2e records a payment through the page |\n| FR-27 | PASS | `recordPaymentSchema` in `validators/fees.ts`; `qa-sh17` payment with method/reference/payer/receivedAt |\n| FR-28 | PASS | `fee-math.test` autoAllocate/validateAllocations; `ledger.test` oldest-first 500/100 and invalid allocations refused |\n| FR-29 | PASS | `ledger.test` \"refuses an overpayment… $1,000.00 and saves nothing\" |\n| FR-30 | PASS | `recordPayment` (RCT number, recompute, `fees.payment_received`, receiptUrl); `qa-sh17` RCT-2096 format; e2e opens receipt |\n| FR-31 | PASS | `ledger.test` reverse → recompute, second reverse CONFLICT; payment row kept with `reversed: true` |\n| FR-32 | PASS | `qa-sh17` listPayments: parent sees own payment, other parent none; `access.test` payment GET 200/404 |\n---\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-17\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T16:20:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"completed\": [\n    \"TASK-1\",\n    \"TASK-2\",\n    \"TASK-3\",\n    \"TASK-4\",\n    \"TASK-5\",\n    \"TASK-6\",\n    \"TASK-7\",\n    \"TASK-8\",\n    \"TASK-9\",\n    \"TASK-10\",\n    \"TASK-11\",\n    \"TASK-12\",\n    \"TASK-13\",\n    \"TASK-14\",\n    \"TASK-15\",\n    \"TASK-16\",\n    \"TASK-17\",\n    \"TASK-18\",\n    \"TASK-19\",\n    \"TASK-20\",\n    \"TASK-21\",\n    \"TASK-22\",\n    \"TASK-23\",\n    \"TASK-24\",\n    \"TASK-25\",\n    \"TASK-26\",\n    \"TASK-27\",\n    \"TASK-28\",\n    \"TASK-29\",\n    \"TASK-30\",\n    \"TASK-31\",\n    \"TASK-32\"\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bdae3a7-5bc6-4a4f-b701-fedb2c55b2b8","uuid":"436e90c8-22c9-4549-ba97-2bd1482113ab","timestamp":"2026-11-10T11:50:50.003Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Dev Log — SH-17 (PRD-17 Fees, Invoices & Payment Records)\n\n> Before this run, this file held the SH-15 log and `task-completion-markers.json` held SH-16 markers. Both are replaced for SH-17, following the precedent from earlier tickets. `dev-rerun-count.json` was left untouched because the engine owns it.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-10)\n\nAll 32 tasks were implemented in one iteration, in dependency order. All 91 entries in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist at their exact paths. No dependencies were added (ADR-1).\n\n### Verification\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm run typecheck` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | clean; `eslint tests/unit/fees tests/integration/fees` is also clean |\n| Unit tests (FR-49) | 23/23 pass: `fee-math` (AC1 `2235.00`, AC2 `-107.50`, clamp, half-up, siblings, allocation, status, reminder slots, aging, NY timezone) and `money` |\n| Integration tests (FR-50, real Postgres, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) | 11/11 pass: FR-45 permission matrix through the real route handlers, 8 parallel issues and 8 parallel payments each numbered exactly 1..8, reversal and recompute, overpayment message, D-10 guard, and a 25-step seeded-random pay/reverse integrity check |\n| `npm run build` | succeeds; every fee route is dynamic (only `/api/health` is prerendered) |\n| E2E `tests/e2e/fees.spec.ts` (FR-51) | passes; run with `APP_URL=http://localhost:3200` because other processes hold ports 3000 and 3100 |\n| `npm run db:seed` | runs and re-runs idempotently. Result: 9 Grade 7 invoices (3 PAID, 2 PARTIALLY_PAID, 1 ISSUED, 3 OVERDUE) and 12 payments across all 5 methods |\n| Manual smoke (`next start`) | All 11 admin and print fee pages, plus dashboard, aging and the 3 CSV exports, return 200 for a bursar admin. Parent: `/fees` and `/api/me/fees` return 200 and are scoped to the family; admin APIs return 403. Teacher: fee pages redirect to `/forbidden` and fee APIs return 403. |\n\nMigration `20261116000000_add_fees` was generated with `prisma migrate diff` and drops nothing. The raw SQL for the 3 partial unique indexes and 2 `CHECK (amount > 0)` constraints is appended to it. It is applied with `migrate deploy`, the client is regenerated, and there is no drift. The MUI MCP lookup (NFR-6) works: `useMuiDocs` returned the x-date-pickers 9.17 index. All components follow patterns already used in the repo against MUI 9.5.0, with system props in `sx` and `slotProps`. No banned imports.\n\n### Failures that already existed (not caused by SH-17)\n- `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts`, `auth-forms.test.tsx` and `useToast.test.tsx` fail on the pre-SH-17 baseline as well. I checked this with `git stash`.\n- `tests/integration/dashboards/risk.test.ts` fails only in the full parallel run against the shared DB. It passes alone, both with and without SH-17 changes. This is the shared-DB flakiness noted in earlier logs.\n\n### Implementation notes and deviations\n- **File outside the matrix: `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`.** One assertion changed. It expected the FINANCE category to have no types, and FR-36 deliberately adds three. Leaving it red would break the NFR-10 gate.\n- **`Invoice.dueDays` (extra column).** A draft must know its due period when it is issued later. Plan invoices copy `plan.dueDays`; manual invoices take it from the input.\n- **`nextDocumentNumber` is one statement.** It runs `INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET nextValue = nextValue + 1 RETURNING`. This takes the same row lock, and a rollback undoes the increment, so it is equally gap-free, in one round trip instead of three (ADR-3 intent). The numbering test proves 1..N under parallel transactions.\n- **`access.ts` loads `requireRole` lazily.** Auth.js / React `cache` cannot load outside Next, and the seed and tests call fees-service with an explicit actor.\n- **`reports.ts` holds shared pieces.** These are the where builders and row serializers, plus `freshFeeSettings()` (settings + `markOverdue`). fees-service imports them; there is no import cycle.\n- **Parent invoice detail hides the audit timeline.** `timeline` is `[]` for parents because it is internal. Payment detail and parent payment rows show only the parent's own children's allocations.\n- **Manual invoices get no discounts.** Draft PATCH recomputes discount lines server-side for plan invoices only.\n- **Seed: fee demo parents.** Payments need a payer family, and the local Grade 7 students (the risk cohort) have no parents. The seed creates `fees.parentN@schoolhub.test`, linked as primary parent only to Grade 7 students who have none. The first two share a parent, so the sibling rule shows (Hugo's invoice carries the 5% line). The 3 OVERDUE invoices come from `issue()` with `today − 45`, then `markOverdue`. Sam gets Merit 10% as a StudentDiscount. In this DB Sam has no grade profile, so Sam is not invoiced.\n- **Record-payment picker.** `/api/students/:id/parents` has no GET, so the page server-renders `listPayerOptions()` (parents plus their children's names). The Autocomplete searches by parent or child name. No new endpoint.\n- **Navigation.** The four admin entries sit under a \"Fees\" group (the nav has no nested children). Because the shell matches by prefix, `/admin/fees/*` also highlights \"Fees\".\n- **FR-40 Fees card.** The page only owns `OverviewCards.tsx`, so the Fees item renders inside the existing Action items card when the balance is > 0. `getFeesSummary` is also added to `OVERVIEW_CARDS`, so `GET /api/students/:id/overview` gains a `fees` key (an additive change).\n- **Admin KPI cache key bumped to `kpis-v2`.** A cache entry from before the deploy has no `outstandingFees` and crashed the KPI row during smoke testing; the new key avoids it.\n- **Fees dashboard term choice.** It uses Chips that link to `?termId=` (a server component, no client select).\n- **Open assumption (D-12).** Optional fees are billed on every plan invoice of the year. This is isolated in `buildInvoiceDrafts` and should be confirmed with the PRD owner.\n- **`ponytail:` notes.**\n  - Reminder scan covers all open invoices.\n  - CSV exports are built in memory.\n  - `/api/me/fees` returns the whole family history unpaginated.\n  - Generation is synchronous and chunked (ADR-6).\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma enums/models + migration 20261116000000_add_fees — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: src/lib/money.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: Zod schemas src/lib/validators/fees.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: pure fee-math.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: unit tests fee-math + money — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: ledger.ts (numbers, locks, recompute, issue) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: access.ts (FR-45 matrix) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: fees.* notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: User.isBursar via users validator/service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: fees-service setup functions — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: setup API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: maintenance.ts + dispatch hook — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: invoice services + reports.invoiceWhere — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: invoice API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: payment services — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: payment API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: reports (dashboard, aging, CSV, my fees, outstanding) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: report API routes + /api/me/fees — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: shared fee UI components — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: invoice/receipt documents + print pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: navigation entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: /admin/fees/setup tabs — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: /admin/fees/invoices list + manual dialog — ✓ complete\n- TASK-24: /admin/fees/invoices/generate — ✓ complete\n- TASK-25: /admin/fees/invoices/[id] + actions — ✓ complete\n- TASK-26: payment pages (list, new, detail + reverse) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-27: /admin/fees dashboard — ✓ complete\n- TASK-28: parent /fees page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-29: admin KPI + parent overview fees card — ✓ complete\n- TASK-30: seed — ✓ complete\n- TASK-31: integration tests (access, numbering, ledger) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-32: e2e fees.spec.ts — ✓ complete\n----\n# QA Report — SH-17 (PRD-17 Fees, Invoices & Payment Records)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-17\n- timestamp: 2026-11-10T11:45:00Z\n- overallStatus: PASS\n- requirementsChecked: 63\n- requirementsPassed: 63\n- requirementsFailed: 0\n\n> The 63 requirements are 51 FRs and 12 NFRs. Every verdict cites a file or test. A few PASS rows rest on code review rather than a running test, and their Evidence column says so. One defect was found that SH-17 did not cause but that affects fee emails (finding 1). This file replaces the SH-15 QA report.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n1. **Pre-existing platform defect: some notification emails are silently lost. This includes fee reminders.**\n   - **Cause.** `@react-email/render@1.0.1` decodes stream chunks with `TextDecoder.decode(chunk)` and doesn't pass `{ stream: true }`. When a multi-byte character from the `<Preview>` padding lands on a chunk boundary, the rendered HTML contains `U+0000`.\n   - **Effect.** Postgres rejects the `EmailOutbox` row (`22021 invalid byte sequence 0x00`). `notify()` logs the error and swallows it. The in-app notification is still written; only the email is lost.\n   - **When it happens.** It is reproducible with titles of 53–63 characters, for example `Fee reminder: invoice INV-2026-000123 for <student name>`. The QA integration run hit it on both manual reminders.\n   - **Scope.** It is not in SH-17 code (`src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx` and the renderer predate it). It hits every module that sends notifications.\n   - **Tracking.** `tests/unit/fees/qa-sh17-email.test.ts` pins it with `it.fails`; that test turns red when the bug is fixed.\n   - **Suggested fix.** Strip `\\0` from `html` in `renderEmail`, or upgrade `@react-email/render`. This is a new ticket, so FR-36/37/38 are not failed for it.\n2. **Fixed by QA: a dangerous test cleanup in Dev's integration suites.**\n   - **What happened.** `tests/integration/fees/access.test.ts` `afterAll` ran `payment.deleteMany({ where: { id: ids.payment } })`. Prisma reads `{ id: undefined }` as \"match all\". When `beforeAll` failed (here, because of leftover fixture users from an earlier QA run), the cleanup **deleted every Payment and PaymentAllocation in the dev DB**. That left the seeded Grade 7 invoices with `amountPaid` but no allocations.\n   - **Fix.** The cleanups in `access`, `ledger`, `numbering` and `qa-sh17` now resolve their fixtures by MARK email or name, so every filter is an id list.\n   - **Proof.** QA verified it by forcing a `beforeAll` failure: payments stayed at 12 and the leftover user was cleaned up.\n   - **Data repair.** The 9 corrupted seed invoices and the 2026 `DocumentSequence` rows were removed and `npm run db:seed` was re-run. The dev DB is back to 9 Grade 7 invoices (3 PAID, 2 PARTIALLY_PAID, 1 ISSUED, 3 OVERDUE) and 12 payments across 5 methods. `amountPaid` equals the sum of non-reversed allocations on every row.\n3. **Fixed by QA: a regression in the test gate caused by SH-17 that Dev missed.** `tests/integration/parent-portal/qa-sh15.test.ts` expected 8 overview cards. FR-40 deliberately adds `fees`, so the assertion is now 9.\n4. **Gates.**\n   - `npm run typecheck` is clean and `npm run lint` is clean.\n   - `npm run build` succeeds, and every fee route is dynamic.\n   - All fee suites pass: 44 SH-17 tests (unit, integration and e2e), stable across 5 runs.\n   - Full suite with files run one at a time: 733–735/738. Of the failures:\n     - `attendance-qa` FR-22, `auth-forms`, `lockout` and `useToast` already failed on the baseline (recorded in the SH-15 report and the Dev log).\n     - `email-dispatch` AC-4 and the `qa-sh10` 50 ms timing check failed once under load and pass in isolation.\n     - In the fully parallel run, shared-DB flakes also show up (`risk`, `gradebook-sync`), and they pass in isolation.\n5. **Dev's self-report matches reality.** All 32 tasks are marked complete. All 91 paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist, and a scan found no `TODO`/`FIXME`/stub markers in fee code. QA ran the e2e test (`tests/e2e/fees.spec.ts`) against a production build: it passed in 3.6 s.\n\n## Tests written or changed by QA\n- `tests/integration/fees/qa-sh17.test.ts` (new, 7 tests, real DB). It covers generation end to end, setup guards, the draft lifecycle, the reminder throttle, the on-read OVERDUE refresh, parent payment scope, the dashboard, CSV and outstanding by student. See `coverage-report.md`.\n- `tests/unit/fees/qa-sh17-email.test.ts` (new, 2 tests). It covers finding 1.\n- Cleanups hardened in `tests/integration/fees/{access,ledger,numbering}.test.ts` (finding 2).\n- `tests/integration/parent-portal/qa-sh15.test.ts`: card count 8 → 9 (finding 3).\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | `prisma/schema.prisma` enums InvoiceStatus/PaymentMethod/DiscountKind (+InvoiceReminderKind); migration `20261116000000_add_fees` applied; all fee integration suites write them |\n| FR-2 | PASS | 12 fee models in `schema.prisma`, Decimal(10,2); `qa-sh17.test.ts` creates FeeItem/FeePlan/Line/Discount/StudentOptionalFee/StudentDiscount/Invoice/Payment/Allocation; DocumentSequence via `numbering.test.ts` |\n| FR-3 | PASS | `InvoiceReminder` model with unique (invoiceId, kind, scheduledFor); `qa-sh17` \"manual reminder…\" asserts the P2002 on a duplicate slot |\n| FR-4 | PASS | `SchoolSettings.currency/invoiceFooter`; DB check: USD + seeded footer; `access.test` `/api/me/fees` returns footer |\n| FR-5 | PASS | `User.isBursar`; `access.test` \"a non-bursar flag revoked in the DB takes effect at once\"; `src/lib/validators/users.ts` |\n| FR-6 | PASS | `qa-sh17` setup test (createFeeItem ×3); `access.test` POST /api/fees/items 201 for bursar. Update/archive by code review (`fees-service.ts` updateFeeItem/archiveFeeItem) |\n| FR-7 | PASS | `qa-sh17` \"plan PUT replaces lines\" (lines replaced, total 2150.00) |\n| FR-8 | PASS | `qa-sh17` createDiscount PERCENT/FIXED/auto rules; percent 100.01 → VALIDATION_ERROR |\n| FR-9 | PASS | `qa-sh17` bulkAssignOptionalFee → `{assigned: 4}`; non-optional item refused |\n| FR-10 | PASS | `qa-sh17` manual merit assigned with note; auto discount assignment refused |\n| FR-11 | PASS | `fee-math.test` siblings; `qa-sh17` preview ranks 1/2/3/null, SIBLING_2ND only on rank 2, 3RD_PLUS only on rank 3 |\n| FR-12 | PASS | `qa-sh17` preview test (plan + optional + manual + auto lines per student); e2e generate page |\n| FR-13 | PASS | `qa-sh17` re-run: all rows `ALREADY_INVOICED`, 0 created; a manual term invoice does not skip |\n| FR-14 | PASS | `qa-sh17` create-and-issue: ISSUED, issueDate today, dueDate today+30 (leap year), 3 `fees.invoice_issued` notifications; `e2e/fees.spec.ts` |\n| FR-15 | PASS | `fee-math.test` AC1/AC2/clamp/half-up; `qa-sh17` AC1 2235.00 and AC2 −107.50 through the DB |\n| FR-16 | PASS | `numbering.test` parallel INV/RCT 1..N gap-free; `ledger.ts` nextDocumentNumber; `qa-sh17` INV-2096-NNNNNN unique |\n| FR-17 | PASS | `listInvoices` + `InvoicesTable.tsx`; `access.test` GET /api/fees/invoices; `qa-sh17` listInvoices |\n| FR-18 | PASS | `reports.ts invoiceWhere` (status/term/grade/section/overdue/q); `qa-sh17` overdue+student filter, CSV `q`+term filter; totals in `listInvoices` meta (code review) |\n| FR-19 | PASS | `getInvoice` lines/allocations/timeline from AuditLog; `ledger.test` reads lines and statuses; `qa-sh17` asserts `invoice.issue` audit rows |\n| FR-20 | PASS | `qa-sh17` draft lifecycle: edit → 80.00, issue, then edit/delete/issue → CONFLICT; draft delete removes row |\n| FR-21 | PASS | `ledger.test` adjust (negative isAdjustment line + reason, guard) and void refused with allocations |\n| FR-22 | PASS | `getInvoice.allocations` with receipt numbers + `InvoiceActions.tsx` receipt links; e2e prints the receipt |\n| FR-23 | PASS | `createManualInvoice` used by `ledger`, `access`, `qa-sh17` tests |\n| FR-24 | PASS | `fee-math.test` deriveStatus; `ledger.test`